(Phnom Penh): Mr. Seng Heang, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on July 2, 2024, decided to charge the perpetrator, 23-year-old Chan Dalin, an employee of Cinema Chef Kofiln Pub Restaurant, with "murder". The accused was sent to the investigating judge to continue the relevant procedure for strangling the victim, 23-year-old Suon Makara, until his death. This incident happened on June 22, 2024.
According to the report on the results of the investigation into the murder case on June 22, 2024 at around 6:00 AM at the point of renting a room with no number on the first floor, location 23, Street 287, Village 11, Group 41, Sangkat Boeung Kak 1, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
The origin of this story was a surprise on June 23, 2024 at 10:30 AM by the specialized force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police received information that there was a dead body of a Cambodian woman lying in the room at the room. No number for rent, 1st floor, Location 23, Street 287, Village 11, Group 41, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
Immediately after receiving this information, the Criminal Police Planning Task Force, in cooperation with the Tuol Kork District Police Inspectorate, went to the scene to conduct a search according to the autopsy of the Technical and Scientific Police Office and Dr. Nong Sovannaroth, an autopsy doctor. Phnom Penh initially concluded that it was a murder case in which the victim died by covering his mouth, covering his nose and strangling.
