(Banteay Meanchey): A 90-meter-long, 5-meter-wide bridge across the Serei Sophorn River in Sangkat Preah Ponlea, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province has begun construction.
The bridge was built in 1960 and is very old and dilapidated, causing severe flooding since 2018. By 2024, the bridge being rebuilt by the Royal Government is gradually taking shape to make it easier for people to travel.
On the morning of July 1, 2024, Mr. Chi Sitha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, Mr. HEL Raya, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Sreng Sophal, Governor of Serey Sophorn City, Mr. Chea Yuthearun, Director of the Department of Rural Development, Ms. Chat Sochea, Sangkat Chief of Preah Ponlea, officials, monks And many people participated in opening the construction site of this bridge.
Mr. Sreng Sophal said that the construction of this concrete bridge connects three villages across the river to Prey Russey village, Preah Ponlea commune, across Wat Preah Ponlea.
Mr. Chea Yuthearun said that the construction of this bridge was initiated by Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Royal Government of the 7th mandate and Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia, donated a bridge. Mr. Ke Kim Yan, Member of Parliament for Banteay Meanchey Constituency.
