Phnom Penh Municipal Court rejects Ny Nak's request for bail
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has rejected the request for bail of Mr. Ny Nak's defense lawyer after a hearing held on the afternoon of July 1, 2024 on the bail application of lawyer Choung Chung Ngy. . Mr. Choung Chung-ngy filed a bail application for his client, Ny Nak, arguing that he had a physical illness.
Prosecutor Seng Heang denied the allegations, stating at the hearing: "First, in each correctional department, there are doctors on duty and for serious illnesses can come to the hospital for further treatment. "Second, the accused Ny Nak was once imprisoned and this time he was convicted of a non-recurring crime, so the prosecution decided to reject the bail application."
At the end of the hearing, Trial Judge Tith Sothy Borachat announced that he would not allow Ny Nak to stay out of the courtroom.
Mr. Ny Nak, born in 1979, was arrested and sent to court immediately on Friday morning, January 5, 2024, after he denounced Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and many government ministries. Another last December. The decision to detain Ny Nak was made by Judge Nhim Pisal, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Ny Nak had already been jailed once in 2020 on charges of "inciting to commit a crime" and was sentenced to 18 months. He was released from prison on June 10, 2021.
