Mr. Suon Somalin led professional officers to continue to inspect the situation of flies destroying rice in Preah Sdach district
(Prey Veng): Mr. Suon Somalin, Governor of Prey Veng Province, on June 30, 2024, led professional officers to inspect the rice cultivation situation of people affected by white flies destroying rice in Lvea commune. Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province.
By inspecting the above location, it was found that the rice fields affected by the flies destroyed many hectares, which is the concern of the people in harvesting. In the past, on these fields, farmers could grow rice three times a year.
The farmers reported to the provincial governor that the white fly had been flying to destroy the rice for more than a month, and that it had landed in the fields, some of which were almost completely damaged, some of which had been damaged by more than one and a half hectares. Residents said he tried to spray but to no avail.
Mr. Phon Samphors, Governor of Preah Sdach District, said that not only in Lvea commune, there are white flies destroying rice all over the district, and the most affected commune in Boeung Dol commune, just walk through the fields and see red rice fields, there are white flies.
Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the more pesticides sprayed, the more destructive the animals, because the pesticides both protect and attract odors to the animals. Looking for a way to get rid of this white fly as fast as possible.
