(Phnom Penh): Residents of Mean commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province, who depend on fishing in Boeung Thom, respectfully asked Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to help restore a canal that leads water from the Mekong River into Boeung Thom. To keep fish alive in the lake, as well as bring fish from the river into the lake.
According to people who used to depend on fishing in the lake, for about three years, the Mekong River has not flooded into the lake and the canal does not flow into the lake. Fish are scarce and the lake water smells bad, affecting fish life.
For this reason, they want to restore the canal from the Mekong River to flow into the lake to change the water in the lake to be more favorable for fish life. In addition, when the river flows into the lake, it also helps bring fish from the river into the lake.
