(Phnom Penh): The silk sector is a sector that the Royal Government of Cambodia recognizes as indispensable in contributing to national economic development and job creation for women, especially in rural areas.
However, the sector does not seem to be growing as much as it should be, which requires joint efforts to grow the sector.
Dr. Mey Kalyan, President of the Khmer Silk Development Center, said that the silk industry is a national sovereignty that Cambodia wants to do at any time because it is a traditional occupation of the Cambodian people from the beginning.
He said that although this is a small business, it also contributes to building the national economy, especially the creation of jobs for housewives in some rural areas.
Silk can not only be used to make clothes, but also to make souvenirs for sale to tourists, while her worm nests can also be processed into various products such as soap.
Recognizing the indispensable importance of the Cambodian silk sector in contributing to the national economic development and preservation of Cambodia's cultural heritage, as well as the importance of attracting tourism, the Royal Government has decided to build a National Silk Sector Strategy 2016-2020 as a guide. For the next step development.
This silk sector strategy aims to revitalize the aquaculture sector (raising her worms) in Cambodia, modernize the Cambodian silk sector, promote public-private partnerships, and encourage large-scale investment in the sector. The future.
The Royal Government of Cambodia is firmly committed to supporting and developing this sector in line with the vision and long-term vision set out in this National Silk Strategy Strategy: Produce high quality silk to maintain the income of those involved in silk products.
