World Bank approves $ 1.25 billion loan for Philippines
MANILA: The World Bank (WB) said on Saturday that its executive board has approved $ 1.25 billion in loans for the Philippines' education and public infrastructure. According to Reuters.
The development bank will provide $ 500 million in loans for a project in the Philippines to repair disaster-stricken schools in the provinces, Reuters reported, citing a press release issued by the World Bank. And increase the capacity of those schools to be able to operate even after a natural disaster.
The World Bank has also approved a $ 750 million loan to support reforms that will increase investment in public service infrastructure and promote renewable energy.
