(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board will act as a favorable and open institutional mechanism, allowing the private sector to fully participate with the Royal Government based on the principle of "think together, act together, take responsibility". . This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Tourism.
The release of this press release follows Decision No. 124 Pillar dated 27 June 2024 of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, who has appointed the composition of the Board of Study, Marketing and Tourism Promotion of Cambodia.
The appointment comes after the Royal Government issued a sub-decree on the revision of the Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board on February 6, 2024 in order to promote public-private partnerships. In studying the market and promoting Cambodian tourism to the international market, based on the principles of common thinking and ownership.
The reorganization of this institutional mechanism has undergone several in-depth discussions and consultations with the private sector and key stakeholders under the direct leadership of Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, under the guidance and guidance of His Majesty the King. Hun Manet, Prime Minister.
The launch of the Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board will play an important role in achieving the Ministry of Tourism's "Increase 5 Development 3" strategic initiative and achieve the vision of the first phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy. The seventh mandate for tourism aims to turn Cambodia into a leading and vibrant tourism destination.
