(Kratie): Ms. Sotha, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, led professional officers to inspect people's rice crops in some villages, communes and districts in Kratie province, which are affected by worms that destroy rice crops. .
In fact, on June 27, 2024, the Secretary of State continued to lead a delegation from the Ministry to inspect the rice crops of the people in two communes: Koulab commune, Chit Borei district and Or Russey commune, Kratie city.
Ms. Sotha also continued to visit farmers in some villages, communes - districts to educate and guide some measures to control and prevent worms that are present.
The Undersecretary of State advised farmers to continue to monitor their rice fields for fear of butterflies or dukes hiding in the ground, so farmers must immediately add water to the rice fields to prevent it.
Experts also urged some methods and safety measures to reduce toxins to farmers when spraying chemicals must use the right mask, wear gloves and boots, and when spraying. However, do not spray on the body.
At the same time, he told how to spray, advise farmers to be careful and choose the time not to spray when the sky is hot in the morning should be sprayed between 7 to 10 o'clock and in the afternoon between 3 o'clock. 4 is highly effective.
Separately, Mr. Sam Sam Ang, Director of the Office of Agriculture and Agricultural Productivity of Kratie Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that in Kratie province, swarms of worms ate and affected 1,160.5 hectares of crops in 14 communes. Affected 387.5 hectares of rice, 287 hectares of corn, 220 hectares of cassava, 228 hectares of cashew and 308 hectares of rubber.
At present, the people's crops seem to be about 70 to 80% better, because the professional officials have promoted and taken measures to get rid of it in time, and these days, Kratie province is getting a lot of rain, which makes Reducing pests will also destroy people's crops. Cambodian fragrant rice finally enters EU's largest supermarket after 5 years of trying (Video inside)
