Health Minister Calls on Cambodian Obstetrics and Gynecology Association to Continue Together to Improve Maternal, Infant and Child Health in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, called on the leaders and members of the Cambodian Association of Obstetrics and Gynecology to continue to work together to strengthen the health of mothers, babies and children in Cambodia in terms of services. Public, especially private services.
This call was made at the opening ceremony of the 23rd workshop of the Cambodian Association of Obstetricians and Gynecologists under the theme "Together to promote women's health" at the Phnom Penh Hotel on the morning of June 29, 2024 with the participation of Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, President of the Association of Members and Members of the Cambodian Obstetrics and Gynecology Association, as well as national and international speakers.
The Minister stated that the 23rd workshop of the Association of Obstetricians and Gynecologists of Cambodia now hopes to provide opportunities and share a lot of knowledge to the members of the Association, as well as participants to gain knowledge, experience and new discoveries. In the world as well as in Cambodia itself.
On October 5, 2023, the Ministry of Health announced the introduction of cervical cancer vaccination of 9-year-old girls into the national immunization program to improve the well-being of the people. Cambodia will also contribute to the World Health Organization (WHO) goal of eliminating cervical cancer by 2030.
At the same time, the Professor recommended some key priorities to the workshop to pay attention to: 1-Capacity building through the organization of additional training courses and increase the number of trainers 2-Standards of professional ethics 3-Human resources, infrastructure and materials 4-Involvement of communities and communication systems.
He also called on the leaders and members of the Cambodian Association of Obstetrics and Gynecology to continue to work together to strengthen the health of mothers, infants and children in Cambodia, both in public services, especially private services.
The Minister expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the Cambodian Association of Obstetricians and Gynecologists for organizing this conference and thanked the national and international speakers for sharing their valuable experiences and thanking them for their support for the conference. This.
It should be informed that the 23rd workshop of the Association of Obstetricians and Gynecologists of Cambodia lasted for a full day, with the participation of the leaders of the health officials who are members from the 25 provinces, a total of 250 participants.
He expressed the expectation that the Association of Obstetricians and Gynecologists of Cambodia will organize this workshop regularly, which demonstrates a strong internal unity, a sense of responsibility and to contribute to further professional development.
