(Kampong Thom): The management of Speu Primary School in Msakrang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province, appealed to philanthropists near and far to support the construction of a new fence of the school, which is still missing 35 out of a total of 47 fences.
With the need for student safety, the Speu Primary School Board immediately measured the location of the old fence to prepare for the new stone fence. After measuring, it was found that the school had to rebuild 47 new stone fences, with each master paying 460,000 Riels (400,000 Riels for the fence and 60,000 Riels for marble to write the name of the benefactor). ).
According to the call of the school, up to now, there are 12 philanthropists participating, and the budget has already been handed over to the school management, the remaining 35 panels have not been sponsored yet. Therefore, the management of Speu Primary School would like to appeal to philanthropists near and far to support the construction of the new stone fence of the school, which is still missing 35 pieces.
