The Ministry of Agriculture and the KOPIA Center in Cambodia jointly enhance the competitiveness of corn in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Chan Saruth, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, attended the workshop on the afternoon of June 28, 2024. International on Improving the Competitiveness of Maize in Cambodia. This event takes place at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
The event was attended by the Ministry of Agriculture, Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum Agriculture Department, corn farmers from Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum provinces and about 70 stakeholders, organized by the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture and the KOPIA Center in Cambodia.
In this regard, Dr. Song Young Ju added that more attention must be paid to agricultural science and technology, as well as to promote the possibility of corn, as corn is an important crop of Cambodia now and in the future.
He said that this corn project is carried out in many provinces such as Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kandal, Battambang and Pailin, which has helped Cambodian farmers to understand and reduce the original price of corn seeds.
In addition, Mr. Chan Saruth advised the farmers to continue this plan by themselves step by step to be strong, even if the project still helps.
Mr. Chan Saruth said that in the past, we have been building capacity and providing various resources from the project, we need to know how to use effectively and on target and can continue this work smoothly when the project is completed. .
(Kampong Cham): Dr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency and Chairman of the CPP Working Group on Local Assistance, stated that the CPP is born of true patriotism to liberate the motherland and stand by the people. Together.
This statement was made by Dr. Ma Chhoeun on the occasion of leading the celebration of the 73rd Anniversary of the Cambodian People's Party (June 28, 1951 - June 28, 2024) in Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province on June 28, 2024. Invitation from Dr. Ouk Maly, Deputy Chairman of the CPP Working Group to visit Cheung Prey District.
On that occasion, Dr. Ma Chhoeun mentioned the history of the establishment of the Cambodian People's Party on June 28, 1951, born of the Cambodian people's resistance movement to demand Cambodian independence from the French colony. "The CPP was born out of genuine patriotism to liberate the motherland, and only the Cambodian People's Party is an important reference for nation-building and development from the past to the present and into the future," he said. "
MP Ma Chhoeun continued that the Cambodian People's Party was originally called the Cambodian Revolutionary Party. From its inception, the party has gone through countless obstacles, struggles for the nation under the ideal for the nation and the people of Cambodia, linked to the well-being of the people in all circumstances, until its full independence on November 9, 1953, under God. Royal crusade of Prince Norodom Sihanouk.
"January 7 Liberation Day is the second birthday of the Cambodian people, the day that made things happen today," he said. These are historical facts that Cambodians, especially young people, must continue to remember. ”
He added that despite the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1993, Cambodia has not yet agreed because the Khmer Rouge forces have not yet joined the government. Therefore, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the outstanding guide set out the implementation of win-win politics in 1998, only to achieve national reunification.
MP Ma Chhoeun added that the Cambodian People's Party has a clear policy, has an emotional education program, and is properly organized from top to bottom, a party that is strong in both political, emotional and organizational.
At the same time, Dr. Ma Chhoeun also prepared the history of the party working group to help Cheung Prey and Batheay districts, in which he himself has participated in working in Batheay district for 2 terms and in Cheung Prey district for 5 terms. Dr. also advised the party working group to continue to work in connection with the people, serve the people and participate in maintaining peace as much as possible to continue the development of the country, local development to move forward.
Please be informed that on the occasion of the 73rd Anniversary of the Birth of the Cambodian People's Party (June 28, 1951 - June 28, 2024) in Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province, today, Dr. Ma Chhoeun and Dr. Ouk Maly donated money to their members. A total of 13 million 864 thousand riels.
