The Code of Environment and Natural Resources, which took eight years to compile, was officially announced.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 28, 2024, the Ministry of Environment announced the official launch of the Environmental and Natural Resources Code after eight years of drafting. The Code of Environment and Natural Resources consists of 12 articles and 865 articles.
The Code of Environment and Natural Resources was initially supported and prepared by Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An. The process of drafting the Environmental and Natural Resources Code took a long time, from 2015 to the present, with nearly eight years, with several meetings with relevant ministries and institutions.
The launching ceremony was presided over by Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, Dr. Mong Reththy, Chairman of the Third Committee of the Senate, and was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State and leaders of the Ministry of Environment. More at the Ministry of Environment.
It should be noted that the Code of Environment and Natural Resources was discussed and approved by the 9th session of the 6th legislature on May 30, 2023 under the high presidency of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, in the presence of members of the National Assembly. At the beginning of the session, 100 people.
This Code of Environment and Natural Resources complements and is consistent with relevant laws such as the Penal Code, the Civil Code, the Forestry Law, the Fisheries Law, the Law on Management and Exploitation of Mineral Resources, the Land Law, the Tourism Law, and the Management Law. Water resources, etc. In order to continue to promote the process of national development and the strengthening of the rule of law to a new stage on the path of sustainability.
In this regard, the Code of Environment and Natural Resources has been formulated based on three main principles, including: 1) Legal norms in the field of environment and natural resources are integrated, and second: Legal documents related to the environment and resources. Nature is harmonized; and third, the relevant legal documents have been modernized to meet the evolving trends of society.
The Code of Environment and Natural Resources has been reviewed, discussed and revised in detail and in depth, based on key input received through consultations at the technical and political levels with relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, the private sector and local communities. .
Recognizing the necessity and benefits of disseminating the Code of Environment and Natural Resources, the Royal Government, represented by the Ministry of Environment, has prepared this publication to be distributed to officials of relevant ministries, sub-national administrations, legal professionals, judiciary, and law enforcement officials. And other relevant institutions as a whole.
