Samdech Techo Hun Sen Sends Condolences on the Death of Kong Nai
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, on June 28, 2024, sent a message of condolences to Ms. Kao Chen on the death of the eloquent elder Kong Nai.
The message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is as follows: "My wife and I are extremely emotional to be informed that the eloquent elder Kong Nai passed away on Friday, the 7th of Roch Khe Ches, the year of Rong Chhasak. 2561 is on June 28, 2024 at 12:40 noon at the age of 80 due to old age.
In this most sad time, my wife and I would like to share our condolences and sympathy with her and her family for the loss of the eloquent elder Kong Nai, the loss of her husband, father, grandfather, and great-great Brahmin temple. Dharma is inexhaustible, the loss of one of the great living legacies and one of Cambodia's rarest resources in the field of ancient Khmer long chapei.
Although the body of the eloquent elder has disappeared, but the elder has left a noble deed of honor, dignity, perseverance, perseverance and works of art that are admirable and proud for the Khmer nation that will remain. Always in her heart she is a wife, children, son, daughter and all her close relatives.
I would like to dedicate myself to pray to the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks, to help the souls of the eloquent elders to reach death, not to be wasted. Abbot Dr. Sar Sokha sends condolences over the death of Chapey Dong Veng, Kong Nai
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, sent a message of condolences on the death of 80-year-old Chapey Dong Veng Kong Nai, who died of a disease at his home in Doung commune. Svay Tong, Kampong Trach District, Kampot Province at 12:40 pm on June 28, 2024.
Dr. Sar Sokha said, "I would like to express my deepest condolences to the family of the eloquent elder Kong Nai, who passed away at 12:40 on June 28, 2024. In Doung village, Svay Tong commune, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province, he fell ill at the age of 80. ”
Elder Kong Nai's death is the loss of the living legacy of the Jabi Dang Veng art, a legacy of Khmer ancestral art left behind for a long time, especially after the brutal genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Physical and mental strength, care, protection, transfer of knowledge and leave work for the next generation of Khmer descendants.
Elder Kong Nai is a well-known Cambodian long-distance chapei artist with the title of Elder Kong Nai. In addition to having a national title as a living legacy, Elder Kong Nai has also won many national and international awards. With always appearing wearing black glasses, he is one of the most well-known and well-known traditional musicians in Cambodia and on the international stage.
The news of his death was a loss of human resources as well as an important living legacy that made the Cambodian people deeply saddened by this loss. Separation from the opposition is raging! Two locomotives of the Candlelight Party and the National Forces Party in Ek Phnom district declared their separation from the party and asked to join the Cambodian People's Party (Video inside)
