A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture led a professional officer to inspect and intervene the rice worms of farmers in Kampom village, Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province.
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Seak Leng, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on June 28, 2024, led a technical team from the General Department of Agriculture, General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Local Authority. Inspected and evaluated the results of the intervention, both natural rules and spraying on swarm worms in some districts in Oddar Meanchey province.
According to Mr. Sot Si Sok Kheang, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the past, three districts in Oddar Meanchey province, Anlong Veng, Trapeang Prasat and Samrong, have been affected by a total area of worms. 814 hectares, including 154 hectares of rice, 658 hectares of cassava and 2 hectares of corn.
The director of the department said that with the timely and effective intervention of all stakeholders and the rain for several days in a row, the presence of swarms in the three districts of Oddar Meanchey province has decreased and almost disappeared. In all, farmers' crops, including rice, cassava and maize, have returned to normal and no growth has been affected.
On that occasion, Mr. Seak Leng praised the excellent results, which reflected the efforts and active cooperation between technical officers from the General Department of Agriculture, the Department of Youth, commune agriculture officials and local authorities at all levels. And timely intervention to assist farmers.
At the same time, the Undersecretary of State also instructed all relevant parties to continue to pay attention to the presence of this swarm, and farmers must cooperate and report immediately to local authorities, agricultural officials, communes, departments or to the Ministry by phone 1289 free. Cost If any challenge needs to be intervened.
(Siem Reap): On June 27, 2024, Mr. Khun Savoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, inspected, evaluated, disseminated and taken measures to prevent the spread of swarms of worms that affect the rice crops and plantations of farmers. Some in Siem Reap, with the participation of Mr. Im Kim Leang, Deputy Governor, agricultural technical officers and some relevant officials.
A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture assessed that the outbreak of swarms of worms had decreased after people reported to the authorities and officials to intervene and educate agricultural techniques in a timely manner. Brief report on the activities of the Buddhist moral education program for the ordination of 500 children for 7 days and 10 sessions at Wat Phneat Simpaly
