(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Australia on June 27, 2024 jointly inaugurated a digital system and portal for registration and licensing for small and medium enterprises (SMEs), handicrafts and factories. This initiative facilitates business registration by replacing manual procedures, reducing the need to meet service providers, reducing request times and facilitating payments.
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, with the participation of government leaders and diplomats on the occasion of the National Day of Small and Medium Enterprises. 1. The event was also attended by entrepreneurs, representatives of business associations, ministries and institutions and many development partners.
Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, said: “The launch of this digital public service system is another significant step forward in our journey towards building a richer business environment. Efficiency and transparency. "By streamlining the registration and licensing process, we will reduce the administrative burden of the private sector and promote a more favorable business environment."
Prior to launch, the system underwent a series of tests by users, including officials from the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, company registration agencies, and representatives of small and medium enterprises, handicrafts and industries, including women and men. Also disabled. As a result, the ministry has developed this system to make it easier for businesses in the business registration process.
Andreas Zurbrugg, Chargé d'Affaires of the Australian Embassy in Cambodia, said: “This system is a testament to the joint efforts of Australia and Cambodia. "We are confident that this system will help eliminate barriers, expand Cambodia's potential in the small and medium enterprises and handicrafts and industries, and contribute to a more resilient, environmentally and economically sustainable Cambodian economy."
With only 13% of Cambodian SMEs properly registered, the system aims to increase official registration, which will enable SMEs to expand access to market access and support. From the Royal Government as well as promoting productivity, competitiveness and attracting foreign direct investment.
(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) and Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Party Working Group, presided over a ceremony to mark the 73rd anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) on the morning of June 28, 2024. In Battambang province.
The ceremony was held at the Happiness Center of Battambang City and was attended by Mr. Sok Loo, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, Chairman of the Party Working Group on Municipalities, Districts, Communes and Sangkats. Nearly 3,000 party members from all provinces attended.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng addressed the gathering, expressing his gratitude and appreciation to the leaders of the party working group at all levels who have worked hard to take responsibility and achieve great success in The last two elections, the election of senators and the election of our provincial councils of Battambang province.
"We should remember the basic principle of our party is to do good deeds," he said. "Doing good will get the support of real justice from the voters and the people."
"We have gained power and we must not be proud to act irresponsibly," he added. For the work of the party, in addition to what is contained in this speech, Samdech suggested that the party must prepare to review the organization of our party, not to change the structure, but about the composition and the ability and willingness to work. Need to update party members.
