He said that now Kong Nai's body has been kept for a traditional ceremony in Kampong Trach district, Kampot province, and his death was due to illness.
Elder Chapey Dang Veng Kong Nai was born on March 15, 1944 in Doung village, Svay Tong Khang Cheung commune, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province. Unfortunately, at the age of four, Kong Nai became paralyzed by foot-and-mouth disease and began studying chapei at 3 years old.
Due to his disability, he often faced ridicule from friends and people around him. During his two years of studying chapei, when he was only 15 years old, Kong Nai began to practice this profession and quickly built a reputation, and he soon received the nickname " Handsome »Nai.
Later, he continued to have a series of successes, such as:
In 1982, he won the first prize in the provincial chapei song. In 1991, he won the first prize in the national chapei song in Phnom Penh and became a chapei artist in the Department of Performing Arts of the Ministry. Culture and Fine Arts until retirement in 2007.
In 2003, he was the artistic elder of Khmer Living Organization and trained many generations of students until he was very old and retired in 2007. In 1982, he won the first prize in the provincial chapei song. In 2001, he received the Certificate of Elder of Khmer Culture and Arts by the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the Monisaraphon Medal from the Royal Government.
It should also be noted that Elder Kong Nai is one of the great traditional artists of Cambodia, one of the most well-known and well-known Cambodian artists in Cambodia and on the international stage. It is very sad that Cambodia has lost the legacy of a great person like him.
