The news of his death was a loss of human resources as well as an important living legacy that made the Cambodian people deeply saddened by this loss. Cambodia, Cuba stress efforts to strengthen trade cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Cuba have emphasized further efforts to strengthen trade cooperation, emphasizing the importance of expanding the relationship between the Ministry of Commerce and the private sector through online meetings and Exchange delegations.
The talks took place on the occasion of Mr. Chum Suntory, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, leading a delegation on a working visit to Cuba from June 24 to 28, 2024 to seek opportunities to expand cooperation. Transactions between the two countries. Third Bilateral Consultation
During his visit, Chum Suntory co-chaired the third round of bilateral consultations with Cuban Deputy Foreign Minister Anayansi Rodríguez Camejo in Havana on June 26, 2024. The meeting reaffirmed the long-standing friendly relations between Cambodia and Cuba and reviewed the progress in bilateral cooperation, focusing on trade, agriculture, health, sports, education, culture and information.
In the field of sports, the Secretary of State expressed his sincere gratitude to Cambodia for Cuba's support during the 32nd SEA Games in Cambodia and encouraged the full implementation of the Agreement on Cooperation in the Field of Culture and Education. Body and Sports Signed in 2022 between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of Cambodia and the National Institute of Sports, Physical Education and Recreation of Cuba.
The meeting also discussed cooperation within the framework of ASEAN-Cuba and the United Nations and exchanged views on a number of regional and international issues of common concern. The consultation ended with a strong commitment to continue the dialogue and cooperation, and the next meeting will take place in Phnom Penh at an appropriate time.
In addition, Secretary of State Suntory briefed the Minister of Foreign Affairs on the important results of the Third Bilateral Consultations, emphasizing the fruitful discussions on strengthening and expanding bilateral cooperation, especially on diplomatic, political and economic relations; Some potential areas include education, health, agriculture, culture and sports.
They also discussed the joint commitment to further strengthen cooperation within the framework of ASEAN-Cuba relations, the United Nations and other international organizations, and exchanged views on ways to further strengthen ties. Within the bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
Meeting with the Deputy Minister of Agriculture of Cuba In the meeting with the Deputy Minister of Agriculture Maury Hechavarría Bermúdez at the request of the Deputy Minister of Agriculture to discuss cooperation in agriculture, the Secretary of State and the Deputy Minister expressed their satisfaction. For the progress made in the past on agricultural cooperation and discussed ways to further strengthen this cooperation.
