Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Neak Oknha Kith Meng: The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce will continue to cooperate to promote more trade and investment in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Hun Manet
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council for Cambodia, on June 28, 2024, attended a press conference on the Franco-Cambodian Business Forum held at the French Embassy. Also in attendance were the French Ambassador to Cambodia, the President of the French Chamber of Commerce and Industry in Cambodia, and 30 national and international journalists.
The main purpose of this press conference is to promote the Franco-Cambodian Business Forum co-organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the French Chamber of Commerce and Industry in Cambodia and the French Foreign Trade Advisor in Cambodia.
He stressed that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce will continue to cooperate in promoting trade and investment in line with the Prime Minister's high recommendation to maintain existing investors and attract new investors in all fields.
The Franco-Cambodian Business Forum will be held on July 8, 2024 under the high presidency of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and will be attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the French side. And business people of both countries, including the French business community in Cambodia, as well as representatives of French companies operating in the region who wish to gain an in-depth understanding of the Cambodian market.
Over the past two years, bilateral relations have been strengthened, marked by a series of recent visits by Cambodia's top leaders to France, including the recent official visit of His Excellency Hun Sen. Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 18-19, 2024.
During the visit, seven memoranda of understanding were signed in key areas such as energy, infrastructure and the distribution sector, marking a new era of cooperation between France and Cambodia. These agreements also reflect the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to promoting private sector development.
Trade volume between France and Cambodia will reach 1,363 million euros in 2023. France is currently Cambodia's second largest European trading partner after Germany. French exports to Cambodia in 2023 increased significantly by 31% compared to 2022, mostly including agricultural products, pharmaceuticals and metal and metal products.
In addition to its large group subsidiaries, the presence of an active network of French foreign businesses (more than 400 companies) demonstrates French investment and presence in Cambodia. These figures show the strength of the Franco-Cambodian economic relationship, which benefits the companies of both countries and contributes to the development of the Cambodian economy.
The third day of the forum will take place in Sihanoukville to provide participants with the opportunity to explore key economic locations and meet with government representatives. The Franco-Cambodian Business Forum 2024 aims to act as a catalyst for new bilateral economic cooperation that benefits the sustainable development of the two countries.
