The Embassy of Japan and the Government of Cambodia welcome a delegation of Asian alumni to Japan, focusing on "E-Commerce between Japan and ASEAN"
This is the 22nd meeting aimed at strengthening trade exchanges and cooperation between Japan and ASEAN member countries through innovative activities in the form of digital and e-commerce.
Mr. Ou Nou Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, expressed his pleasure that the Cambodian Alumni Association of Japan has played an important role as a potential partner and has good relations between each member and the Alumni Association. In ASEAN countries.
At the same time, he believes: "The Japanese embassies in the nine ASEAN countries have good relations with the ASEAN Alumni Association from Japan, as the Japanese embassies in Cambodia are. "We also hope that these strong relationships will continue to expand and grow."
He would like to express his gratitude and appreciation to all members of the ASEAN Alumni Council from Japan (ASCOJA) for their cooperation. He strongly hopes that all members will continue to serve as a bridge between Japan and ASEAN countries and continue to play an active role in their respective fields in the future.
For Heng Sour, a former Cambodian Alumni Association from Japan, currently the Minister of Labor and Training, stated that our goal is to increase our skills and network to benefit Cambodian society and improve relations between Cambodia and Cambodia. Japan.
At the same time, the Minister of Labor said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is actively seeking to attract foreign direct investment from Japan and neighboring ASEAN countries, a policy strengthened by new diplomatic and economic missions.
Mr. Tsukiyoshi Fumi, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, said that the network of international alumni who have deepened their knowledge of Japan through study in Japan and have personally experienced the importance of accepting cultural differences and Mutual understanding is an invaluable asset for Japanese diplomacy.
"Many years have passed since I came to Cambodia, and this time I was surprised to see that Phnom Penh has developed beyond my imagination. In addition, I am still excited about the spirit and friendliness of the Cambodian people to Japan. This was further stated by the Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan.
Please be reminded that the Cambodian Alumni Association of Japan (JAC) had organized a meeting related to the ASEAN Alumni Council from Japan (ASCOJA) in Cambodia in 2018 in Siem Reap, which is a contribution to improve awareness. Of the Cambodian people about Japan and help strengthen the friendly relations between Japan and Cambodia.
Deputy PM Sun Chanthol Receives World Trade Group to Study Investment Projects in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, on June 27, 2024, allowed the World Clan Trade Delegation to meet to discuss investment-related work in Cambodia. The meeting was organized by the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
The main objectives for the working meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol and the leaders of the Cambodian Ministries and Institutions with the above Lin family trade delegation are:
Objective 1: To report on the update of the investment project study that the Lin family trade delegation discussed with the Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol on May 29, 2024 on two major projects. There are: 1: Durian cultivation and processing project 2: Health sector development on stem cell project.
Objective 2: The Lin World Trade Delegation requests additional recommendations from Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol and the leaders of Cambodian ministries and institutions on other potential areas, including: 1: Affordable housing development 2: Construction Phnom Penh flyover 3: Development of renewable energy (solar energy) 4: Metal production 5: Investment in education by establishing international standard schools in Singapore.
Objective 3: The Chamber of Commerce will invite the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Agriculture and Minister of Health to visit Malaysia and Singapore to see first-hand the achievements of the Duren agro-industrial project and stem cell research laboratories.
Speaking at the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol expressed his happiness and welcomed all investors who wish to invest in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that under the leadership of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the current Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government has facilitated investors who come to invest in Cambodia to grow the national economy.
Recognizing that Cambodia is a country with high potential and attractive investment opportunities, the World Clan Chamber of Commerce has mobilized its members from various countries, including Malaysia, Singapore, Japan and China. In Cambodia on May 25-29, 2024 recently.
