The second Franco-Cambodian Business Forum to promote investment and trade in Cambodia will be held on July 8-10, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian-Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry (CCIFC) will hold the second Franco-Cambodian Business Forum to promote investment and trade from July 8 to 10, 2024. The opening ceremony will take place in Phnom Penh under the high presidency of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
This business forum is conducted in collaboration with the French Foreign Trade Advisory Committee in Cambodia (CCEF) and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce (CCC) with the support of the French Embassy in Cambodia, the French Federation of International Employers (MEDEF) and the Cambodian Duke Association.
The event will be attended by members of the French business community in Cambodia, as well as representatives of French companies in the region who wish to better understand the Cambodian market, representatives from major companies such as construction and infrastructure companies, digital, Health, energy, urbanization, tourism, leaf logic, transportation, agriculture and agri-food, as well as sustainable development and the environment.
The volume of trade between France and Cambodia was 1.363 billion euros in 2023, with France now Cambodia's second largest trading partner in Europe after Germany. French exports to Cambodia in 2023 increased significantly, by 31% compared to 2022, especially agricultural products, food, medicine and metal products.
The forum also features presentations on the economic and legal vision of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as public and private financing. The roundtable will allow participants to discuss in detail the opportunities in priority areas such as tourism, digital, distribution, construction, health, energy, agriculture, logistics, transportation and the environment, as well as sharing experiences with language actors. France will enrich the talks.
