Chinese electric cars make indispensable contribution to green development
BEIJING: As the world enters a modern age, the environmental impact of over-development of traditional industries has become a common concern of the international community. From development in return for environmental impact to green development.
Following the introduction of the National Green Development Policy, China has begun implementing a number of relevant measures, including reducing greenhouse gas emissions and carbon emissions in daily life. In the past, in major Chinese cities, gasoline vehicles were an indispensable means of transportation. However, since 2001, the Chinese government has included the production and development of new energy vehicles or electric vehicles as a major project of national policy.
After many years of development, China's electric vehicle production technology has matured day by day. In the first phase of testing electric cars, the Chinese government has encouraged people who do not yet have electric cars to buy electric cars instead of gasoline cars, with some subsidies.
Initially, the difficulty of finding a charging station was a concern that led many consumers to be reluctant to buy an electric car, but later stations or charging stations were deployed on a large number of streets in labor units and communities. Can charge the car easily and quickly.
It should be reminded that Chinese-made electric cars are not only energy-saving and environmentally friendly, but in line with the advances in science and technology, electric cars are beautiful, modern and intelligent, which meet both aesthetic requirements. And consumables.
China has set a "double carbon" goal: achieving carbon emissions reductions after reaching a peak by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2060. In this sense, the use of electric vehicles is an important measure to reduce carbon emissions in daily life and has become an important current that people directly contribute to the country's green development plan.
From the above data, we can clearly understand that electric vehicles have played an indispensable role in the evolution from traditional development to green development, and China is also willing to cooperate with other countries to Together achieve the goal of sustainable development.
Sustainable development is the common vision of the international community. To achieve sustainable development, green development is the main task in this era, which requires countries to work together, but not to oppress each other for personal gain. A unique planet needs the united forces of nations to work together to preserve it for a long time.
