Sri Lanka still needs to persuade bondholders to restructure about $ 12.5 billion in international bonds, which the IMF says it hopes will see rapid progress in the near future. This.
Sri Lanka signed agreements with China and other creditor countries to restructure about $ 10 billion in bilateral debt on Wednesday, Reuters reported.
The deal brings Sri Lanka closer to completing its debt restructuring process, which began in September 2022 after its international reserves plummeted. The island nation failed to pay its foreign debts for the first time.
