Samdech Preah Moha Arey Vong Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat has been appointed as the Chief Bishop of Wat Ounalom
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Moha Arey Vong Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat has been appointed as the Chief Bishop of Wat Ounalom, succeeding Samdech Preah Akka Moha Sangka Rajathipati Tep Vong, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who was the Bishop from 1979 to 2024. He passed away on February 26, 2067 at Wat Ounalom, Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that the name Ounalom is derived from the name of the big stupa or ancient temple named Ounalom (eyebrow hair is the hair that grows on the meeting of both eyebrows different from normal eyebrows), which is the place to bury the hair of the Buddha. The name Aschit is stable, which is in the pagoda compound today.
Most of the history of this pagoda's chief priest is the title of Samdech who led the pagoda in the past, including Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Nil Teang, Samdech Preah Sangka Reach Chuon Nath, Samdech Preah Sangka Reach Huot Tat and Samdech Preah Moha Sangka Reach Tep Vong.
Please also note that at present, Samdech Preah Moha Areyvong Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat is the Rector of the Buddhist University of Sihanoukville and the Ballet of the Phnom Penh Capital Council.
