(Pursat): The international standard stadium project worth millions of dollars, namely "Samdech Techo Krakor Stadium" is scheduled to officially open on July 1, 2024 soon at the field of Samdech Yos. About 25 hectares in Veal Vong village, Sna Ansa commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the stadium will be presided over by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Pursat Province.
This project works to respond to the growth of sports in Cambodia and leave a legacy for the province, especially to attract investment from all walks of life by providing international standard gymnasiums to investors as well as workers because the location is Near Krakor Special Economic Zone, which also includes many large factories and enterprises.
The stadium includes an international football field, a theater, a volleyball court, a basketball court, a track, a badminton court, a gymnasium, a maze system, a lawn, a playground, a swimming pool and a parking lot. 22 more business-investment projects in Sihanoukville with a total investment of over 2 billion USD received special incentives from the Royal Government
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hean Sahip, Advisor to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in the morning of June 26 and 27, 2024, chaired a meeting of the Investment Promotion Working Group in Sihanoukville to review Proposed by investors and businessmen, in principle, provided incentives, favors, facilitation procedures and dispute resolution for 22 projects with an investment of more than 2 billion US dollars.
The meeting was attended by members of the working group and representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, including the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Health, the Gambling Management Committee and the Real Estate and Mortgage Regulators, as well as relevant officials and staff.
These projects are mixed-use projects owned by Cambodians and foreigners and small, medium and large with capital ranging from US $ 100,000 to US $ 500,000.
The above special incentives are in line with the "Special Program to Promote Investment in Sihanoukville 2024", which is a great initiative of the Prime Minister and was officially launched on January 31. 2024.
Through this and the following, from February to the present, the working group has achieved the principle of providing special benefits to 63 investment / business projects. In the near future, the team will review the special incentive proposals of 26 more investment / business projects.
Dr. Hean Sahip, Chairman of the Working Group, highly appreciated the support, especially the commitment and willingness of the working group and relevant ministries and institutions to contribute to the smooth implementation of special programs and improve the business environment in Sihanoukville. Favorable.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the work of statistics and civil status is an important task and a service that every Cambodian needs in daily life. Therefore, the officials who perform this work must continue to strengthen their capacity and must clearly understand the purpose and content of the new law.
He added that the work of statistics and civil status is an important task and a service that every Cambodian needs in daily life, and the civil status document is a document confirming the status of each individual, including: (1) Birth (2) ) Marriage and (3) death.
He added that from a legal point of view, civil status documents are written evidence that shows the legal status of an individual and is used as a basis for determining rights and obligations.
Based on this and in accordance with the National Strategic Plan on Identification for 10 years (2017-2026) in order to strengthen and modernize the work of identification, the Law on Civil Status and Identification was promulgated on July 1, 2023 And will come into force soon.
Mr. Keut Chhe stressed that the management of people's identities is an important national security task that allows the authorities to control and prevent crime. He suggested that registrars continue to strengthen their capacity and understand the purpose and content of the new law, as well as their knowledge of the use of technology. The administration must raise the training plan for 2025 as soon as possible.
