Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions Complains to Central Officials for 100 Million Riels
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, which represents more than 40,000 workers, filed a lawsuit against officials of the Center for Labor Alliances and Human Rights (Central) in court on the afternoon of June 27 after its officials used Insulting words hurt their reputation, honor, dignity, and discriminate against unions.
Hang Ravy, president of the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, told reporters in front of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court that Khun Tharo gave an interview to RFA on June 15, using the words "fake union" to attack independent unions and Fake youth or civil society to attack youth and independent civil society is the most serious false accusation that more than 40,000 workers' members are dissatisfied with.
"Khun Tharo's remarks have had a profound effect on unions across the country. Secondly, his impact has been on insulting reputation, honor, dignity, and discrimination, incitement to other forms of discrimination," he said. "I am suing Khun Tharo. I want to clarify that in the case where we sue Khun Tharo, we ask the court to take legal action against this person."
Mr. Hang Ravi said that in the lawsuit against Khun Tharo, a member of the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions demanded 100 million riels in compensation for mental illness, but all members did not want the money, the most important thing was to be clean. And all the budget that came from the Union agreed to donate to Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Huy Sambath, spokesman for the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, said that Khun Tharo's allegations were serious, without a clear legal basis, and that he violated the rights and freedoms and dignity and defamation. Professional organizations (unions) as well as the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions (CWPUC) with a certificate of professional registration.
He added that not only the use of the word "fake union" is a serious distortion and does not value the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Article 36, paragraph 5, Khmer citizens of both sexes have the right to form a union and Join this union member and paragraph 6, the organization and functioning of the union and set out in the law on trade unions and labor law. General knowledge: When was the motorcycle made?
