(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly President of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Excellency Yuon Sodary, sent a message congratulating Mr. Om Birla on his re-election as Speaker of the National Assembly of the Republic of India for the 18th term on June 26. 2024.
Through this message, Samdech stated: "On behalf of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia and on my own behalf, I would like to extend my warm congratulations to His Excellency who has been re-elected President of the National Assembly for the 18th term of the National Assembly. "Parliament of the Republic of India on June 26, 2024."
Samdech stated that the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of India have a long history of trade and culture. High-level exchanges of visits between the leaders of the two countries have provided additional impetus to these existing ties.
Samdech firmly believes that the friendship and multilateral cooperation between the legislature and our two countries will continue to deepen in the future for the common benefit of our two peoples.
He looks forward to continuing his close work and fruitful cooperation with Om Birla and his colleagues to strengthen our diplomatic, parliamentary and legislative relations at both bilateral and multilateral levels.
