Establishing a Digital Literacy Framework for Media and Information is the implementation of key measures in line with the guidelines of the Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework and the Digital Government of Cambodia policy, in which all Cambodians must become "digital citizens". It is an important pillar to support the digital transformation process in all areas and to take full advantage of the evolution of technology.
The purpose of this framework is to provide: 1: Provide a clear vision on the capabilities of digital citizens of Cambodia, 2: Promote the promotion of digital literacy, media and information effectively and comprehensively to each other, 3: Provide a basis for curriculum development Appropriate to the needs and circumstances and for assessing the level of digital literacy, media and information in Cambodia.
The Digital Literacy Media and Media Framework stipulates that digital citizens in Cambodia should have the ability to digitally digitize media and information in eight areas and have some behavioral knowledge in accordance with these eight areas in order to use technology wisely and thoughtfully. Responsible, efficient and safe.
"We aim to increase the digital literacy rate of the Cambodian population by 50% by 2030," said Chun Vat. "The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has set up community technology centers in public high schools, and digital skills will continue to be used in conjunction with the next literacy program."
He added that in addition, we should take advantage of the cooperation between the Royal Government and the existing private sector to increase the efficiency of projects implemented in the past by telecommunications operators, media and civil society organizations to continue to develop young people with disabilities. Less and turn them into "digital citizens".
