Senior Agriculture and Administration Officer of Svay Rieng Province Leads Experts to Evaluate the Results of Intervention on Worm Control on Rice Crops in Two Communes in Romeas Hek District
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Kim Son, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture in charge of Svay Rieng Province, and Mr. Sor Sodany, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, representing the Provincial Governor, led a working group and professional officers to inspect the situation of swarms of worms that are destroying rice in Romeas Hek District. To publicize and take immediate action to prevent further spread.
At the same time, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture and Mr. Sor Sodany and his team continued to inspect the cultivation of rain-fed rice and modern community vegetable cultivation in Svay Chrum and Svay Teap districts, and the working group also met with agricultural officials. 7 communes in Svay Rieng province to visit and discuss work.
At the same time, according to the Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, the impact of the rice worm epidemic in Svay Rieng Province has only been in Romeas Hek District in two communes, while other districts have not yet exploded. However, the authorities as well as professional officials will take the most drastic measures to prevent the swarm from spreading further.
In addition, Mr. Kimson also called on farmers in Ampil and Tros communes, Romeas Hek district, to visit their rice fields frequently. The nearest or can contact the agricultural officials in the commune-district so that they can provide technical advice or how to choose a drug to kill the worms.
