Chong Kal District Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province Instructs Students to Study Hard to Get Better Results
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Rithy Pak, Governor of Chongkal District, Oddar Meanchey Province, instructed the students who are preparing for the upcoming high school diploma (Bakdup) exam to study hard to get better results in the upcoming exams.
Remarks by the Governor of Chongkal District on the occasion that he led the team to meet with students and parents of students who are preparing for the high school exam at Hun Sen Chongkal High School on June 26, 2024.
Mr. Rithy Pak told the students that the date for preparing for the Baccalaureate exam is approaching and all the students have to do now until the day of the exam is to study hard and study with him. Teachers in schools need to learn more at home, generally speaking, do not waste time.
At the same time, the Governor of Chongkal District also told the parents who are the parents of the students who are preparing for the upcoming exam to give their children the opportunity to study fully and avoid taking time for their children to do other things. Children who miss out on special study time should be encouraged to study from now until exam day to get good results.
Mr. Rithy Pak also encouraged young students who do not get good results during the exam, do not be discouraged and despair, instead to find a real skill to practice in everyday life in the future.
He stressed that good learning is good for students, but not good learning is not sure that we fail in life, so it is necessary to grasp a certain professional skills.
He also called on all students, young men and women, to be good people, good youth, role models who are the bamboo shoots for the nation in the future, and not to be gangsters that the law is enforcing. Strictly avoid various tricks, especially away from all kinds of drugs.
