The yen weakened to its lowest level since 1986.
The yen weakened to its lowest level since 1986 against the dollar, prompting exchange markets to be wary of any signs of intervention by Japanese authorities to bolster the currency. That is falling prices. According to Reuters.
The US dollar traded at 160.39 yen, the highest level since December 1986, as interest rate gaps between the two countries continued to hurt the Japanese currency.
Analysts say traders are waiting to see the resolution of the Ministry of Finance and the Bank of Japan, which spent $ 62 billion in late April and early May to support the yen as the currency traded higher. Fell more than 160 yen to the dollar.
Although Japan has raised interest rates this year to between 0.1% and 0.1%, US interest rates from 5.25% to 5.5% mean that investors are rushing for higher returns on assets. Active in dollars, pushing the US currency higher against the yen. According to Reuters.
