(Phnom Penh): Yoga or Yoga (Yoga) has a history of more than 5,000 years in ancient Indian philosophy, which was originally a training of the mind and body. Nowadays, yoga is very popular as a fitness exercise.
Here are the 10 benefits of practicing yoga:
1. Breathing techniques: Breathing techniques focus on controlling breathing and can significantly strengthen lung function. Techniques such as deep breathing, mouth-to-mouth breathing, and nasal breathing can expand the capacity of the lungs, increase oxygen uptake, and improve the efficiency of the respiratory system.
4. Reduce stress: Chronic stress can worsen respiratory conditions and impair lung function. Yoga's focus on relaxation, mindfulness, and stress reduction techniques such as meditation and deep breathing can help reduce stress, improve mental well-being, and improve overall respiratory health. .
6. Increase oxygen flow: Yoga exercises that focus on controlled breathing and careful movement can improve the flow of oxygen throughout the body. Oxygen flow helps the health of the entire respiratory system, increases energy levels and reduces the symptoms of respiratory conditions such as asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).
8. Boosts immune system function: Regular yoga practice has been shown to strengthen the immune system, reducing the risk of respiratory infections and other diseases. By strengthening the immune system, yoga can help protect against exacerbation of respiratory conditions and promote faster recovery from respiratory diseases.
9. Improving the effectiveness of the lungs: Yoga encourages breathing techniques that improve the efficiency and function of the lungs. By practicing conscious breathing patterns, individuals can improve their airway rate, air volume, and airflow throughout the lungs, leading to better oxygen exchange and carbon dioxide emissions.
10. Support lifestyle changes: Incorporating yoga into a comprehensive treatment plan for respiratory ailments can support other lifestyle changes such as smoking cessation, maintaining a healthy weight and avoiding the surrounding factors that can cause Respiratory symptoms worsen.
