(Phnom Penh): At the Phnom Penh International Airport on the evening of June 25, 2024, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Mission, invited 19 Cambodian Hajj pilgrims to meet and retire after performing their pilgrimage duties in Saudi Arabia. Successfully for the first leg.
On the occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan said that in the last few days of the 2024 Hajj in Saudi Arabia, 1,301 people lost their lives due to long walks in the sun. There are no suitable shelters and shelters for the elderly and the chronically ill.
The senior minister confirmed that most of the people who died due to the extreme heat were illegal immigrants. More than 1.8 million people from around the world.
He added that those who go to Hajj legally have the right place to stay, have regular health care, that does not affect their lives due to the hot weather, including Cambodian Muslims. No one has been affected by the heatwave so far, but the Cambodian Hajj has lost one person to chronic lung disease despite a thorough medical examination at a hospital.
For the year 2024, a total of 910 Cambodian Muslims went on the Hajj to pay homage to them, in which King Salman Pin Abdul Aziz Al-Saud, King of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, presented 19 Cambodian Muslims with sponsorship. Fifty contributors, with a total budget of more than 5.5 million US dollars.
He said that this is because the people are able and have a prosperous life under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister and then Samdech Moha Bovathi Padei Hun Manet, who is making the country peaceful and constantly developing. And make it easier for people to eat.
Please be informed that from June 30 to July 15, 2024, nearly 900 more Cambodian Muslims will return to Cambodia, while those who return home today have The 19 are special guests of the King of Saudi Arabia.
