ASEAN Senior Officials of Cambodia Participate in the 39th ASEAN-Japan Senior Officials' Forum
(Bangkok, Thailand): Mr. Kong Phok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Senior Minister of Cambodia, attended the 39th ASEAN-Japan Senior Officials' Forum, which was held on June 24-25, 2024 in Phnom Penh. Bangkok, Thailand.
The meeting discussed and evaluated the effectiveness of the existing ASEAN-Japan cooperation and the future direction under the framework of the ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Strategic Partnership after the ASEAN-Japan Anniversary Summit to Celebrate the Year. 50th ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation in 2023
The meeting focused on partnerships for peace and stability, partnerships for future economic and social development, and a partnership of all generations.
The meeting also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern. Russia plans to block European media in retaliation
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia on Tuesday said it would block several EU media outlets, including the AFP website, in response to EU bans. Appeared on some Russian media last May. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, June 26, 2024.
The announcement comes after the European Union imposed a ban in May on four Russian media outlets allegedly under the control of the Kremlin. The EU said the media served as a propaganda tool for Moscow's invading war in Ukraine. Russia has condemned the EU action, accusing it of being politically motivated.
