BEIJING: China's new energy industry talk show was recently launched. The following are questions and answers related to this topic:
】 Questions】 This program will discuss China's building of clean energy, what is it? 【Answer】 Mankind has gone through many energy revolutions in history from the use of firewood and coal to oil Coming to new energy, zero carbon.
Research shows that about 2.4 billion people around the world use fuels such as firewood, coal and kerosene to meet their basic needs, such as cooking, heating and lighting. Experts note that this has a broad impact on human health. The World Health Organization estimates that 3.2 million people worldwide die prematurely each year from indoor air pollution.
Today, the active development of clean energy and the promotion of green and low-carbon socio-economic revolution have become a common concept of the international community in response to global climate change.
In particular, China's clean energy development has attracted worldwide attention. In 2023, the clean energy industry contributed 40% to China's GDP growth, and the green economy contributed 11.4 trillion yuan to China's GDP, a record high and up 30% year-on-year. . Growth and investment are driven mainly by the production of solar panels, electric cars and batteries.
It should be noted that due to the development and use of modern technology to produce clean energy equipment, which has pushed global prices sharply in just one year, the price of solar panels fell 42%, the price of batteries also fell. 50% as well.
In recent years, China's new energy industry has risen to a new level since 2023. Of the three vehicles imported from China, one is a new energy vehicle.
Chinese enterprises involved in the production of new energy vehicles now number more than 1 million. Most factories are located in Guangdong, Shandong and Jiangsu provinces. It should be noted that the Chinese economy is now focused on promoting the development of new quality production forces, ie innovation, good quality, referring to the future, making the industry smarter and greener.
China's goal is to build more than 40 national parks by 2035 with a total area of more than 1 million square kilometers, which will benefit millions of local farmers as well as increase employment opportunities. And assist in the development of tourism in the region. The harmonious coexistence of humanity and nature is one of the key elements in modern Chinese-style modernization.
