Singapore seizes more than $ 4 billion in assets involved in illegal activities and money laundering since 2019
SINGAPORE: The state capital has seized a total of S $ 6 billion ($ 4.4 billion) in assets since 2019, the government said on Wednesday. Money laundering. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, June 26, 2024.
In 2023, Singapore launched a series of raids on a massive S $ 3 billion money laundering case, one of the largest in the world. As a result, property, expensive cars and many luxury products were confiscated, while some foreigners were detained.
Of the estimated S $ 6 billion in assets, $ 416 million was returned to the victims, while about $ 1 billion was transferred to the state. The remaining billions of dollars are still under investigation and court proceedings.
