Samdech Hun Sen Presides Over 5 Guidelines for Relevant Ministries and Institutions and Veterans Association to Strengthen Veterans' Protection (Phnom Penh): Five recommendations to relevant ministries, institutions and veterans associations to guide the achievement of the Royal Government's strategic goals to strengthen the protection of veterans.
The introduction of Samdech Hun Manet was made this morning, June 26, 2024, on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 17th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2024. The ceremony was held at the National Defense University in Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
Recommendations made by the Prime Minister of Cambodia include:
* First, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation must promote the establishment of Commune / Sangkat Veterans Community Development Committees in the capitals and provinces and continue to collect data on the living conditions, challenges and needs of veterans, civil servants and families. And develop a well-functioning Veterans Community Development Program to increase the efficiency of providing better veterans' welfare support services.
* Second, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation must continue to implement well and effectively in providing social security for veterans and veterans' families and social security allowances, funeral allowances and one-time allowances, through National Social Assistance Fund (NFF) will work throughout the country to promote the implementation of housing projects for veterans and their families, as included in the Royal Government's public investment plan.
* Third, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation shall cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to continue to promote the implementation of the policy on the provision of social land concessions to the former Armed Forces and their families more effectively.
* Fifth: Relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities and the armed forces of all kinds must be involved in supporting veterans, especially to pay attention to supporting the families of veterans who are experiencing difficulties.
