Sri Lanka plans to sign debt agreement with bilateral creditors
The Sri Lankan government said on Tuesday that it plans to sign a long-delayed debt agreement with its bilateral lenders, including China, to meet key conditions for access. IMF relief fund.
The government had expected debt agreements with all its creditors before the end of 2022, but negotiations have dragged on.
According to the AFP news agency, bilateral creditors accounted for 28.5 percent of Sri Lanka's current foreign debt of $ 37 billion, according to Sri Lanka Treasury data at the end of March.
Court orders detention of 5 foreign criminals after Phnom Penh police cracked down and confiscated nearly 150 kg of drugs
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 25, 2024, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a detention order for 5 criminals, one Japanese and 4 Taiwanese, to be temporarily imprisoned after the Phnom Penh Police Force Phnom Penh launched a large-scale crackdown operation and seized nearly 150 kilograms of drugs.
It should be noted that on June 24, 2024, the Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor's Office yesterday issued a press release indicting five foreigners (one Japanese and four Chinese Taiwanese) in connection with 148 kilograms of drugs. Gram, which was cracked down on by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Anti-Drug Crime Force on a large scale in 2024.
A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court confirmed that on June 16, 2024, these criminals and drugs were raided by the Anti-Drug Bureau in cooperation with the Chroy Changvar District Police Inspectorate. 4 include:
After completing this operation, the police prepared a case file and sent the five suspects to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings. As for the factions involved in the above drug case, the authorities have been investigating.
After receiving and examining the case, the prosecution decided to charge the five suspects and their accomplices with "trafficking, storing, transporting and using illegal drugs and money laundering as a crime." "Penalties will be imposed in accordance with the provisions of Article 40, Article 5, Article 48 of the Law on Drug Control and Article 38 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing."
Speaking at a press conference on the afternoon of June 21, 2024, Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, said that this operation took place on June 17, 2024 in Chroy Changvar district. Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin claimed that the operation was carried out in accordance with the order of General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner, under the coordination of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
He pointed out that after several days of investigation, a group of Taiwanese Chinese were actively involved in drug trafficking in Phnom Penh and some provinces.
On June 16, 2024, at 20:30, the Anti-Drug Bureau's specialized force cooperated with the Chroy Changvar District Police Force to crack down on the above drug trafficking case by arresting a Taiwanese suspect named Fan. Yean Kuy, a 26-year-old male, at a point in a Borey, Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, confiscated 3 pieces of ketamine, equal to 3 kg.
Then, on June 17, 2024 at 14:10, the search force cracked down on 4 more suspects, 3 Taiwanese and 1 Japanese at Orchid Borey, Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva Phnom Penh.
The five foreign drug offenders have already been sent to prison. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police in collaboration with Prey Nup District Police Force Disseminate Road Traffic Law to Factory Workers in Bitrang Special Economic Zone to Reduce Traffic Accidents
