(Kampong Speu): Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, on June 25, 2024, disseminated the results of the evaluation and recognition of tourism service businesses that have done well in eliminating malaria in the tourism sector in Kampong Speu. Kampong Speu Province.
The event was attended by Mr. Kao Sonarith, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Dr. Huy Rekol, Director of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Archeology of the Ministry of Health.
On that occasion, Mr. Hor Sarun reminded that on April 30, 2024, the Ministry of Tourism cooperated with the Ministry of Health, the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bureaucracy, Kampong Speu Provincial Administration and the Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Tourism. The School on "Raising Awareness of Measures and Eliminating Malaria in Tourism" was established with the participation of tourism service businesses in Kampong Speu province.
Mr. Hor Sarun said that the launch of this campaign is not only to participate in the eradication of malaria in Cambodia by 2025, but this campaign will help protect the reputation of Cambodia's tourism destinations from suffering from the malaria crisis. And ensure safety, provide warmth and build confidence for tourists, all of which will make Cambodia's tourism destination even more attractive.
At the same time, Mr. Hor Sarun added that the eradication of malaria requires the participation of all sectors from all sectors and all levels, and today's award is a recognition and encouragement to Tourism service business base to support the "Malaria Eradication Campaign in Tourism" going forward in a sustainable manner.
In addition, in a message on the occasion of the National Malaria Day, the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Hun Manet, also stated that in the context of peace, political stability, freedom, unity, dignity and progress throughout the country. Cambodia is moving closer to "eradicating all forms of malaria by 2025."
The award ceremony and recognition of outstanding tourism business establishments made it clear that tourism business establishments have a very important role to play in eradicating malaria and contributing to the attractiveness of tourism through attention. Put the safety of tourists, which makes them more trustworthy and participate in promoting the reputation of Cambodia's tourism destinations.
He hopes that all tourism service businesses, especially today's winners, will continue to implement the malaria eradication campaign in the tourism sector more effectively "for Cambodia to be free of malaria, for the growth of Cambodia's tourism" in the cause. Contribute to the promotion of the Royal Government's political program in response to the sacred aspirations of the people towards achieving the vision of Cambodia by 2050.
Mr. Hor Sarun would like to thank the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration for supporting the campaign to eradicate malaria in tourism.
