Tuesday's meeting follows an April tripartite meeting between the two ministers and the US Treasury Secretary in Washington, DC, where both ministers were recognized by US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen. Concerns about their currency.
Concerns raised at the bilateral meeting will be closely monitored by the market. The yen is depreciating close to 160 yen per dollar. The 160 yen level, which erupted earlier this year, prompted Japanese authorities to intervene to support its currency as the won depreciated by about 7 percent against the dollar this year to a significant 1,400 won per dollar. .
"The two countries have become close neighbors," South Korean Finance Minister Choi said in his opening remarks. "Last year, the two countries renewed their currency exchange agreements and agreed on the importance of rapid financial market fluctuations, providing strong support for each other," he added.
The statement boosted speculation that Japanese and Korean officials could intervene as the dollar continues to appreciate amid a surprisingly resilient US economy. According to Reuters.
