KENYA (Reuters) - Police in riot gear stormed a rally on Tuesday, killing at least five people and wounding dozens more, officials say. This is according to the release by Reuters on June 25, 2024.
The incident comes as lawmakers are debating a new financial law aimed at raising taxes.
Demonstrators defeated police and drove them away in an attempt to storm the National Assembly, where flames were seen burning inside. Police opened fire after failing to use tear gas and water cannons to disperse the crowd.
Protests and clashes also took place in cities and towns across Kenya.
