The ICC said in a statement that its judges had found reasonable evidence to believe that Shoigu and Gerasimov were responsible for the missile strikes carried out by the Russian armed forces against infrastructure. Electricity of Ukraine. The attacks were reported to have taken place between October 10, 2022 and March 9, 2023.
The arrest warrant accuses the two senior Russian military officials of committing war crimes and crimes against humanity, leading attacks on civilians and civilian targets in Ukraine.
Russia, a non-member of the ICC, has repeatedly defended its actions, claiming that Ukraine's energy infrastructure is a legitimate military target and rejecting any intentional targeting of civilians or civilian infrastructure.
The International Criminal Court (ICC) action represents a significant increase in the international community's response to the ongoing Russia-Ukraine conflict, adding to the legal and diplomatic pressure on the international community. Rising on Russia.
