(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor and Chairman of Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, and Mrs. Relieve and bring humanitarian aid to 97 families affected by the typhoon from 22 villages in 5 communes of Bavel district.
Of the 97 families affected, 14 houses were completely destroyed, 33 houses were severely damaged and 50 houses were badly damaged by the strong winds. One person was killed by lightning.
On this occasion, Mr. Sok Lou delivered a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always pays high attention to the well-being of vulnerable and vulnerable people. Images without regard to caste, color, creed, religion, or political affiliation.
The President expressed his deep regret over the damage to homes, property, which was a natural disaster that no one wanted to experience, and said that despite the humanitarian donations brought to the people. Now there is an insufficient amount of your loss, but it can also alleviate your suffering for a while. That is, the Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone - never leave anyone behind.
Mr. Sok Lou continued to call on the general public to be vigilant against natural disasters that often occur without telling us in advance, and in that series, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has always issued a statement. Weather forecast news to keep people informed to increase awareness of possible natural thunderstorms.
He reminded people to pay attention to safety in traveling on the road to avoid traffic accidents, because in the past, many people were disabled due to war, but now we live under the roof of Peace, we must not allow ourselves to become disabled due to traffic accidents.
Please note that the humanitarian donation provided to each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 case of pure water, 1 case of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish, 1 blanket, 1 sarong. In particular, the people completely collapsed and added a tent skirt.
