Statement: The National Labor Union of Cambodia informs the network of buyers about Central's distorted report
(Phnom Penh): The National Labor Union of Cambodia (NLC), representing 70,000 workers, on June 24 issued a statement to the network of buyers on the report of the Center for Labor Alliances and Human Rights (Central). Disseminate facts, interfere, incite, divide and paint unions in Cambodia.
The contents of the statement told the network of buyers not to believe the report of the Central Organization, because the report only mentions the problems that occur between the union and the union in a company. The content is inconsistent with the title of the report and cannot be considered as an obstacle to the representation of all freedom of association in Cambodia.
The National Labor Union of Cambodia (NLC) sees the term union as an independent professional organization formed by a group of workers who have agreed to set up for the purpose of protecting the rights and freedoms and serving the legitimate interests of workers.
"In Cambodia, any union is independent, only some institutions are evaluating that this union is independent, that union is not independent," the statement said.
According to the source, some trade unions and organizations are under the command of civil society organizations that receive foreign aid and serve politics to some corrupt foreigners, and they often incite those unions to create images or problems. They want to slander, destroy the image of their country on the international stage, destroy the national economy, destroy the family economy and make workers afraid of losing their jobs and losing money.
"Confederations and organizations of this type always receive foreign aid, work for foreigners to destroy the common interests of their compatriots and destroy the image of their own country," the statement said.
At the same time, the NLC also requested the relevant authorities to investigate and take legal action against those behind Central and to investigate the assistance that Central has received to carry out regular activities with the intention of inflating. Indeed, inciting and destroying security, public order, causing instability, loss of interests of workers and our society as a whole. International Analysis: Why Malaysia and Thailand Want to Join the BRICS?
