Industry Minister praises Honda for innovating domestic production instead of importing, highlighting growth in domestic industry
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, praised Honda for its efforts in domestic motorcycle production instead of importing, promoting innovation and reaffirming the support of the Royal Government. For this effort.
Currently, most Honda Dream motorcycle components are manufactured in Cambodia. Not only that, some components are also manufactured and exported to neighboring countries. This development has raised the profile of Cambodian products and highlighted the growth of the local industry.
The Minister encouraged the company to open its production chain to small and medium enterprises to study and understand the company's standards and work ethic and encouraged the company to explore the possibility of cooperation with local small and medium enterprises to study the potential. Of the production of some of the more than 500 components for a Honda motorcycle.
In addition to recognizing Honda's environmental efforts, especially wastewater management, he urged the company to continue to invest in innovations such as robotic technology to help manpower and continue to develop human resources to manage and utilize those technologies.
At the same time, he suggested that Honda consider opening up opportunities for Cambodian artists to contribute to design, as well as providing financing options to expand the ability of Cambodians to buy Honda motorcycles and increase travel convenience. . Minister of Rural Development: Techo Village 100 project will play an important role in making rural areas more developed
This statement was made on the occasion of Minister Chhay Rithy Sen's participation in the meeting on the document of Techo Village 100 (TECHO Village 100) on June 25, 2024, chaired by Mr. Sous Yara, Chairman of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Information Of the National Assembly.
Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen thanked Mr. Sous Yara for giving him trust and confidence in the Ministry of Rural Development to continue the implementation of the Techo Village 100 project, which is a further contribution to the development of mixed villages, peace village development and development. Model villages that the Ministry of Rural Development has been implementing today.
The Minister informed about the vision of the Ministry of Rural Development is to improve the quality and value of life of people in rural areas with a comprehensive economic, social and cultural environment to achieve development and live in harmony and civilization. Outline four key strategies:
First. Development of physical and rural transport infrastructure to connect all rural villages with roads and become integrated rural areas, especially areas with high economic potential.
Second, improve the living conditions of rural communities through the supply of clean water and sanitation in rural areas, as well as training for people in rural areas to have a good attitude in living in a hygienic, clean and comfortable environment.
Third, diversification of rural economic activities through the training of basic skills, life skills to create jobs and occupations to reduce poverty and live in prosperity. In addition, the Ministry has focused on establishing model villages based on the economic, social and cultural potential and favorable conditions in rural communities.
Fourth. Strengthening institutions at both the national and sub-national levels in order to serve the people in rural areas with integrity, efficiency, efficiency and high responsibility.
