(Phnom Penh): In congratulatory message on the occasion of the 1st National Day of Small and Medium Enterprises, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, encouraged and encouraged the private sector to continue to contribute to the development of investment capacity to strengthen standards and The quality of its products and services increases productivity by continuing to train staff and provide social security.
In a message received by Fresh News on June 25, Hun Manet stated, "The Royal Government would like to encourage the private sector to continue to contribute to the development of investment capacity to strengthen the standards and quality of products and services. "It increases productivity by continuing to train staff and provide social security, as well as capturing technology and modernizing its production and service chains."
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet said that compliance with laws and regulations and accounting records should be promoted and considered a return on investment rather than a business burden.
In this regard, the Royal Government has introduced a number of key measures, including tax incentives, to support and encourage compliance with the sole purpose of enabling all enterprises to achieve accreditation. A sustainable market and receiving financial support and financial services for its potential expansion. Skills development programs are also a key priority.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the celebration of the National Day for Small and Medium Enterprises shows the great achievements of small and medium enterprises in contributing to the national economic growth in the past with efficiency and environment.
The Royal Government strongly hopes that all enterprises will continue to have a more positive impact in the future and may the theme of this First National Day be a source of energy and strength for promoting cooperation and mutual support. Mutual support between all actors of the entrepreneurial ecosystem.
On behalf of the Royal Government and the leaders of all ministries and institutions, I would like to support all activities and measures that will nurture and support this sector to grow for the prosperity of all our people.
At the same time, Samdech Hun Manet also called on the owners of small and medium enterprises and all stakeholders to continue to support the leadership and coordination of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation to promote this sector to become a pillar of development. Cambodian Economic Society.
According to the National Report on the Final Results of the Cambodia Economic Census 2022 by the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, there are 753,670 small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) with a total workforce of 2,980,569, including women. 1,841,362 people.
