(Laos): On June 25, 2024, the six countries of the Greater Mekong Subregion: Cambodia, China, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam met in a meeting of senior police officers to control drugs in Bokeo, Laos. Which is a province in the Golden Triangle.
Mr. Kham King Phula Monivong, Deputy Minister of Public Security of Laos, said that the drug problem has seriously affected people of all ages and all walks of life, including students, workers, the unemployed, as well as some employees and civil servants. To have socio-cultural impact, political stability and social security.
With this, the Deputy Minister said that the joint promotion and cooperation on information exchange, capacity building can enable us to prevent, solve and solve the drug problem, which is a dangerous obstacle to threaten the order and social security, and called for Let all member countries continue to cooperate and help each other to maintain security and social order.
From that meeting, Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that all countries in the Greater Sub-Region have cooperated well to continue to plan for the fight against drugs, especially synthetic drugs. The increase along with the smuggling of drugs, chemicals into the production area has also increased.
After the meeting, Lieutenant General Yuthea also gave an interview on Yunnan Chinese TV. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: The opening of the second phase of the Bak Kheng factory is a complete closure of the water shortage problem that used to occur in Phnom Penh and Takhmao City
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, stated that the opening of the second phase of the Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant is now a complete closure of the water shortage problem. The coverage area of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has been in the past in some areas of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City of Kandal Province.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said this at the inauguration ceremony of "Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Phase 2 and Groundbreaking Ceremony for Bak Kheng Plant Phase 3" on June 25, 2024.
At present, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority can produce about 982,000 cubic meters of clean water per day, which can meet the current needs of the people in Phnom Penh. And Takhmao City of Kandal Province.
At the same time, the third phase of Bak Kheng plant, which started construction on June 25 and is scheduled to be completed in the third quarter of 2027, will boost the production of 1.2 million cubic meters of clean water. Days.
For the future direction, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority needs to continue its mission and role to increase production capacity more actively to achieve high quality, efficiency, and high quality, aiming to achieve The goal of sustainable development in the supply of clean water to the people.
The General Secretary requested the Board of Directors, leaders and officials-employees at all levels of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, the leadership of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, as well as relevant ministries and institutions, both at the national and sub-national levels. , Continue to pay attention to some of the following priority tasks:
First, ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations and all stakeholders must continue to work closely with the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation to implement the Law on Clean Water Management to ensure adequate water resources, without adverse effects. To the environment for the supply of clean water to meet the four basic conditions: quality, safety, sustainability, and affordability.
Second, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, as well as the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, must continue to expand the scope of water supply through the main network to the people, both in and out of town, through incentives. Involve the private sector in additional investment in clean water production, both large and medium, to help supply clean water to areas facing water shortages.
At the same time, the Ministry must continue to strengthen the implementation of laws and regulations in force in the management of licenses, as well as continue to strengthen the capacity of private operators to provide better water supply services.
Phnom Tnaot community forest land in Chhouk district was illegally encroached upon, experts seized 3 excavators
(Kampot): Recently, opportunists brought three machines to dig and dig the border to encroach on the land of Phnom Tnaot community forest in Lobeuk commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province, but these violations were reported by the authorities and Relevant professional institutions cracked down in time, confiscating exhibits and three Taikong Atrak people, brought them for interrogation and kept them at the administrative police station in Lobeuk commune on June 24, 2024.
After reporting to the provincial governor, the provincial governor instructed the competent forces to hand over the three tractors and release the tractor drivers to return home, instructing them to stop. Committing such crimes again.
The release was due to the fact that the three Atrak drivers were all mercenaries, as they did not know that this act was a crime. The director of the Kampot Forestry Administration confirmed that the expert will continue the procedure by inviting those who rented the three units to dig the illegal land above to come to the procedure next week.
According to the Kampot Provincial Forestry Administration, the Phnom Tnaot community forest land in Lobeuk commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province covers an area of about 458 hectares. According to the villagers, the land of Phnom Tnaot community has been occupied by opportunists for many years and there is free trade, but the local authorities have not confirmed any documents. However, citing that the community lands are all state lands managed by the community.
A man was hit by a car turning right and broke his leg in Khan 7 Makara and is being treated at Calmette Hospital. The victim asked for the intervention of the General Commissioner after the driver paid $ 300
This incident happened on June 23, 2024, at the Canadia traffic light on Russian Federation Street, Khan 7 Makara. After the incident, the car did not stop dealing with the victim, leaving only the phone number for the victim to contact later.
Until June 25, 2024, the relatives of the victim contacted the owner of the car, but the car owner said that he did not touch the motorcycle, but the motorcycle came to touch his car. The mediation took place at the 7 Makara police station, but the driver wanted to pay only $ 300, while the victim demanded $ 1,000 for medical treatment.
The victim, 18-year-old Put Seiha, was born in Sambo village, Sambo commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province.
Currently, the relatives of the victims have filed a complaint at the Police Inspectorate of Khan 7 Makara and requested General Commissioner Chuon Narin to help with the investigation to provide justice to the injured party. Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Delivers Congratulatory Message on the Occasion of the 1st National Day of Small and Medium Enterprises on June 27, 2024
The following is the full text of Hun Manet's message: Dr. Ly Thuch opens political dialogue at Wilton Park, London, UK to ensure the success of the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit Mines of the Ottawa Convention
On behalf of Cambodia, President of the 2024 Ottawa Convention and host of the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit, Dr. Ly Thuch is committed to the unifying mission of the spirit of international solidarity and the relentless pursuit of peace and security for all mankind. Towards a landmine-free world and restoring hope for communities devastated by the remnants of war.
Dr. Ly Thuch said that political-level talks in Wilton Park would lay the groundwork for the Siem Reap-Angkor Action Plan, an action plan to lead global mine action efforts and a goal to pave the way for a strong action plan. Promote the objectives of the Convention over the next five years.
In the political level discussion, HE Dr. Ly Thuch highlighted some important points, including:
1. Progress and Challenges of the Oslo Action Plan: The report on the implementation of the Oslo Action Plan (2020-2024) should reflect progress and challenges, including demining, stockpiling, mine clearance, mine awareness education, and victim assistance. Dangers of international cooperation, globalization of conventions and compliance measures. This report is in line with the Sustainable Development Goals, with a strong emphasis on participation in the international framework.
3. Priorities for Cambodia's presidency: Priorities for Cambodia's presidency, which at the beginning of Cambodia's mandate set clear priorities: Globalization of the Convention on the Implementation of Article 5 (Mine Action) and Victim Assistance. These priorities will lead to discussions and actionable solutions to ensure that everyone can live without the shadow of fear left by the remnants of these wars.
Finally, he reaffirmed that the commitment, dedication, and collective struggle can turn this vision into reality for a world where landmines are no longer a threat to life and create a legacy. Of safety, peace and hope for the next generation.
