On that occasion, Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet congratulated and supported the successful establishment of Cyber University of Cambodia Network and highly commended the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Management, Faculty and all staff of Cyber University of Cambodia. So far, 12 universities have joined as members and have developed both the digital infrastructure and the capacity of relevant officials to produce content and content.
This statement of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was made on the morning of Tuesday, 4 Roach Khe Ches, Rong Chhasak, BE 2568, which is on June 25, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech's official inauguration. The Cyber University of Cambodia network. The event was held at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia (School of Technology).
Samdech Hun Sen stated: "Innovation, the use of creative tools, how to create conditions, and the creation of online learning is a very important way, of course, not in our class, but not sure. That learning in the classroom is better than learning online, the determining factor also depends on a student.
At this point, Samdech President Hun Manet Ban also raised the question that if there are 30 students in the class and the students do not pay much attention to the explanations of the teachers, they will not learn. But if the student learns online, he pays close attention to the teacher's explanations and seeks to research more lessons, making the student who learns online more knowledgeable.
Hun Manet added that sitting in class or online is similar, but this point is constantly evolving, so to ensure this requires innovation.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the online course is to meet the needs of training because the current training needs flexibility and the new training does not need to sit in class and need to set study hours. In Cambodia, online teaching has become more prevalent during the Kovid 19 epidemic phase.
Regarding this online study, Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet reminded that this online study has been around for a long time in Cambodia, but just different situation because in the 90s there was not enough internet service, so teachers taught Video recording on TV, so this means that the teaching is similar, but just using different means.
Samdech Thep Dey Hun Manet: The quality of education determines the quality of human resources and the development of the country (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Thep Dei Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that the quality of education is the quality of human resources and the development of our country. This statement was made by Samdech President Hun Manet on the occasion of the inauguration of the Cyber University of Cambodia network on the morning of June 25, 2024.
On that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen stated that education must be proactive and have a long-term vision. Samdech's policy can be successful only if the staff is strong, clear and proactive.
"The quality of human resources is a determinant of the quality and capacity of our country for sustainable development," he said. "At the same time, the quality of education and training is the key factor, the quality of human resources, so we can say that the quality of training is an important factor for ensuring the development of our national competition."
Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet Congratulates and Supports the Successful Establishment of Cyber University of Cambodia Network and highly commends the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Management, Faculty and all staff of Cyber University of Cambodia Network Twelve high schools have become members and have developed both the digital infrastructure and the capacity of relevant officials to produce content and content.
At the same time, Hun Sen encouraged other universities to explore the possibilities of this network for the benefit of our professors and students. At the same time, Samdech thanked the development partners who helped to establish and operate the University of Cyber Cambodia from the first stage until the official inauguration now and in the future.
Minister Peng Po Na: Law on Inland Waterway Transport is a New Achievement of the Royal Government to Regulate Waterway Transport by Sea and Port
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that the Law on Inland Waterway Transport is a great achievement of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is the first law to regulate waterway transportation by sea. And ports in Cambodia.
He also stated that this law sets out the management and development of water transport and ports in order to maintain order and ensure the safety and security of water transport, as well as the construction and maintenance of relevant infrastructure and contribute to environmental protection. As well as providing investment opportunities and fair competition, equity and transparency to serve the national economy.
Mr. Peng Ponna said this this morning, June 25, 2024, on the occasion of opening a seminar to disseminate the law on water transport at the Phnom Penh Hotel and with the participation of Mr. Ou Sino Assusi, Ambassador. Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia Mr. Sanoy Kasimasa, President of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia, and many other dignitaries and participants.
Mr. Peng Ponna added that this law is an important legal tool to strengthen the management and promote the development of the water transport sector in the Kingdom of Cambodia to grow, which will contribute significantly to achieving the vision. Cambodia 2050 is a high-income country.
While the water transport sector is growing rapidly from day to day, the operation and operation of water transport and some ports are not yet implemented and implemented in accordance with the laws and regulations in force. It is necessary and important to manage, promote and develop the water transport sector to be better and more sustainable.
