Polish president expresses hope China can help bring peace to Ukraine
China did not attend the Ukraine Peace Summit in Switzerland in the middle of this month, saying it did not live up to its expectations without Russia. Russia, which launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, was not invited and condemned the rally as futile.
China has led governments with an alternative peace plan for Ukraine, diplomats told Reuters this month.
"I have expressed my views on the security situation in Europe and the world, especially in Europe," Duda told reporters after meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping in Beijing. "I hope China will ... support Russia's efforts to end the Russian-led war in Ukraine," he said, adding that such peace must respect Ukraine's international law and internationally recognized borders.
China and Russia declared an "unlimited" partnership before President Vladimir Putin ordered an invasion of Ukraine. Beijing says it is neutral in the conflict and has not supplied weapons or ammunition to Moscow.
Chinese state television reported that Xi had told Duda that China supported all efforts to bring the war in Ukraine to a peaceful end and that China would continue to play a role in finding a political solution to the crisis.
