Mr. Oknha Pung Kheav Se and Managing Director of the National Bank of Cambodia inspected the progress of the construction of Techo International Airport, which achieved 78%, equal to $ 1.134 million
(Kandal): Mr. Oknha Pung Kheav Se, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Canadia Group, together with the management of the National Bank of Cambodia and the Commercial Bank, on June 24, 2024, inspected the progress of the construction of Techo International Airport, which achieved about 78 % And.
Speaking to reporters after the visit, Mr. Charles Van, Managing Director of Cambodia Airports Investment Private Limited (CAIC), said that the management of the National Bank of Cambodia and the Commercial Bank noted that the construction This is very unique and seen as a construction on an unprecedented scale.
According to Mr. Charles Van, as of June 24, 2024, the construction of Takhmao Techo International Airport is about 78% completed, while the new airport is scheduled to open in the first half of 2025. Coming soon.
According to a press release from Techo International Airport, the visit underscored the strategic importance of Techo International Airport in Cambodia's economic development and ongoing infrastructure development.
Techo International Airport is Greenfield Airport with a total area of 2,600 hectares located 19 km from Phnom Penh. It is classified as a 4F airport and will be developed in three phases. The investment budget for the first phase is $ 1.5 billion, not including airport land.
The construction of Techo International Airport is now in its final stages, with the remaining $ 300 million to be spent on MEP, ICT and ID work, installation of special airport systems, including security and baggage management, airport work, including roads. Airport fire mats.
Construction of dams, fencing and pumping stations, testing and commissioning and ORAT. This is confirmed in the press release of Techo International Airport.
There are currently 16,000 staff and workers working on the project, and construction is now 78% complete with a total investment of $ 1.134 million, of which about $ 340 million through signage purchase. Bonds from banking and financial institutions.
