Cambodia, China Establish Cassava Coalition Association to Promote High Quality Cassava Processing
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-China has officially established the "Cambodia-China Cassava Alliance" to promote the cultivation, processing and export of high quality cassava products. The inauguration ceremony of the association took place on the evening of June 24, 2024, presided over by Mr. Varuth San, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
The Cambodia-China Cassava Coalition Association is a non-profit organization and is legally registered with the Ministry of Interior in order to promote the high quality development of the entire Cambodian cassava industry chain. Linking Chinese enterprises and scientific research institutions to the deep integrated development of Cambodia's cassava industry.
Mr. Vong Cheav, President of the Cambodia-China Cassava Coalition Association, said that the Cambodia-China Cassava Coalition Association is like a bridge connecting Chinese and Cambodian investors in the cassava sector. At the same time, he said, the Chinese side will also help Cambodian farmers on production and cultivation techniques, including materials to help Cambodia compete with other countries.
Mr. Varut San, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that the Cambodia-China Cassava Coalition Association will provide technical assistance to help promote the first strategy, which can produce more because the Chinese side may have factories with raw materials or technology to promote. However, increasing yields that make farmers profitable and can attract investors to process cassava in Cambodia, increase value added, as well as make the Cambodian people have more work to do.
China is the world's largest consumer of processed cassava, with annual imports exceeding 10 million tons (dry) and growing steadily, and is expected to reach 20 million tons (dry) in For the next 5 years. On this basis, it is very important and necessary to improve the level of cassava cultivation of Cambodian farmers, develop the value chain of cassava processing and open up direct trade channels between Cambodia and China.
Cassava is an important crop in the agricultural sector in Cambodia Cassava is also the second most important crop after rice, which covers more than 1 million hectares and yields more than 20 million tons annually. Cultivation, harvesting, processing and export of cassava provide employment and support for the livelihoods of tens of thousands of Cambodians. This is according to Ms. Son Keo Raksmey, Vice President of the Cassava Coalition Association.
However, she said, most of the farmers 'cultivation is still customary and follow from one area to another, so the farmers' cultivation has to be modified to apply the technique to get the yield. High.
