Mr. Chhim Sauki, Permanent Secretary of State, stated that in the first six months of 2024, the Ministry of Rural Development has achieved the results of the four priority programs of the Ministry, including:
First. Development of physical and communication infrastructure reached 44%. Improving the living conditions of rural communities achieved about 36%. Diversification of rural economic activities achieved about 52% and fourth. Strengthening administrative support services and general affairs achieved about 47% results.
In line with the strategy of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Rural Development has been actively involved in improving the quality and value of life of people in rural areas with a comprehensive economic, social and cultural environment to achieve development and live in harmony. And civilization, outlining four key strategies:
First. Develop physical infrastructure and rural communication so that all rural villages have access roads and become integrated rural areas, especially areas with high economic potential.
Second. Improve the living conditions of rural communities through the supply of clean water and sanitation in rural areas, as well as training for people in rural areas to have good living habits in a hygienic, clean and comfortable environment.
Third. Diversification of rural economic activities through training of basic life skills to create jobs and careers in order to increase income in addition to agricultural activities and reduce poverty and live in prosperity. In addition, the Ministry has focused on establishing model villages based on the potential and economic, social and cultural potential of rural communities and especially indigenous communities.
Fourth. Strengthening institutions at both the national and sub-national levels by implementing the policy of decentralization and deconcentration, as well as strengthening the capacity of civil servants in accordance with the principles and reform programs of the Royal Government in order to serve the people in rural areas with integrity, efficiency and effectiveness. High responsibility.
The Minister praised the efforts of all officials of the Ministry and highlighted the merits of the previous generation of leaders as well as other leaders who have achieved many achievements and leadership experience, which is a good example. For turn-by-turn guidance.
