(Jakarta): The Jakarta city administration is working on a plan to maintain the city's role as Indonesia's economic hub, despite losing its status as the capital. This is according to the release by Reuters on June 24, 2024.
Jakarta, which celebrated its 497th birthday on Saturday (June 22) and its last anniversary as the capital, contributed almost 17 percent to Indonesia's economy.
The local government hopes that the congested and flooded city can maintain or increase its contribution, but that vision may be hampered by obstacles.
Widodo has announced his decision to move the Indonesian capital from Jakarta in 2019.
