(Kratie): Sambo District Authority and Kratie Provincial Department of Agriculture on June 23, 2024, educated farmers on measures to prevent and eradicate swarms of worms that are eating crops of people in Kratie. At the local level, 980 families are affected, equivalent to 1,380 hectares in 4 communes of Sambo district, Kratie province.
Mr. Kong Meta, Governor of Sambo District, said that the officials of the District Office of Agriculture, Natural Resources and Environment, in cooperation with the professional officers of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, village and commune authorities, have educated and disseminated measures to prevent and control the worms that destroy the people's crops. In some communes in Sambo district, Kratie province.
According to the official, the swarms of worms are currently destroying the crops of 980 families on 1380 hectares in 4 communes in Sambo district, Kratie province.
1087 hectares of rice affected 877 families, of which 12 families in Sandan commune equal to 30 hectares, Kampong Cham commune affected 173 families equal to 159 hectares, Koh Khenh commune affected 413 families equal to 706 hectares and Sambo commune affected 279 families equal to 192 hectares. Separately, 103 families of cassava equal to 293 hectares, of which Sandan commune affected 80 families equal to 188 hectares and Koh Khen commune 23 families equal to 105 hectares.
