Senior Minister Kun Kim Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a New Headquarters of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Preah Vihear Province and Celebrates the 17th Anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day
(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on the afternoon of June 23, 2024, celebrated the 17th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day on June 21, 2024 and laid the foundation stone of the building. New headquarters of the Cambodian Veterans Association, Preah Vihear province.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Prak Sovann, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Association of Cambodian Veterans, as well as Mr. and Mrs. Chairman of the Provincial Association of Municipalities and Districts 3 and many other association members.
The Senior Minister also instructed the leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Preah Vihear province and in the districts to pay more attention to the veterans who lack veterans, difficulties or problems and to respond to them in a timely manner. Especially for homeless veterans, without land for cultivation, etc., to collect data and prepare to build houses and allocate social land concessions.
With the celebration of the 17th Anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2024, the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province brought a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association to 200 members of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Preah Vihear Province. Each person receives: 1 bag of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 bag of fish, 1 bag of fish sauce, 1 towel and a budget of 40,000 riels.
Police in Oddar Meanchey Province Trapeang Prasat District Arrest 6 Suspects
(Oddar Meanchey): Six suspects were arrested by the Trapeang Prasat District Police Force of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police with the confiscation of drug exhibits and other materials.
The district inspector said that with the operation to detain the six suspects, the police confiscated the exhibits, including: 6 packs of methamphetamine (ice), 1 big pack and 5 small packs, 5 mobile phones. Drug packaging materials and glass bottles and hoses that serve as drug paraphernalia.
Currently, the six suspects, together with the above exhibits, are being interrogated by the competent authorities in order to complete the case-building procedure and send it to the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police for legal action.
Royal Academy of Cambodia Holds International Workshop on Culture, Science and Technology, Food Security, Single Health, Food Safety, Climate Change and Economy
The workshop was attended by leaders, representatives of ministries, professional institutions, as well as representatives of many national and international partner organizations.
Speaking at the opening of the seminar, Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that this workshop has three main objectives:
First, disseminate and share information to the participants (representatives of ministries, institutions, development partners, national and international organizations, the private sector, senior research and training institutions, national and international researchers) to better understand the structure, roles and responsibilities. Of the Royal Academy of Cambodia as well as the achievements of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
Second, explore the possibility of cooperation in research and development in key areas such as culture, science and technology, food security, food security, single health, climate change, and the economy.
At the same time, Dr. Yong Pov said that the Royal Academy of Cambodia, a national gathering of researchers, has the main mission to play a role in scientific research to find input for the Royal Government and society and play a role in training. Benefits contribute to building human resources to strengthen the development of the nation.
(Phnom Penh): At the Ministry's office on June 24, 2024, Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Chairman of the National Committee for River Basin Management, opened the first inter-ministerial meeting of members of the National Committee for Basin Management. River.
The current inter-ministerial meeting was attended by the Secretary of State, the Deputy Chairman, the Permanent Vice-Chairman and members of the National Committee for River Basin Management, representing the relevant ministries, institutions, capital-provincial governors, ladies and gentlemen, directors of the Capital-Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, as well as the chairmen. And members of the Secretariat of the National Committee for River Basin Management.
Addressing the opening of the meeting, the Minister emphasized that the first meeting of the members of the National Committee for River Basin Management is aimed at strengthening inter-ministerial cooperation in river basin management, as well as discussing and strengthening basin management. Sustainable rivers.
He added that river basin management is an important practice in the protection of water resources, conservation and sustainable development in accordance with the Law on Water Resources Management in the Kingdom of Cambodia, ensuring the overall benefits to the system. Ecology and socio-economics.
At the same time, the Minister stressed that the management of the river basin requires the participation of inter-ministerial and stakeholders from various sectors, including national and sub-national government agencies, local communities, NGOs, the private sector and development partners to Discuss, plan, find solutions, and strengthen coordination mechanisms to ensure effective and comprehensive implementation of policies and programs.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia on November 30, 2023 issued a decision on the appointment of the composition of the National Committee for River Basin Management, chaired by Mr. Thor Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Deputy Secretary of State Lol Chhea Bunrith. The Permanent Chairman, together with the Secretary of State, the Deputy Chairman and 17 members from relevant ministries.
