General Department of Taxation Reminds Tax Incentives for Investment Projects in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation, through its weekly newsletter, reminded about tax incentives and other procedures for investors wishing to invest in Sihanoukville.
According to the General Department of Taxation, there are three types of investment projects that provide various incentives, including tax incentives and other procedures:
First, investment projects related to stagnant buildings, namely projects that have been built and suspended, suspended or stopped construction in Sihanoukville from 2016. Second: Investment projects that can be implemented immediately in 2024. : Expansion of existing projects.
The General Department of Taxation has confirmed that all three types of projects will receive various tax incentives, including the exemption of some important types of taxes, exemptions from registration fees, simplification of tax procedures in stages, exemptions from administrative penalties. Conduct tax audits and provide tax incentives as a state burden on the production and / or promotion of tourism products and tourist destinations in Sihanoukville.
To receive incentives under this special program, Cambodian and foreign investors, residents or non-residents can apply to the Investment Promotion Team in Sihanoukville, which has two locations: in Sihanoukville on National Road 4, Village 3, Sangkat No. 1 Sihanoukville or in Phnom Penh, located on the 21st floor Business Development Center, Sangkat Chroy Changva.
