National Police decides to suspend Colonel Bun Soeung, Deputy Commander of Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie, in dispute with a taxi driver
(Phnom Penh): The National Gendarmerie issued a press release confirming the suspension of Colonel Bun Soeung, Deputy Commander of the Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie after a dispute with Ho Thi, a taxi driver. On June 12, 2024.
After being widely shared on social media, the case of a dispute between a taxi driver and the Deputy Commander of the Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie, Mr. Sar Bunsoeung, General Sao Sokha, the Commander of the National Gendarmerie, was immediately assigned to inspect and hold a meeting. Command to discuss the above conflict case on June 21, 2024.
After hearing the report of the Office of Legislation and Inspection of the National Gendarmerie and discussed the facts, law and ethics for law enforcement officers, the meeting unanimously decided as follows:
1. To make a request to the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to suspend the position of Colonel Bun Soeung, Deputy Commander of the Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie in accordance with Article 41 of Sub-Decree No. 29, dated April 9, 2002. General for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
2. Proposing the establishment of a hierarchical disciplinary council in accordance with the Law on the General Statute for Soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Article 46 states: The organization and functioning of the Disciplinary Council shall be determined by a Prakas of the Ministry of National Defense.
According to the report, at 8 pm on June 11, 2024, Mr. Sar Bunsoeung, known as the Deputy Commander of the Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie, was accused by a taxi driver of taking his child. To catch him at Phsar Prom because of 20,000 riel.
