(Kandal): The mosque Al-Ek Chrey Andet Mosque in Prek Ta Prohm Village, Kampong Os Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province, was officially inaugurated on the afternoon of June 23, 2024 under the presidency of Mr. HUN Many, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Public Works. Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, after the construction was completed on November 10, 2023, at a total cost of 321,380 dollars.
Addressing the ceremony, Mr. HUN Many sent greetings from His Excellency Hun Manet to the participants who were present at the event.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many praised and thanked all the local and foreign philanthropists, Hakemtoun Ongmei Vakpuming, who have always supported the material, budget and spirit of building achievements to date. Serve the field of Islamic religion in Cambodia.
At the same time, he stated that Islam has contributed to other religions to play an important role in Cambodian society, especially the promotion of education, behavior and morals for all Muslim people. In this regard, the strengthening of the roles and responsibilities of the Imam Hakemtoun and Masurai, as well as religious schools, is very important and beneficial for the practice of religion and contribution to the development of the Islamic community and society.
He highlighted that the Islamic community has received humanitarian donations and assistance in the last five years, receiving a total of $ 24,042,196, including gifts of Ramadan food, cows and goats. Raya Haji festival every year.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many added that the factors of peace and political stability have provided an opportunity for all of us to come together to celebrate and gather suffixes from all over to build many achievements in the form of serving Islam as it is now.
As Cambodians, whether this generation or the next, must record and remember regularly that the genocidal regime actually took place. This bittersweet historical truth makes us understand the value of peace, which is the foundation of investment and development, as well as providing opportunities for the younger generation to learn, work, and bring about religious harmony. For the nation, too.
It should be noted that according to the report of the organizing committee of the inauguration ceremony of the mosque Al-Ekpre Chrey Andet, Chrey Andet village was born during the 1960s and currently has 217 Muslim families living in the area, equivalent to a total of 851 people, 443 females. People.
