China's new energy sector does not face overproduction
A special report released in 2024 by the International Department of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) shows that the industry's competitive advantage is achieved through hard work and real skills rooted in competition. Marketing, Innovation and Entrepreneurship. These strengths open up significant opportunities for mutually beneficial cooperation.
"China's burgeoning new energy sector is a testament to technological prowess and a major driving force in the global drive for sustainable development," the report said. "In contrast to oversupply, new energy infrastructure around the world has great potential."
At the global level, the shortage of new energy capacity is increasing. The International Energy Agency (IEA) forecasts a surge in demand, with new energy vehicle sales expected to reach 45 million by 2030, quadrupling sales. In 2022.
A statement from G20 leaders last year underscored the urgency, calling for a three-fold increase in renewable energy capacity by 2030.
"China's new energy vehicle sector is a testament to this growing demand, with both production and sales showing steady and strong growth in recent years," the special report said. This.
In the first quarter, profits in China's auto sector grew by an impressive 32 percent from the same period last year, highlighting the country's dynamic electric vehicle sector, the report added. .
