Power outage at Manchester United airport causes flight cancellations and chaos
Although electricity was restored at 7:45 a.m., the airport said flights from terminals 1 and 2 had been canceled and passengers were told not to go to the airport until Additional notice. Passengers planning to depart from the third terminal should arrive at the airport as usual, but have been warned that there may be a delay.
The airport also confirmed that the power outage could make it impossible to carry luggage and that it would work with the airline to ensure passengers receive their luggage as soon as possible. Passengers scheduled to arrive at the airport are being diverted to other airports.
Problems with the power supply in the area are thought to have affected the airport as well as other nearby buildings. Photos and videos on social media show a long line of passengers trying to check in and chaos on the luggage belt as passengers try to find their luggage without information.
