(Phnom Penh): The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has decided to detain the accused, the former tycoon Srey Sina, temporarily in the 1st Correctional Center (Prey Sar Prison). This is according to the press release of the Prosecutor and the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on June 23.
The statement added that after examining the damage to the two victims who died and two others were injured, the prosecution charged the case in two cases:
In the first case (two victims were killed), Srey Sina was charged with murder and unauthorized use of a weapon. In this case, the defendant faces up to 15 years in prison.
In the second case (two injured persons) charged with attempted murder and unauthorized use of a weapon, the defendant faces up to 15 years in prison.
After receiving the above two cases, the investigating judge decided to detain the accused Srey Sina temporarily in accordance with the law in force. The investigating judge will further investigate these two cases in case of finding new evidence that could lead to a change in the facts and charges. The investigating judge has the authority to change the charges. Persevere forever.
