(Phnom Penh): Scholars and researchers in Cambodia consider the book "Global Civilization Initiative by Chinese President Xi Jinping" is very valuable in promoting peace and harmony in terms of religion, culture and belief for all people. Ethnicity.
This presentation follows a book in Khmer on Understanding the Global Civilization Initiative was released to the public on the afternoon of June 21, 2024 with the support of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, the Cambodian Center for 21st Century Maritime Silk Road Research, and Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association.
According to Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association and the compiler of this book in Khmer, this book will be able to increase the number of readers and researchers in Cambodia.
"The main point of this global civilization is to focus on four main points: first, it is about mutual respect for diverse civilizations; second, it is a deeper understanding of pluralism; third, it is about learning from each other," he said. "Mutually, between different civilizations, and the fourth is to work together to improve the harmony between people by making people understand each other in order to build a community of common destiny."
Ms. Ieng Socheata, a Student of International Relations at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, highly appreciates the book in Khmer on the deeper understanding of China's Global Civilization Initiative, as it embodies an important educational meaning of global culture in promoting Harmony between humanity.
"I think the book in Khmer on deeper understanding of this global civilization initiative is very important because it gives us an understanding of global civilization for all mankind," she said.
It should be noted that Chinese President Xi Jinping launched the "Global Civilization Initiative" on March 15, 2023 to solve common problems of humanity and promote world peace based on four core principles: Respect for the diversity of world civilizations, 2-Dissemination of common values of humanity, 3-Focus on the continuation and innovation of civilization, and 4-Strengthening cooperation on people-to-people exchanges.
