The 26th Shanghai International Film Festival, co-organized by the National Film Administration of China and co-organized by the Central Radio and Television of China and the Shanghai Municipal People's Administration, was held on June 14 for 10 days. Days.
This year's Shanghai International Film Festival is held under the theme "City of Movies", with more than 3,700 films from 105 countries and regions registered for the competition. After the selection, 50 films from 29 countries and regions participated in the competition, of which 38 films were screened for the first time in the world.
2: The wave of innovation gathered here. Entering the new century, Shanghai's film industry chain has undergone transformation and development, forming a complete industrial ecological chain that includes production, distribution, screening and development. The vibrancy of the Shanghai film industry not only shows the future development direction of the Chinese film industry.
5. Audience friendliness is an indispensable driving force of Shanghai, a movie city. Shanghai has a deep cinematic environment, an active consumer market and a supportive audience of films with high cultural knowledge and aesthetic standards.
Therefore, Shanghai is not just a city, it is also a living movie, where everywhere is full of story and every time plays a different story. Here everyone can discover their own world of light and shadow and every dream can come true. This is Shanghai and this is the charm of "Movie City".
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Ngoeun Chanlin Polen, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Information in charge of Tbong Khmum Province, accompanied by Mr. Van Virak, Acting Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Information Department and his team recently visited and took pictures at the "Hong Waterfall" resort. »To promote to tourists to know and visit here.
