BEIJING (Reuters) - A spokesman for the Chinese embassy in Japan said that the Japanese side had recently re-slandered the South China Sea issue and made unreasonable accusations against China. Ignoring the fact, the Chinese Embassy in Japan is very dissatisfied and strongly opposes this and strongly protests.
"As we all know, the South China Sea Arbitration Court has seriously violated international law, including the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea," the spokesman said. China does not accept or recognize this trial, nor does it accept any initiatives or actions based on this trial.
Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture and local authorities educate farmers on measures to prevent worms from destroying crops
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Sot Sisokkheang, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture, Hunting and Fisheries, on June 20, 2024, cooperated with Samrong City Authority and relevant officials to inspect the situation of worms that are destroying rice farmers in Kandek village, Sangkat Samrong and Kamnob village, Sangkat Bansay Raak, Samrong city.
The director of the Department of Agriculture said this morning, June 21, 2024, that the inspection of farmers' fields now see that there are insects that are eating rice on the type of worms or worms and the team. Assessed that the damage to the farmers' rice crops is only an impact, not to the extent of damage yet.
In addition, the expert team introduced the method to get rid of worms and butterflies to the affected farmers to apply. 1 bite 1 liter of vinegar, 1 liter of wine mixed with 25 liters of water and sprayed on the fields with worms.
Mr. Sot Sisokkheang stated that throughout Oddar Meanchey province, the department cooperated with three district and municipal authorities: Samrong, Anlong Veng and Trapeang Prasat districts and continued to visit villages in the damaged areas as we know. Immediately disseminated preventive measures as well as techniques to prepare farmers for measures such as how to protect potatoes. And how to protect rice? And how to sprinkle lime?
He said that this campaign must be done together, including municipal authorities, district chiefs, village chiefs, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, agricultural officials, and the Ministry of Agriculture has also sent professional officers to help with this work.
The director added that it is not yet known whether the situation of worms that destroy farmers' crops will be relieved if there is no rain, but if there is heavy rain, this situation will be. Relieved because there are no doves, because this dove evolves into a butterfly, and the egg butterfly evolves into a worm, and this worm evolves into a dove, so if it rains, these animals will be gone.
In front of the director of the department also called on farmers who own rice fields to take measures to prevent damage to their own crops caused by this swarm of worms.
Khmer language book on deeper understanding of global civilization initiatives released to the public
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 21, 2024, with the support of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, the Cambodian Center for Maritime Silk Road Research in the 21st Century and the Cambodian-Chinese Association of Progress Researchers (CEC) co-organized a program to promote books in Khmer on better understanding. Deepen the Global Civilization Initiative, an initiative of Chinese President Xi Jinping.
Addressing the event, which was attended by a total of 80 people, Wu Chuanbing, Adviser to the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, expressed his sincere congratulations on the publication of Dr. Chea Monirith's new book and highlighted that it will help Cambodian readers. Fully understand and deepen the meaning of the Global Civilization Initiative and promote exchange and mutual learning between Chinese and Cambodian civilizations.
Dr. Nak Chendarith, President of the Cambodian Center for the Research of the 21st Century Maritime Silk Road, summed up that the Global Civilization Initiative summarizes four "joint initiatives": 1. Respect for the diversity of world civilizations. Common values of humanity 3- Focusing on the continuation and innovation of civilization and 4- Strengthening international cooperation to change humanity.
He agreed that the book in Khmer would help the public better understand the Global Civilization Initiative, which has been empowering as a pillar to support the building of a community of common destiny with the recognition of universal ideas and The responsibilities of superpowers, theoretical significance and practical values are constantly presented with the development of the times and the progress of mankind.
As the author and compiler of this book in Khmer, Dr. Chea Monirith stated that the compilation of this book to contribute to deepen the understanding of the Global Civilization Initiative initiated by the wise President Xi Jinping of China. Traditional Chinese philosophy and this book in Khmer will be able to increase the number of readers and scholars in Cambodia.
It should be noted that since 2010, Dr. Chea Monirith has written many books in Khmer on Cambodian-Chinese relations, Chinese philosophy, Chinese culture, and translated into Khmer the book on Xi Jinping: Governance of China.
A security guard and his wife, who gave birth at Techo Santepheap Hospital, received a gift from General Sar Thet
(Phnom Penh): After learning about the poor family situation of a security guard and his wife who gave birth at Techo Santepheap Hospital, General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner General, donated some gifts to the man's family through Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director The Department of Drug Offenses to support the needs during childbirth.
The donations include: rice, fish sauce, soy sauce, sugar, baking powder, salt, canned fish and baby milk, as well as 1 million riels. The team added that this is the motivation of the leaders who always take care of the people who are in need or needy, there is always a leader nearby.
Mr. Suon Sopheaktra and his wife were very happy and raised 10 fingers to thank the General Commissioner of the National Police, as well as to Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath and all the team.
