Two gangsters angry at a masseuse who threw the windshield of a lawyer's car were arrested by the police
(Phnom Penh): Two gangsters got angry with a masseuse because they did not give her a massage and stole money and ran away. The frightened man filed a complaint and asked the police to arrest the suspect.
After that, the police force of Kambol district conducted a search for several days before arresting the two gangsters. The incident happened on June 11, 2024 at about 5:30 in the morning on the concrete road south of the gate of Wat Snguon Pich, about 50 meters in Snguon Pich village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kambol.
The first suspect, Heang Pisey, 32, was the perpetrator and the second, Vorn Kuy Neang, 29, was the driver of a black Honda Dream 125 motorcycle. Boeung Thom, Khan Kambol.
According to the police, on June 11, 2024, at around 5:30 in the morning, the victim drove the car from his house in Thmor Da village on the concrete road of Snguon Pich village from south to north.
When they arrived at the scene, the suspect on a motorcycle in the opposite direction arrived and threw the windshield of the victim's car. He fled to the south and disappeared, while the victim filed a complaint and asked the police to search until June 21, 2024 to arrest the suspect.
Police said that after interrogation, the suspects admitted that they had thrown the windshield of the car because they were angry and a masseuse took 20,000 riel from them. Then they ran away without a massage for them, and they rode a motorcycle to find him. Suddenly, they saw the car above, thinking that the masseuse was in the car above, so they threw the windshield.
On the morning of June 22, the two suspects were sent to court for legal action.
Kampong Svay District Working Group Chairman Urges All Party Members to Have Good Unity and Internal Unity
(Kampong Thom): Ms. Khuon Khun Dy, Head of Kampong Svay District Field Team, urged all CPP members to maintain good internal unity. She said this at the district party monthly meeting on the morning of June 22, 2024 at the party office in Kampong Svay district.
She said that in order for the party to be strong and to have the support of the people, all party leaders and members must be united and have a strong internal unity by working together to resolve their concerns. In the local area in accordance with the procedures and capabilities of the local working group in collaboration with the central working group.
The chairperson of the working group must control the number of party members by implementing the retention of old members and the formation of new members in order to keep the party active and continue to carry out its work on a regular basis without neglecting to wait for election day. Not yet arrived.
She added that the dedication of the working group in the 11 communes in Kampong Svay district must continue to work closely with the central working group to study the needs, concerns and challenges to find a solution. Timely, appropriate, in accordance with clear principles and procedures.
In addition, she urges the team to do their best to serve them with their hearts, so that the work will be successful, not only money, but the heart that gives them warmth, confidence. A smile that makes us all successful all the time.
She went on to say that the grassroots working group must further strengthen its internal structure and continue to cooperate with the central working group, as well as reassure the working group chair, as well as support the CPP on the way to support. From the people in the new mandate.
Ms. Khuon Khundy thanked the central working group for their participation in the Party's working life by sacrificing their physical and mental strength, both financial and material, to help build trust and gain the support of the people in the 7th mandate. This. Donation of Raincoats by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Distributed to Troops in Preah Vihear Provincial Military Operation Area
