Minister Thor Chetha: Progress of Irrigation and Flood Reduction Development Project in Banteay Meanchey Province Achieved 46.97%
On that occasion, the Minister and the working group inspected the actual progress of the main locations of the project:
* 1: Veang Heng Reservoir with a reservoir area of 157.7 km2, a dam with a length of 6.23 km, with a maximum storage capacity of 4 million meters * and 2: Towel Reservoir with a reservoir area of 760.5 km The square dam is 7.12 kilometers long and has a maximum storage capacity of 15.3 million cubic meters.
The Minister stated that the development of irrigation system and flood reduction in Banteay Meanchey province is to increase agricultural productivity, reduce the impact of natural disasters and increase the efficiency of water resources, ensure adequate water supply for agricultural production. Use in daily life as well as serve interdisciplinary.
It should be noted that the Banteay Meanchey Irrigation and Flood Reduction Development Project will take 54 months to build, starting in December 2021 and scheduled to be completed in June 2026. The project has the capacity to irrigate a total area of nearly 20,000 hectares and has a population of 42,213 families.
Minister Chhay Rithy Sen Inspects Progress of Construction of 3 Roads and Conversation with Leaders and Civil Servants of Battambang Provincial Department of Rural Development
(Battambang): Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on June 22, 2024, inspected the quality and progress of the construction of 3 double-story paved roads (DBST) in Battambang province and had a meeting with Leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Battambang Province.
Activities to inspect the three roads include:
Road 1: 14,617 km long, 6 meters wide, 1 meter on each side, and there are some artistic structures connecting National Road No. 5 at Puk Chhmar village, Reang Kesey commune to Wat Kandal, O'Dambang 2 commune, Sangke district. The construction site was opened on February 5, 2024. So far, it has reached 10.10% and is scheduled to be completed on August 5, 2025.
Road 2: 14 km long, 6 meters wide, 1 meter on each side, and there are some artistic structures connecting Koh village, Koh Koh commune, Maung Russey district to Pen village, Maung commune, Koas Kralor district, which started the construction site on the 5th February 2024, so far reached 27.43% and is scheduled to be completed on August 5, 2025.
In inspecting the road construction site, the Minister instructed the technical advisor and the construction company on site to pay attention to the proper implementation of technical standards to ensure the quality of the road and longevity, especially should be considered. Selection of new technologies to replace rare and expensive natural raw materials.
On the occasion of inspecting the progress of the work, the Minister also met with people living on both sides of the road. The Minister said that all these achievements are due to the efforts of the Royal Government under the shadow of complete peace, which provides an opportunity for a happy gathering and can benefit greatly from these achievements.
Banteay Meanchey-Cambodia-China Friendship Radio sends two suspects to court in connection with drug case in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): On June 5, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Local Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, launched an operation to crack down on drug trafficking and illegal use at In front of Gold World Casino in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, two suspects were arrested.
The two suspects include:
* First name: Roeun Sopheak, alias Hup, female, 38 years old, unspecified occupation, current address: Kbal Koh village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city * Second: Name: Bin Sothet, 30 years old, Occupation: Uncertain address .
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that prior to the crackdown, the Municipal Gendarmerie received information from security that there were cases of drug trafficking and illegal use in front of the Gold World Casino. After receiving the information, the force went down to the scene and detained the suspect for questioning at the Municipal Gendarmerie Base.
After being arrested and interrogated, the two suspects confessed that they had actually bought drugs to sell and actually used. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has built a case and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime investigation and investigation, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and coordinated. Proceedings from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits have been sent to the provincial court by the Anti-Drug Bureau.
(Phnom Penh): Currently, the expansion of the use of new technologies is the expansion of business ventures in the tourism sector, in which Travelport Cambodia has played an important role in providing new technologies to travel companies to help communicate with tourists. As well as overseas tourism market more convenient, fast and modern.
She added that CATA always informs its members to be ready to change the way of communication of the tourism sector, that is, can not communicate directly as before. Instead, association members as well as tourism businesses need to be able to partner online.
She added that as technology advances and some CATA members do not keep up, they will lose the opportunity to communicate with the external tourism market, so please follow up with the association to develop the national tourism industry. More.
Mr. Aing Sovannaroth, Director General of the General Department of Tourism Industry Management, Ministry of Tourism, said that the use of technology is very important and has helped a lot in the tourism sector, the Ministry of Tourism has been promoting this work since before the 19 Kovid crisis. And the circumstances of Kovid became a catalyst for the use of indispensable technology.
Mr. Ang Sovanrath continued to highlight the importance of technological change and change in demand. Technological change is a necessary need of people and customers, so businesses need to know how to use those technologies. In the field of tourism, tourists do not have to travel to ask for information, buy tickets or book a hotel, etc. at the tourism business directly as before, they communicate with tour operators only online.
Restaurants in Pursat City Continue to Commit Not to Sell Wildlife Meat to Customers and Call for Joint Wildlife Conservation to Attract Tourists
(Pursat): By promoting awareness of the value of wildlife and facing legal action to bring wild meat to cook and sell to customers, a restaurant owner in Pursat has announced not to sell Food made from wild animals for guests to eat, although customers order and expensive.
According to Ol Oun Cham, manager of ZARA Restaurant in Pursat, a restaurant that has received a certificate of commendation from the Ministry of Environment for its commitment not to sell wildlife, since its inception in 2018, That uses wild meat as a dish to sell to guests.
He expressed the view that not taking wild meat for cooking for guests is a contribution to curbing illegal wildlife hunting "no eating, no trafficking and no hunting".
Mr. Ol Oun Cham added that the protection and conservation of wildlife present in the natural forest, it will provide many benefits to people living in mountainous areas, because wildlife can attract national and international tourists to visit. By that area and so on.
According to Mr. Chhorn Sophannareth, Representative of Mlup Svay Restaurant Manager in Pursat Province, if we protect rare wildlife more in the natural resource protection area, it will attract more tourists to visit. Provide employment opportunities for local people.
Mr. Sophan Nareth said that now, according to the publicity and measures of the Royal Government, more and more people are aware of the importance of wildlife.
"We should start with ourselves, not eating wild meat, not selling wild meat, because wildlife is very valuable for everyone," he said. Ask the owner of the restaurant who used to sell wild meat to cook for customers, please stop together to keep the presence of wild animals for generations to come.
The senior official emphasized that the participation of the restaurant owners is an important part in preventing the killing of wild animals and also to reduce the trapping in natural areas. The participation of the people is an important mechanism in the conservation of wildlife for the longevity of future generations.
