The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his pleasure and warm welcome to the presence of Dr. Saia Ou Pukala and his colleagues on their first visit to Cambodia after his appointment as Regional Director for the Pacific. West of the World Health Organization in February 2024.
In his replacement, the Deputy Prime Minister highlighted the good cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the World Health Organization over the past decades and praised the World Health Organization for its contribution to The perpetual development of Cambodia's health sector, including technical and financial assistance, and especially in the difficult circumstances of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
Dr. Saia Uypukala expressed his gratitude for the warm welcome from the Deputy Prime Minister during his mission and praised the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to develop the country. Establish policies, strategic plans and continuous investment until significant socio-economic growth.
At the same time, the doctor also praised Cambodia for its success in preventing and responding to the epidemic of Kovid-19 and reforming the Cambodian health system to be more resilient and resilient, ready to respond. To the challenges and epidemics that may occur in the future.
Taking this opportunity, Dr. also congratulated the Royal Government of Cambodia for the official launch of the "Roadmap to Global Health Coverage in Cambodia 2024-2035" and expressed strong support. Strongness of the World Health Organization through collaboration with the Ministry of Health of Cambodia to promote the implementation of this important road map to be more effective.
With his gratitude again, the Deputy Prime Minister also mentioned that Cambodia's current successes and achievements are the fruits of achieving peace and socio-economic development under the leadership of The wisdom of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister.
Meanwhile, the Deputy Prime Minister requested that the World Health Organization continue to support Cambodia both technically and financially in response to the World Health Organization (WHO) Global Resolution on Health and Climate Change, as well as the General Work Program. Fourteen new World Health Organization 2025-2028 aimed at promoting health and well-being for all people everywhere.
The Deputy Prime Minister wished the doctors and their colleagues success in their mission and strongly believed that this mission would contribute to the further strengthening and expansion of cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the World Health Organization. To be more robust.
