(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation has awarded the 2024 National Productivity Achievement Award (S5) of the Asian Production Organization (APO) to Lily Biscuit Enterprise of Tycoon Dr. Keo Mom for Promoting Productivity. Implementing S5 "in service manufacturing enterprises to increase productivity in service manufacturing enterprises to progress.
The award ceremony was held by Mr. Phok Sovannarith, Secretary of State, Representative of the Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation in the seminar to disseminate the "S5" Productivity Achievement Award 2024 on June 21, 2024 at the meeting hall. Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority.
It should be noted that Disk 5 is a method for organizing the workplace that is derived from the five Japanese words, including:
* 5: Shitsuke Consistency: Always train people to implement the 5 system, so it will become a habit and be kept in the work culture in the company.
According to Phok Sovannarith, a presentation by Lily Foods through a workshop organized by the National Productivity Center, the company has improved its production efficiency by reducing energy wastage (switching from a wood-burning stove to a wood-burning stove). ) Instruct staff to turn off the air conditioner 15 minutes before leaving the office to reduce damaged products ....
"The company makes tens of thousands of dollars a year, which allows the company to maintain the selling price of products (a pack of cakes costs 100 riel) from 2005 to the present and also be able to expand production for export." Mr. Phok Sovannarith further confirmed.
APO is an intergovernmental organization established in 1961 to increase productivity in the Asia-Pacific region through mutual cooperation.
