Dang Luong group is destroying 15 hectares of rice fields in Thpong district, Kampong Speu provincial governor led an agricultural officer to inspect urgently to find a solution for farmers
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of June 21, 2024, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, led a working group of local authorities and agricultural experts to inspect and assess the impact on rice damage of farmers in Keamony village, Rong Roeung commune. Thpong district, Kampong Speu province, after reports of the destruction of swarms of worms, where more than 15 hectares of primary rice are being affected.
Mr. Vy Samnang expressed his condolences for the destruction of the rice fields of the farmers by the swarm of worms that have been present in the above commune, and he sent experts to take immediate action on this case.
The Governor of Kampong Speu Province instructed the local authorities, especially agricultural officials, to continue to inspect various areas and investigate the presence of this swarm of worms in the districts and cities and take immediate action to intervene to save the rice of farmers. Avoid harassing these pests.
At the same time, the Governor of Kampong Speu Province also advised all farmers who are engaged in farming to pay close attention to the presence of worms, swarms and other pests that destroy your crops. In case of presence of worms, swarms and pests above, farmers should cooperate and report immediately to the agricultural officer of the commune or district so that the authorities and professional officers can intervene in time.
