(Phnom Penh): In order to strengthen the health and well-being of the staff of the National Bank of Cambodia and their families to receive high quality health care, which is to promote a better working environment and increase productivity of the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia has partnered with InterCare Hospital to help alleviate the health problems of officials.
The collaboration was held recently in the presence of Mr. Kruy Veasna, Secretary General of the National Bank of Cambodia and Mr. Jason Harrison, Co-Founder and General Manager of InterCare Hospital. Many other employees of Intercare Hospital as well.
The National Bank of Cambodia is confident in promoting health and productivity participation by providing a wide range of health care benefits and well-being and productivity enhancement initiatives by satisfying health care staff. Everyone. In addition, this collaboration will bring about many positive changes to the wider community by supporting various health and social initiatives.
InterCare Hospital was established in 2020 at the Olympia Medical Center and offers a comprehensive range of health care services focused on medical care with ease and a commitment to providing medical services with respect. And equality, ensuring that every patient receives the highest level of professional care.
It should be noted that this collaboration emphasizes access to high international standard health care in Cambodia and highlights the development of domestic health care services to reduce access to health care abroad. Also. CRC Siem Reap Branch Provides CRC Youth Towels to 203 Students from 4 High Schools in Prasat Bakong District
(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Siem Reap province on June 21, 2024, provided 203 Cambodian Red Cross youth handkerchiefs from 4 high schools in Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province. The ceremony was held in the presence of Ms. Tuy Chi Prak Sophoan, Vice Chairwoman of the Siem Reap Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross.
On that occasion, Ms. Tuy Chi Prak Sophoan said that the installation of CRC youth handkerchiefs for the 203 students now shows the attention of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Siem Reap in the fifth mandate. The Branch Committee then builds the human resources of the Cambodian Red Cross, the largest humanitarian institution in the Kingdom of Cambodia and an assistant to public authorities in the humanitarian field.
Ms. Tuy Chi Prak Sophoan continued that the Cambodian Red Cross, the leading humanitarian institution in Cambodia, will become a highly autonomous national association with a focus on four priority areas: First: Management Priority Sector Disasters, Crisis and Climate Change, Second: Community Health and Health Care, Third: Promoting Fundamental Principles and Humanitarian Values, and Fourth: Institutional Development.
She said that Cambodia considers youth as the fundamental and most valuable resource for economic, social, cultural, environmental development and peacekeeping. In all eras, in all societies, youth is a strong force with strong physical and mental strength, courage and perseverance in overcoming all obstacles, especially young people are the pillars of the nation both now and in the future.
She added that the Cambodian Red Cross Youth is a young volunteer who is one of the most important and active core forces in providing humanitarian services with high commitment and unwavering commitment in line with the theme "Red Cross". "Cambodia is everywhere for everyone" and "youth are agents of change in society."
Ms. Tuy Chi Prak Sophoan also instructed and instructed the Red Cross youths who were wearing handkerchiefs at that time to adhere to the spirit of solidarity between the youth of the Cambodian Red Cross and other youths in carrying out humanitarian missions. Absolutely any actions that lead to division, disintegration and solidarity as well.
