According to the announcement, some media outlets have recently posted on social media about the importation of durian fruit from neighboring countries to the Cambodian market, declaring that it is a product grown locally and using chemicals to Dip one foot into warm paraffin.
After receiving the above information, the Minister of Commerce instructed the professional officers of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and the suppression of "KPR" fraud. Urgently investigate and research on the market and at some border crossings of Cambodia.
According to the preliminary research results, the sellers of durians claim that the durians they display are Cambodian products originating from Kampot, Kampong Cham, Battambang, Tbong Khmum, etc., but the research shows the presence of imports. Durian fruit from neighboring countries below the thumbnails at some border gates of the country.
At the same time, the investigating officer of the General Department of PPR It was also observed that some imported durians were soaked in a substance that officials have not yet been able to identify and affect the health of consumers.
General Department of PPR And continue to conduct research to identify the substance in collaboration with relevant ministries and professional institutions.
