Senior officials of the Ministry of Interior chaired a meeting on strengthening the working conditions of the Committee on Combating HIV / AIDS and STIs
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ong Sopheavy, Secretary of State and Chair of the HIV / AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Interior, chaired a meeting on “Strengthening the Procedures of the HIV / AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Interior and Collecting Inputs Prepare a strategic plan to fight HIV / AIDS of the Ministry of Interior for 2023-2028 "Prepared on June 20, 2024.
The meeting was attended by the Under-Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, the Vice-Chairman, the members of the Committee on Combating HIV / AIDS, the Ministry of Interior, the Deputy Governor, the Deputy Governor, the Deputy Commissioner of the Capital-Provincial Commission, a total of 120 people.
Speaking at the meeting, she said that the HIV / AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Interior will act as a staff for the Ministry of Interior to participate in ending AIDS in accordance with the national policy and the government's national program will be integrated into the village policy. Communes are safe.
She also presented the key results and would like to urge all members to bring their duties to the sub-national administration, including:
1: Continue to prepare and adjust the composition of the committee and strengthen the working system, especially the quarterly meetings, reports, monitoring
3: Continue to advise health centers, health centers and health posts to strengthen the provision of medical services and solve problems as much as possible to patients who do not come for treatment.
4: Continuing to lead the administration of communes, sangkats, municipalities, districts, Khans, especially front-line officials who provide public administration services by creating an atmosphere of peace and non-discrimination to the victims. In particular, they provide continuing education, outreach, counseling services, free testing to target groups facing HIV / AIDS.
It should be noted that between 2020 and 2021, when national and global institutions are forced to divert resources to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, in late 2021 and early 2022, there will be a resurgence of HIV / AIDS. The number of new infections and deaths from HIV is alarming.
On the issue of HIV / AIDS as a threat to public health, the Royal Government of Cambodia for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly unanimously approved the National Policy to End AIDS and Sustainable AIDS Program for 2023-2028 on 15 March. 2024 recently.
The National Policy to End AIDS and the Sustainability of the AIDS Program for 2023-2028 is designed to be a vital tool in promoting multidisciplinary participation in HIV and AIDS response at both the national and sub-national levels.
