World Bank approves $ 275 million new financing to support Cambodia's economic growth and resilience
(Phnom Penh): The Board of Directors of the World Bank on June 21 approved a US $ 275 million loan package to support Cambodia's efforts to boost economic growth and resilience in the long run. Far ahead. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on June 21, 2024.
According to the press release, the funding, which comes from the International Development Association (IDA) low-interest funds for developing countries, will be used to drive reforms aimed at enhancing the competitiveness of the private sector, strengthening the position. The country's finances will provide assistance to the most vulnerable populations.
"After recovering from the effects of the Kovid-19 pandemic and the subsequent quake, Cambodia is now turning its focus to To achieve high quality steady economic growth.
"The new loan will boost the competitiveness of the private sector, strengthen the government's fiscal position and provide assistance to the most vulnerable Cambodians," she added.
The Kovid-19 pandemic has slowed Cambodia's economy for the first time in 25 years, and the recession is among the largest in East Asia. The economy has now recovered, but its growth has yet to return to pre-epidemic levels.
This situation in Cambodia is a reflection of the global economic situation and the structural challenges of the country's growth pattern. Cambodia's structural challenges include poor productivity growth, low human capital development, and barriers to the establishment and competitiveness of private businesses.
Cambodia's economy is heavily concentrated in products, export markets and financing resources, which has been hit hard by the volatile situation. The country is also vulnerable to the effects of climate change, especially floods and droughts.
New loans will be used to address these challenges. This assistance will help create a conducive environment for the company's business operations, business closures and fair competition.
Other parts of the loan will help strengthen fiscal resilience by improving expenditure efficiency, mitigating capital expenditure risks and enhancing public-private partnerships, and strengthening the government's ability to mobilize financing through bonds. National.
The new loan will also facilitate the provision of timely relief to more vulnerable families in the event of a natural disaster or economic downturn, improve environmental regulations and improve disaster management.
Zelensky calls for protection of Ukraine's energy system (Video inside) (Kiev): President Volodymyr Zelensky on Thursday announced measures to protect Ukraine's energy system, including networks under attack from Russia. And the development of renewable energy sources to be used as alternative energy sources. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, June 21, 2024.
Russia's drone and missile strikes have affected about half of Ukraine's power generation capacity since March last year, while Thursday night's attacks on four regions of Ukraine left more than 218,000 people without electricity. "The lives of the Ukrainian people must be protected, and that includes energy security in particular," Zelensky said in a video address.
Zelensky has set out plans to manage the impact on Ukraine's energy infrastructure, including a solar energy development program, energy storage facilities and the search for alternative energy sources. According to Zelensky, the work must be completed before winter and before energy demand increases as the seasons change.
Russia invaded Ukraine's energy system in the early winter of the war in February 2022, while Ukraine had few air defense missiles in Western-supplied stockpiles.
