Unions in Cambodia support Kampong Speu court ruling to convict local union leaders
(Phnom Penh): Unions in Cambodia support the decision of the Kampong Speu Provincial Court to announce the verdict of Chea Chan, president of the local union of Wing Star Su, who committed the crime of conspiracy to steal. The announcement came after the Kampong Speu Provincial Court announced its verdict on the morning of June 20.
Fasali, president of the National Union Coalition, said he supported the Kampong Speu provincial court's decision to convict Chea Chan fairly and justly. He expressed his disapproval of any crooks who have committed illegal acts of stealing other people's property because no one can escape the law.
"I do not encourage the protection of a leader who is a thief. If it is found and there is evidence, there is a video and he really confesses, then it is our responsibility before the law," he said. In force, it is not possible to use the words justice or injustice.
Sam Soeun, president of the National Trade Union of Cambodia, said that the Kampong Speu Provincial Court's verdict against Chea Chan, a former worker and union leader at the Wing Star Su factory, was not a threat to persecute the union. It is a criminal case where the perpetrator must be punished according to the law. He stated that as a union leader, he must also respect the law, and if he makes a mistake, he must be punished, and he cannot take his role as a union to cover up his mistakes.
"We support the conviction of the Kampong Speu Provincial Court, which convicted the perpetrators of theft as well as other illegal acts," he said. "I also urge other unions to fulfill their profession in accordance with the law, not to use the union to cover up their mistakes."
It should be noted that this morning, June 20, the Kampong Speu Provincial Court sentenced Mr. Chea Chan to 12 months imprisonment with 6 months imprisonment and 6 months parole. Interior Ministry spokesman: 63 gangsters arrested on June 20
