View photo: Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Presides Over the Celebration of the Royal Ceremony
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, the 15th day of the lunar month, the year of Rong Chhasak, BE 2561, which is on June 21, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the celebration of the Royal Ceremony of Tikhayuvat Mongkul Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei, Honorary Doctor Dr. Non Nget, Acting Samdech Preah Moha Sangkareach of the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the age of 100, enters 101 years.
At the age of 11, he studied Khmer literature at Wat Po school, Po Angkor commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province. Two years later, his mother, Moeung Yim, passed away.
At the age of 17, he went to study Dharma Discipline, and at the age of 19, he was ordained as a monk by Venerable Prum Meas (Indather), a monk at Wat Po, Po Angkor commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
At the age of 21, he was ordained as a monk (for the first time) at the same Po pagoda, with Venerable Khlok X, Venerable Ung Chea, and Venerable Sous Meas as the Vice-Chancellor. The provision states that "Nanthero".
In the early 1950s, he left Wat Po to serve Venerable Prum Meas (Indather), a venerable monk who was seriously ill and treated at a school in Popel commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province. . Chres Thla Buddhists united to build the school into a new pagoda called Wat Ampovan called Wat Prey Chuor.
In 1963-1964, he continued his studies in Khmer literature for teaching at Wat Preah Vihear Andet, also known as Wat Chheu Teal Chrum, Kraing Leav Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province. After graduating and passing the exam, he returned to live at Wat Ampovan (Prey Chour) as a teacher until 1975, when the Khmer Rouge forced him to leave the seminary.
During the Democratic Kampuchea era of 3 years, 8 months and 20 days, Dr. Non Nget was forced by the Khmer Rouge to work non-stop like the general population, especially forcing Dr. to marry, but Dr. refused and kept Brahmacharya forever.
After the day of liberation, January 7, 1979, on Wednesday, September 13, 1979, he was selected as one of the seven candidates by the National Council of the United Front for National Salvation. He was officially ordained as a monk (second time) at Wat Ounalom, Phnom Penh.
After being ordained as a monk, he stayed at Wat Ounalom, Sangkat Chey Chumneas, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh for only 7 months and was a member of the Central Committee of Priests as well as an ordained priest to participate in the ordination ceremony in Cambodia. . This morning, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet presided over the celebration of the Royal Tikhayu Vattanamongkol Ceremony for Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Non Nget
