Through this project, RT4D expects that 20 entrepreneurs with disabilities will be able to use their brand-related knowledge and brand building to further strengthen their business.
On this occasion, Mr. Suon Vichea, Advisor to the Ministry of Commerce, Chairman of the Secretariat of the National Committee for the Management of Intellectual Property (CIP) and Chairman of the Department of Intellectual Property, expressed his pleasure that the Regional Trade Project for Development (RT4D) under The collaboration between the Department of Intellectual Property and RT4D has been successfully implemented and is now nearing completion.
He added that this achievement is due to the efforts of entrepreneurs with disabilities, the team of the Department of Intellectual Property and RT4D, who have spent valuable time involved since the announcement of the project until now.
Seeing the benefits of the RT4D project for Cambodian entrepreneurs, especially those with disabilities, the Ministry of Commerce has prepared a project proposal and has implemented the project until now, and the participation in this project is in response to the pentagon strategy. The first phase of the Royal Government to participate in raising the knowledge and increasing the competitiveness of Cambodian entrepreneurs.
