Dr. Moeung Makara urges the leaders and officials in Memot district to contribute to turning the military historical site of Techo Koh Thmor X 16 into a tourist site
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Moeng Makara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, urged the leaders and officials in Memot District to contribute to the transformation of the 16th Koh Thmor X Military Historic Site. A battlefield to become a tourist destination.
Dr. Moeng Makara stated that the main purpose of the working group of the Royal Government to visit Memot district is to contribute to turn the historical area that used to be a battlefield into a historical tourist area, agricultural tourism and a special economic zone that brings tourism. And export and import of goods between the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, to improve the living standards of the people and the national economy.
Dr. Moeng Makara highlighted the heroism of Samdech Techo on June 20, 1977, who decided to leave his beloved wife and children and change his life to save the nation and motherland of Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and led Building a country of peace and sustainable development to this day is the greatest merit for the entire Cambodian nation that Cambodian children will never forget.
As a Cambodian and on behalf of the leaders and members of the National Working Group on Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, we would like to express our deepest gratitude to the heroic example of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and all Cambodian heroes. Dedicated to the cause of our beloved motherland for the survival and peace, full development forever.
Please also note that Dr. led the team to commemorate the memory of Hun Komsat, the son of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who died tragically during the Pol Pot regime yesterday. November 10, 1976 at the district hospital, now Bun Rany Hun Sen Memot High School.
Dr. Moeng Makara continued to lead a team to visit the military historical site of Techo Thmor X 16, the site of the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia on the way to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on the 20th. June 1977 in Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province, Cambodia-Vietnam border.
