The National Council for the Khmer Language organizes a workshop on "A study of the word formation model of the National Council for the Khmer Language", glossary data extracted from the glossary and published 5,063 words.
(Phnom Penh): The National Council for the Khmer Language of the Royal Academy of Cambodia on June 20, 2024, organized a workshop on "Study of the word formation model of the National Council for the Khmer Language".
Based on the approved word data, this research aims to review the word formation model approved by the National Council for the Khmer Language to present and review the past implementation of word formation mechanisms.
The study of the advantages and disadvantages of the word selection method used in the past is an important contribution to support the technical committee and the National Council for the Khmer Language to decide and choose the method to continue to form. And adopt future terminology in order to maintain the balance of the Khmer language, the Khmer national identity.
Vocabulary data used for this study are excerpts from glossaries published from 2013 to 2022, including terms related to agriculture, medicine, economics, chemistry, physics, literature, linguistics, political science and diplomacy, philosophy, culture and fine arts, science and technology. History, geography, and architecture and construction. The total data is 5,063 words.
Borrowing words and borrowing even more grammar rules of a foreign language can affect the form and structure of the Khmer language, which is a non-critical language in the Mon ethnic group.
Unable to find Khmer words or Pali-Sanskrit loanwords or Khmer-Pali-Sanskrit pronouns tend to borrow phonetics from French to English, a model that is more widely applied in French-English loan script, phonetic recording Foreigners who are not in the phonetic system of the Khmer language have two standards of practice: Khmerization and the creation of alphabets.
A Reuters investigation released last week found that the US military launched a covert campaign during the peak of Kovid-19 in the Philippines to spread false information about the safety and efficacy of China's Sinovac vaccine. Like other life-saving supplies provided by Beijing.
Sinovac, the first Kovid-19 vaccine introduced in the Philippines, has been plagued by fears of its unreliability. Reluctance to vaccinate among Filipinos is higher than in other countries in the region, with almost half rejecting or unsure whether they should be vaccinated by September 2021, according to the report. According to a World Bank report.
The death toll from the epidemic in the Philippines has risen to more than 66,000, making it the second-highest in Southeast Asia after Indonesia.
