MOSCOW (Reuters) - During the visit of Russian President Vladimir Putin to Pyongyang on Wednesday, Russian and South Korean media reported that he had handed over another Russian Aurus luxury car as a gift to the South Korean leader. Kim Jong Un and Putin also received two dogs from Kim. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, June 20, 2024.
As a gift from Kim Jong Un, Putin received two North Korean Pungsan dogs. Russian President Vladimir Putin is known for his love of dogs. In North Korea, the two leaders signed a comprehensive strategic partnership treaty, including limiting the amount of military aid available if Russia or North Korea undergoes an armed invasion by the enemy.
