(Banteay Meanchey): The Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Base Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, conducted a crackdown on drug trafficking and illegal storage at a flat in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat. Ochrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro said that prior to cracking down on the case, the Municipal Gendarmerie had received information from security guards that there was a case of drug trafficking at a flat in Samaki Meanchey village, Poipet city. Immediately after receiving this information, he led the force down to the apartment above and arrested one suspect, Duch Kim Huot.
With the permission of Brigadier General Ban Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, and with the coordination of Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor's Office, the force searched the residence of Duch Kim Huot to find drugs. Some of them were brought to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for questioning and processing.
After being detained and interrogated, the suspects confessed that they had actually bought drugs for sale. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie local force has built a case to be sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of investigating and cracking down on crime, confirmed that the two suspects and their exhibits have now been sent to the Provincial Court by the Anti-Drug Bureau of the Provincial Gendarmerie Command. According to the procedure.
Stong district governor instructs teachers to pay attention to student safety, especially drowning
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, instructed teachers to pay attention to the safety of students, especially drowning. Mr. Say Kimlam said this at the ribbon-cutting ceremony for the inauguration of a new pond and many achievements in O'Chok Primary School in Prakeab Village, Msakrang Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province on June 20, 2024.
He advised students to study hard as much as possible, both in school and at home, especially parents to encourage, guide and monitor their children's education on a regular basis to ensure quality learning and results. Well, everyone has at least a high school diploma.
In addition, he advised principals, teachers, students, community to plant more trees on campus and greenery as a shade and as part of reducing global warming as today. .
Please note that the achievements inaugurated on this occasion include a pond size of 40 meters x 20 meters, 5 meters deep, equipped with solar lights, fences around the pond, school gates, lamps, fans, name tags, etc. Japan's continued support for Cambodia's 20224 Ottawa Convention and its continued support for the 2025 Ottawa Convention.
Both sides stressed and appreciated the important role of the Convention Implementation Support Unit (ISU) in providing support to the States Parties to the Ottawa Convention in fulfilling its obligations and compliance with the Convention's standards.
The two sides discussed the current contract and the process of selecting a new ISU Director, and agreed on the need for further discussions and consultations regarding the contract process and the selection of a new ISU Director.
The two sides discussed and outlined the requirements for continued support for Cambodia's 20224 Ottawa Convention and continued support for the 2025 Ottawa Convention, which Japan will assume in the near future.
