After taking office, Phnom Penh Capital Council held the first ordinary meeting for the fourth mandate.
(Phnom Penh): The first ordinary meeting of Phnom Penh Capital Council of the fourth mandate was held this morning, June 20, 2024 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall. The meeting was held in the presence of Mr. Mop Sarin, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor and Representative of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Mop Sarin stated that based on the provisions of Article 70 of the Law on the Administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans, the Council should hold its first ordinary meeting no later than 15 days after the inauguration meeting. He said that we announced the inauguration of the Capital Council on June 7, which means that we have complied with the law.
