Samdech Thipadei made the remarks at a ceremony to commemorate the national liberation struggle of Samdech Techo and his comrades 47 years ago at the Techo Thmor X 16 military historical site in Koh Thmor village, Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
President Hun Manet stated that the third phase is the opening of a new page in the history of the revolution against the color revolution, namely the phase of maintaining peace, which is the precursor of national development and harmony. Of all Cambodians under the roof of peace that came from the win-win policy of Samdech Techo, the former Prime Minister
Samdech Hun Manet continued, "This is evident from the historical reality, which clearly states that there was a beginning of the process towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on June 20, 1977, when the first military organization was formed in "May 12, 1978 and the establishment of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia on December 2, 1978, the victory of January 7, 1979."
He added that the day of the victory on January 7, 1979, the political victory on December 29, 1998, reached the end of the civil war in Cambodia, bringing peace and full national unity. This is an invaluable historical fact and the next generation of Cambodians must remember. President of the Cambodian Logistics Association: Cambodia's transportation activity has declined significantly as shipping costs increase by 10-20%
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Sin Chanthy, President of the Cambodian Logistics Association, on June 20, 2024, confirmed that currently, the transportation activities of Cambodia have decreased significantly due to the orders of people around the world. He is down.
Speaking to the press on June 20, 2024, Duke Sin Chanthy confirmed, "As for the activities of the transport, we see a lot of decline, this decline is the whole world, it is lost. Orders.
The president of the Cambodian Logistics Association confirmed that the cost of transportation seems to have increased slightly due to the geographical location of Cambodia, which has a lot of goods in and out of friendly countries of China.
"For a while now, exports from China as well as imports to China have been declining compared to the past, thus reducing the number of ships," he said. "When the hull is cut, it will lead to a 10 percent to 20 percent increase in shipping costs."
