(Phnom Penh): In the first five months of 2024, Cambodia exported more than 770,000 tons of raw cashew nuts to Vietnam, exceeding exports for the whole of 2023, earning more than 1 billion USD. Cashews have been affected by the hot weather.
He added that after the cashew harvest ended in early May, Cambodia no longer had wet or fresh cashew nuts, leaving only a handful of dried cashews. At present, the price of dried cashew nuts is between 7,300 riel and 7,500 riel per kilogram, which is a high price.
While the export of raw cashew nuts has increased so much, he also hopes that the export of processed cashew nuts will also increase as the number of processing factories in Cambodia continues to increase as the international market for imported cashew nuts Cambodia's processing also recognizes the quality of Cambodian cashews.
