Kambol District Hall held a meeting on the issue of gangsters with teachers, principals, deputy principals of public and private schools
(Phnom Penh): Kambol District Police participated in a meeting to disseminate information on gangs with the Kambol Khan Administrative Unity Command and Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Director of all public and private schools in Kambol district. To eradicate all gangster activities that often cause anarchy, beat each other, causing disorder in society.
The above meeting took place on the afternoon of June 19, 2024 in the meeting hall of Kambol district under the chairmanship of Mr. To Virou, Deputy Governor of Kambol district.
The meeting was attended by Colonel Hong Piseth, Police Inspector of Kambol District, Representative of the Local Commander of the Khan Gendarmerie, Khan Administration Director, as well as the Chief of the Office of Education, Youth and Sports, the seven Sangkat Chiefs, the seven Police Chiefs. - She is the director and deputy director of all public and private schools in Kambol district.
Colonel Hong Piseth told Fresh News that after Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Phnom Penh's deputy chief of police and commissioner, decided to take the second step in cracking down on the gang.
He also reported the matter to the Kambol district governor, and the district governor convened an emergency meeting involving the principals of all public and private schools. On that occasion, on behalf of the district police inspector, he asked all principals and deputy principals to raise the challenges, then the district inspectorate requested all schools to install security cameras and set up a telegram group with parents.
The inspector confirmed that he also asked the deputy director to check the students 'means and the students' handcuffs related to the sword and knife, and also asked the teachers to try to create time for the district inspectorate to disseminate information. Gangs and drugs make some students give up bad ideas and become good students, study hard for a bright future, avoid punishment.
Cambodian Human Rights Committee announces Cambodia's participation in Joint Statement on the Elimination of Global Sanctions on Homosexuality in Geneva
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee says that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to join France in supporting the Joint Statement on the Elimination of Global Punishment for Homosexuality, which will be issued on the 20th. June 2024, during the 56th session of the UN Human Rights Council in Geneva, Switzerland.
The Union of Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union requests the Central Center to correct reports that do not reflect the facts affecting the common interests of workers
"We find that the content of the above report does not reflect the facts and has no clear basis, which affects the national honor, affects the job stability and the common interests of workers in Cambodia as a whole." This is according to the letter from the president of the Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union.
The President of the Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union continued, "We, as workers' representatives, are very concerned about the impact on job stability and workers' interests, so we urge the Central Director to make adjustments. "Its report repeats the many achievements that are the progress of the common working conditions of workers and unions in Cambodia."
On June 20, 2024, Mr. Un Dara, Spokesperson of the Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union and Vice President of the National Assembly of the National Union of Cambodia and his colleagues also brought the above letter to the "Central" office to request The organization has revised the content of its report.
He told reporters in front of Central's headquarters that the Central report had been misleading investors, misleading investors into believing that union freedoms were discriminating and that buyers were moving out of Cambodia. Therefore, Central should re-study the progress of the Cambodian labor sector.
The letter also warned that in the event that the director of Central did not edit the report upon request, the Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union would write a letter to donors and the Ministry of Interior to review the compliance with Central's statutes and regulations. Comply with the laws of Cambodia and finally gather workers to hold large-scale protests in front of the Central Office and the Ministry of Interior to request the closure of the Central office.
