Ministry of Agriculture monitors and disseminates measures in response to the case of eruption of worms eating farmers' crops
(Phnom Penh): Due to the hot weather this year and prolonged, the life cycle of the larvae is shorter, the eggs hatch faster, eat more quickly and fertilize faster. Combined with the loss of biodiversity due to climatic factors, the loss of some beneficial species that often play a role in destroying these worms.
The swarms of worms also began to explode in large numbers, so far many provinces have already reported the problem and negatively affected many crops. Meanwhile, professional officials of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries have been rushing to monitor the spread of the response and intervene directly if necessary.
A similar incident had already occurred in Cambodia in 2016, during which time it destroyed the crops of many farmers in Preah Vihear and Kampong Cham provinces.
Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture, called on farmers to be extra vigilant, monitor their crops regularly and take timely action to avoid serious losses to crops. .
He said that in this case, finding a swarm of worms in their fields, farmers may have some options:
+ For effective and safe use, please follow the instructions in the label and use only pesticides that are registered with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Key Remarks by Samdech Hun Sen President on the Occasion of Celebrating the 47th Anniversary of the Journey to National Liberation Struggle
(Phnom Penh): On June 20, 2024, it has been 47 years since Samdech Techo Hun Sen and four other loyal comrades-in-arms took their lives as capital to Vietnam to seek support for Strive to liberate the nation and the Cambodian people from the brutal genocidal regime of Pol Pot and his cronies.
The ceremony, which took place on the border with Vietnam, was also attended by senior Vietnamese officials, senior Cambodian government officials, government officials, the armed forces, historians, scholars and youth.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet's opportunity to celebrate the 47th anniversary of the journey towards national liberation struggle:
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that this morning, Samdech was very pleased to participate in the celebration of the 47th anniversary of the journey towards national liberation.
* Samdech Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia is always grateful for the sacrifices of all compatriots reflected in the organization of this Memorial Day event every year to thank the parents, siblings and nephews of Koh Thmor villagers. There has always been trust in Samdech Techo Hun Sen from the beginning from 1970 to 1975 and until 1977.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the celebration of the 47th anniversary of the current journey towards national liberation is a lasting memory to commemorate the heroic example and great merits of the heroes, the heroines, the armed forces and the people. All citizens who have bravely sacrificed their lives for the cause of the motherland.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the patriotic sacrifices of warriors, women and people at all stages of history have led Cambodia to liberate its miserable homeland from the brutal genocidal regime of Pol Pot and to build Cambodia. Peace, social stability and development to this day.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Cambodian people will always remember the historical truth for the Vietnamese volunteer army and experts who sacrificed their lives to help Cambodia in the cause of national liberation and the people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet expresses his deepest gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Leader, as well as all the win-win political operators, as well as the leaders, members of the Cambodian People's Party and all the Armed Forces. Made great sacrifices until achieving complete peace, national unity and development in all fields for the benefit of the nation and the people of Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Cambodian people must be united in order to maintain this most difficult peace that has been achieved, no matter what the cost.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the pages of history are connected from one stage to another, which is divided into three major stages.
* President Hun Manet stated that the third phase is the opening of a new page in the history of the revolution against the color revolution, that is, the phase of maintaining peace, which is the precursor of national development and prosperity. Harmony of all Cambodians under the shadow of peace that comes from the win-win policy of former Prime Minister Samdech Techo
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that this history clearly states that the beginning of the journey towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on June 20, 1977, the first military organization was formed on May 12, 1978, Established the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia on December 2, 1978, and won on January 7, 1979.
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that it was only on Victory Day, January 7, 1979, that there was a win-win policy on December 29, 1998, leading to the end of the civil war in Cambodia, bringing peace and complete national unity throughout the country. This is an invaluable historical fact.
* Hun Manet stated that win-win politics still plays an important role in providing people's trust in the Royal Government, which has always given high priority to improving the lives of the people through environmental economic development. Which ensures the distribution of economic benefits to all citizens.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Capital and Provincial Authorities to set up Techo Santepheap Park and Techo Military Historical Area according to the location.
