Officials from the 27 EU member states have been debating the 14th sanctions package for more than a month. The new measures include a ban on Russian LNG transit and plans to hold EU operators accountable for any violations by their subsidiaries and partners in third countries. .
The point to be removed is the extension of the so-called "No Russia clause" to subsidiaries in third countries. This requires subsidiaries to enter into contracts prohibiting re-exports to Russia and re-exports for consumer goods in Russia. According to diplomats, Germany's reluctance stems from an internal disagreement between its foreign ministry and the chancellor's office.
