(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on Wednesday, June 19, 2024, led a high-level delegation of the Ministry to attend the 10th Singapore International Water Week 2024 in Singapore.
The 10th Singapore International Water Week in Singapore brings together about 20,000 governments, the private sector, civil society, water experts, meteorologists and environmentalists from around the world.
The Minister stressed that the main topics at the Singapore Water Forum 2024 focus on climate change, which affects all sectors, including water management, energy, environment, agriculture and the private sector, and that global climate change requires adoption. Attention and immediate action from the government, the private sector and the involvement of all stakeholders.
At the same time, the Minister emphasized that in the forum, there is also a specific plan and immediate response to:
* 1: Efficient and sustainable water management * 2: Sustainable environmental management through plans to reduce greenhouse gas emissions to zero in the atmosphere * 3: Search for renewable energy Environmental issues such as solar energy or the development of hydropower by conserving the environment *; and fourth, government-level participation and high commitment to responding to climate change.
