Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development Branch of the Ministry of Information Donates 400 Cases of Vitamin Rice to the Cambodian Red Cross
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 19, 2024, the branch of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development of the Ministry of Information brought 400 cases of vitamin rice for the third time and handed over to the Cambodian Red Cross, which took place at the headquarters. Central Cambodian Red Cross.
The ceremony was presided over by Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross and Ms. Tuy Serey Ratanak Netphatra, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information.
The Secretary-General said that for the supply of rice, vitamins, which are the most essential food to help nutrition for people of all ages, especially children. She continued, "In the past, the Cambodian Red Cross has brought this rice to help the most vulnerable children in orphanages in Phnom Penh, such as Borey Infant and Children's National, etc., and delivered to the villages." Some districts in the provinces as well.
That is why the Cambodian Red Cross, both at the central level and in all branches, always mobilizes donations from philanthropists on the occasion of May 8 to help people in need. This is according to her additional confirmation.
She added that the donations received from the Cambodian Red Cross will be used for humanitarian purposes, regardless of race, color or political affiliation. Especially the elderly, helpless and orphans, widows, many children and people living with HIV.
Ms. Tuy Serey Ratanak Netphatra said, "Today we are very happy to continue to join the Cambodian Red Cross to help the most vulnerable people in Cambodia, especially in remote areas where we can not go. To.
She also strongly hopes that the following opportunities will continue to bring these vitamins to help people continue to help supplement nutrition and improve the health of our human resources.
Please be informed that the branch of Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information has donated vitamin rice to the Cambodian Red Cross for the third time, the first time on July 23, 2016, 200 cases of vitamin food, the second time On December 8, 2023, 200 cases of vitamin rice were donated, and the third time, on June 19, 2024, 400 cases of vitamin rice were donated.
According to Ms. Tuy Serey Ratanak Netphatra, last week she also led the members of the Women's Association to distribute bags and school supplies to students of Kbal Chuor Primary School and Kampi Primary School in Chit Borei District, Kratie Province. More than 300 people.
