Key remarks by His Excellency Hun Manet Opportunity to deliver a keynote address at the "Cambodia-Singapore Business Forum" (Singapore): On June 19, 2024, Samdech Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the Cambodian Business Forum. Singapore, held in Singapore with a total of 481 investors from 348 companies.
The following are the keynote speeches of His Excellency Hun Manet on the occasion of the keynote address in the program "Cambodia-Singapore Business Forum":
* Samdech Hun Manet thanked the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Singapore Business Federation, the Singapore Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia and the Singapore Alumni Association of Cambodia for their valuable cooperation in organizing this event.
* President Hun Manet stated that this forum acts as an important forum to promote deeper relations between the business community and open up mutually beneficial opportunities. Cambodia and Singapore can work together to promote innovation, build strong economic ties and create a more prosperous future for our nation.
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia and Singapore have had a deep and lasting relationship since Cambodia's recognition of Singapore's independence in 1965.
* President Hun Manet stated that the strong Cambodia-Singapore partnership, which was founded by King Father Norodom Sihanouk and the first Prime Minister of Singapore, Lee Kuan Yew, is growing.
* Over the past decades, we have seen a resurgence of growing bilateral relations, high-level agreements and a shared commitment to progress.
* President Hun Manet stated that Singapore has become one of Cambodia's top trade and investment partners with an active exchange of goods and services. In terms of investment, by 2023, the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) has approved 268 investment projects worth nearly $ 4.9 billion.
* President Hun Manet stated that Singapore has always been ranked as one of the top 10 sources of foreign investment in Cambodia.
* Over the past decade, Singapore has contributed nearly $ 2 billion to Cambodia's investment landscape. Singapore's investment has played an important role in Cambodia's development, driving growth in areas such as manufacturing, real estate and hospitality.
* President Hun Manet says the two countries are working together to promote tourism, build key infrastructure and seize opportunities presented by digital transportation.
* President Hun Manet says that Cambodia's economic trajectory is impressive, with an average annual growth rate of more than 7% more than two decades before the outbreak of Kovid 19. Despite a minor crisis in 2020, Cambodia's economy is recovering rapidly, showing remarkable resilience in 2021, achieving a 5% growth rate in 2023, with projected growth. Will increase by 6% in 2024.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to creating a conducive environment for success for both start-ups and emerging enterprises in all fields.
* President Hun Manet stated that our new investment law provides incentives, including tax breaks for up to 15 years, for many priority areas.
* President Hun Manet says that while protecting investment guarantees, there is no discrimination between local and foreign investors and there are no restrictions on the transfer of profits and capital. The Royal Government has also launched a special program to promote investment in Sihanoukville by 2024, providing special benefits to investors in addition to the investment law, making the province a regional hub for diversification.
* Samdech Hun Manet said that for the connection and development of infrastructure, the construction of expressways, deep-sea ports, logistics centers, international airports and waterways, especially the Funan Techo canal, the groundbreaking ceremony on August 5, 2024 is Strengthen regional connectivity and ensure effective access to key economic corridors in Cambodia and across the region.
* President Hun Manet says that these strategic investments directly benefit businesses by reducing transportation costs and improving operational efficiency, allowing them to take full advantage of the huge potential of the regional market.
Samdech Hun Manet says Cambodia's commitment to energy sustainability presents a unique opportunity for Singaporean investors to rely on the potential of solar and hydropower, coupled with the ambitious goals set out in the 2022 Energy Development Master Plan. 2040.
* Samdech Hun Manet said that in the first few months of his term as Prime Minister of the Seventh Legislature, he led the 19th Government-Private Sector Forum to address the challenges and concerns raised by business units and investors in business operations. Of them in Cambodia.
* Hun Manet said that clear measures have been put in place to further strengthen trade facilitation and alleviate almost all burdens that lead the private sector to priority sectors such as tourism, agriculture, agro-industry, transportation and infrastructure. Construction, real estate, banking and more.
* President Hun Manet said that he warmly welcomes all Singaporean investors to explore the rich opportunities in the vibrant and growing market in Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet says those investors will have enormous opportunities for value-added sectors such as financial technology, innovation, digital technology, green energy and agro-industry. Singapore's technological expertise can be a catalyst for our industry transformation, creating mutually beneficial opportunities for both of our nations.
* President Hun Manet said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to provide comprehensive support and guidance throughout your investment process, ensuring a smooth and successful business experience. Ministry of Agriculture spokesman: Modern farming community will be able to compete with imported vegetables without closing imports
