(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of Tuesday, June 19, 2024, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, presided over the ceremony to build a reception and accommodation building. As well as awarding the winners of the poems, songs and drawings under the theme of the national liberation struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Yut Mith 47 years ago.
Both ceremonies were held at the Techo Thmor X 16 military historical site in Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. Techo Thmey X16 Military Historic Site is a historical site of the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his loyal comrades in the national liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot 47 years ago.
Under the leadership of General Sao Sokha, the current Techo Thmey X 16 military historical site has built many structures, such as the statue of King Kork Thlok, the Great Stupa to house the remains of fighters who sacrificed their lives during the national liberation struggle, the Techo Thmor Sala Friendship Museum. Sdech Neak Moha Chey Pond Forum, Helicopter landing site, football field table, planting trees and flowers, lighting roads, building rubber roads and some infrastructure.
Construction on Cambodia's most important historical site has not yet been completed, with General Sao Sokha continuing to build more than $ 1 million worth of hospitality and accommodation facilities.
After the Krong Pali ceremony for the construction of this building, General Sao Sokha also presented awards to the winners in the field of poetry, song and drawing on the theme of the national liberation struggle from No. 1 to No. 5.
By 2023, Kantha Bopha Hospital will treat more than 1 million pediatric cases, while the hospital will have to spend more than $ 42 million per year
(Phnom Penh): Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Executive Director of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, stated that by 2023, Kantha Bopha Hospitals in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap will receive more than 1 million pediatric patients. In that case, the hospital has to spend more than $ 42 million a year to continue its mission to provide free check-ups and treatment to infants, children and pregnant women.
This statement was made by Dr. John Narith on June 19, 2024 at a press conference on the progress of the "10,000 Riel 10,000" campaign of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, initiated by Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chan Mony Hun. Manet, Honorary President of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, held at the Ministry of Information.
Dr. John Narith continued that for the Kantha Bopha Department in Siem Reap, there is a maternity service (pregnancy and childbirth), a service that Kantha Bopha Hospital in Phnom Penh does not yet have. While Kantha Bopha Hospital, which is adjacent to the Royal Palace, also has access to specialized treatment services slightly more than children due to patients who have been treated for childhood diabetes and leukemia.
"For this year, the hospital has a cost of around $ 42 million, some can be added or subtracted depending on the year, whether there is a severity of any disease, such as disease," he said. "Dengue fever, which occurs every three to four years, is on the rise, so costs are fluctuating accordingly."
The Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia has informed all ministries, institutions, private companies and philanthropists, especially the national and international media, to co-sponsor the "10,000 Riel 10,000" campaign and to donate to save the children. Your donation is very valuable to save the lives of children in Cambodia.
