PM Hun Sen Continues to Meet with Former Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong
The Prime Minister of Singapore made the remarks at an official dinner hosted by Prime Minister Hun Manet and a high-level Cambodian delegation on Tuesday evening, June 18, 2024.
He reminded that the relationship between the two countries (Cambodia-Singapore) was established at the highest level back to the time of Lee Kuan Yew and Norodom Sihanouk, where they both enjoyed close ties through mutual respect. Each other. In fact, a day after August 9, 1965, His Majesty the King sent a message to Lee Kuan Yew stating that Cambodia had officially recognized Singapore's independence.
"Certainly for all of us in Singapore, we will never forget Cambodia's unwavering support for our sovereignty," he said.
The Prime Minister of Singapore said that over the decades, Cambodia-Singapore bilateral relations have grown significantly, marked by mutual respect and common aspirations and commitment to stability and prosperity in Cambodia. Area.
Trade and investment are important pillars of the two countries' relationship. Singapore was one of the first countries to believe in Cambodia's potential and today Singapore is one of Cambodia's top investors. Singapore's investment covers key sectors such as real estate, logistics, agribusiness and finance.
He said education and human resource development were also at the heart of Cambodia-Singapore relations. Both countries have paid close attention to investing in people. Cambodia is now the second largest participant in the Singapore Cooperation Program, with more than 18,000 Cambodian officials participating so far.
Lawrence Wong said Singapore enjoys strong cultural and people-to-people exchanges. These are facilitated by direct flights between Singapore and Siem Reap. Many Singaporeans and foreign tourists flock from Singapore to visit the magnificent Angkor Wat temples and other parts of the beautiful country.
He also expressed his pleasure during the visit of the President to Singapore, now there is also a special exhibition showcasing the replica of Angkor Wat decorated with more than 50 types of Khmer orchids and named hybrid orchids. One under the presidency of Prime Minister Hun Manet.
"Cambodia and Singapore are at different stages of economic development, but as two countries in Southeast Asia, we face common problems and we share similar views and interests on many issues," he said. We both have to go through a dangerous geopolitical environment and many more problems. "We both have a stake in making ASEAN a strong and prosperous country on the international stage."
Diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Singapore were established on August 10, 1995, 59 years before the independence of Singapore, Lee Kuan Yew, former Prime Minister of Singapore and former King Norodom. Sihanouk exchanged visits. Cambodia was also one of the first countries to recognize Singapore's significant independence in 1965.
Speaking at a joint press conference with the Prime Minister of Singapore on June 18, 2024, Samdech said that for decades, the two countries' relations have grown and diversified. Regular exchanges of visits between the leaders and officials of the two countries are often held between the two peoples. Tourism and education have strengthened mutual understanding and cooperation.
Singapore is an important partner of Cambodia in various fields, including trade, economy, infrastructure, development and people-to-people contacts.
"Going forward, we aim to deepen this partnership by seeking new ways, including in the development of human resources, food security, energy security and other key areas that are in line with our common priorities," he said. Aspirations for the future.
He thanked the Government of Singapore for its significant contribution to the development of Cambodia's human resources, especially through scholarships and integrated training programs, as well as extended care and well-being for our workers. The Singapore International Foundation has also made significant contributions through humanitarian projects in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
"We are committed to continuing our efforts to deepen our economic partnership, promote regional integration, support regional security and stability, and promote the prosperity, well-being and sustainability of our people and beyond," he said. "More."
Samdech also looks forward to receiving the Prime Minister of Singapore to visit Cambodia. He stressed that his presence is a testament to the long-term partnership between the two countries and the joint commitment to build a strong cooperative partnership that meets the aspirations of both countries. The King issued a Royal Decree ordering the retirement of 26 general police officers of the Cambodian National Police.
