(Singapore): The Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Singapore have agreed to promote stronger and more prosperous cooperation. The agreement was reached during a bilateral meeting between Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and Singaporean Prime Minister Laren Wong on June 18, 2024.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister of Singapore warmly welcomed the first official visit of the Prime Minister and the high-level delegation of Cambodia to the Republic of Singapore.
The Prime Minister of Singapore highlighted the long-standing relationship between Singapore and Cambodia, with 2025 marking the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries, and the current official visit of the President is a driving force for strengthening And expand relations and cooperation to be more prosperous and strong.
President Hun Manet thanked the Prime Minister and Government of Singapore for the warm hospitality and congratulated Loren Wong on his appointment as Prime Minister of Singapore.
He also highlighted the development of diplomatic relations between the two countries as well as the strengthening and expansion of cooperation in various fields, and the official visit will further enhance cooperation between the two countries.
On the occasion of the bilateral meeting, the two counterparts also agreed to further strengthen and expand cooperation, as well as support and share experiences in key areas, including:
1. Within the framework of political cooperation, the two counterparts agreed to continue regular political consultations between the Foreign Ministries of the two countries to further expand cooperation.
2. Trade and Investment Cooperation The two counterparts agreed to set up a joint working group to discuss ways and action plans to improve the country's trade and investment cooperation. Both.
3. Continuing cooperation in people-to-people exchanges, building human capital, vocational training, and promoting tourism through the expansion of more direct flights between Cambodia and Singapore, with efforts to attract tourists from Other countries visit both countries.
4. For cooperation in the field of energy security, the two counterparts welcomed the outcome of the Ministerial Meeting between Cambodia, Laos and Singapore, the establishment of the Ministerial Working Group of the three countries and encouraged the participation of the two sides. More relevant
5. Cooperation on defense and security The two counterparts discussed exchanges of visits by senior officials and training sessions, as well as cooperation on combating transnational crime, human trafficking and drug trafficking. Technology crime and online fraud.
In addition, the two counterparts continued to discuss a number of regional and international issues to participate in building peace, stability, unity and prosperity in the region and the world, as well as providing mutual benefits between the two countries.
