(Phnom Penh): Tourism connects the land! Traveled and got to know their country and helped to improve the livelihood of local communities and better contributed to the protection and conservation of natural resources.
This is the statement of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, on the occasion of leading more than 100 government officials and leaders of the Ministry of Information to visit Kep National Park, Kep Province on the morning of June 18, 2024.
On this occasion, Minister Net Pheaktra, together with National Park officials and officials of Kep Provincial Department of Environment, led by officials of the Ministry of Information, planted peacock trees on the streets of Kep National Park to make it more beautiful and attractive. Tourists come to visit.
Minister Neth Pheaktra informed that Kep National Park is the only national park in Cambodia, located in the center of the city, the beauty of Kep National Park is covered with greenery in all seasons and has been attracting pedestrians to enjoy the scenery and forest. Other wildlife.
Kep is one of the most attractive coastal cities in Cambodia due to its beautiful beaches and lush national parks and tranquil atmosphere, making it a great destination for nature lovers and tranquil seekers.
With a view tower built by the Ministry of Environment for Kep Province, it provides national and international tourists with the opportunity to see Kep from the top of the mountain, which is full of beautiful scenery: the sea and the beaches, the archipelago and the wooden sea of Kep. .
According to Minister Neth Pheaktra, the 12-meter tower was built at the expense of the sale of carbon credits as part of the protection and conservation of natural resources and the promotion of eco-tourism.
This observation tower is an additional means of entertainment for tourists visiting Kep National Park, in addition to the natural beauty, wildlife and mountain ring road that can walk and exercise for the general public. In Kep National Park, there is also a fun roller coaster ride.
Through this, Minister Net Pheaktra called on national and international tourists to visit Kep National Park and see the scenery of Kep province from the tower.
The Kep Provincial Administration has been developing several other major tourist sites, along with the construction of infrastructure to access the area to make it easier for visitors to visit.
It should be reminded that the 6,000-meter-long concrete road around Kep National Park, named "Bopha Prasidh Blvd" in Kep City, Kep Province, was inaugurated on May 4, 2022.
