Saudi Arabia allows Thailand to import live goats and sheep
BANGKOK: Saudi Arabia has given the green light for the import of live cattle, sheep and goats from Thailand, the Thai Minister of Commerce said last weekend. According to the Bangkok Post.
He said the animals could be imported from Thailand and then stored and slaughtered in Saudi Arabia.
The Bangkok Post reports that importers and exporters can apply for a permit for the animal trade on the Saudi Ministry of Environment, Water and Agriculture's Naama service website.
Mr Phumtham said the Saudi Food and Drug Administration had previously allowed Thai chicken exporters to export fresh chicken, processed chicken and cooked chicken to Saudi Arabia through all checkpoints there.
Last year, the value of trade between Thailand and Saudi Arabia was $ 8.79 billion, of which Thailand's imports from Saudi Arabia were worth $ 6.13 billion.
In the first four months of this year, trade value was $ 2.59 billion, down 17% from the same period last year, including Thai imports from Saudi Arabia worth $ 1.66 billion, down 28 percent. %. Thai exports to Saudi Arabia during the same period were estimated at $ 926 million, up 12 percent. According to the Bangkok Post.
