(Siem Reap): Dr. Prak Sophoan Neary, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, stated that breast milk is a perfect milk and rich in all nutrients for babies, exclusive breastfeeding. From birth to 6 months, help your baby get enough nutrition to reduce the risk of various diseases.
Dr. Prak Sophoan Neary said this recently on the occasion of Plan International Cambodia leading more than 10 journalists to study health and hygiene in Siem Reap.
Dr. Prak Sophoan Neary said: "Breast milk is a perfect milk and rich in all nutrients, and do not worry about the lack of hygiene and other risks. "No, breast milk, clean, safe and quality will be enough to meet the needs of the baby."
Exclusive breastfeeding from birth to 6 months not only benefits the baby, the mother also benefits, such as helping the mother to be healthy, can reduce the risk of breast cancer and Cervical cancer.
Dr. Prak Sophoan Neary claims that breastfeeding will help babies to be healthier, grow smarter, have better memory and be more mature than babies who are not breastfed. It helps reduce various diseases, especially malnutrition, which is also a point of concern.
