(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Public Works, expressed his shock at the shooting incident that left two people dead in Niroth Sangkat, Chbar Ampov District, Phnom Penh.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many described as follows:
"I was shocked to receive the news of a horrific incident that left two people dead, Lee Song and his fiancé. I would like to share this sad grief with the families of your two corpses.
I am deeply saddened by the most fragile loss of life, from conflict to violence to the worst crime. We really do not want this to happen and strongly condemn such atrocities.
I would like to commend and thank the competent forces for their efforts to arrest the perpetrators and bring them to justice.
We should have mutual understanding and tolerance as a Buddhist society that adheres to morality and chastity. Finally, I would like to call on all of you to join in promoting a culture of peace, tolerance, understanding and high tolerance for Cambodian society to be harmonious and happy.
Please be reminded that this shooting incident happened at more than 3 pm on June 17, 2024 at the victim's house in Borey Peng Huoth, Boeung Snor. The incident left two people dead and one seriously injured.
