The KCNA news agency reported that Putin "will pay a state visit to North Korea" at the invitation of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un.
The visit is part of a major tour that will include a holiday in Vietnam from Wednesday to Thursday. And it will be Putin's first visit to North Korea since July 2000, when he met with Kim Jong-il, the father of the current leader.
The visit underscored the deepening military cooperation between North Korea and Russia, especially amid suspicions that North Korea was providing Russia with weapons for the war in Ukraine in exchange for aid. Food and potential modern weapon technology.
