Accompanying the President are Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as well as key ministers of the Royal Government and representatives from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
During the visit, the President will also pay a separate courtesy call on the President of the Republic of Singapore, Mr. Thamenshan Mugarat Nam, and the Senior Minister of the Republic of Singapore, Mr. Lee Hsien Loong.
(Kampot): Addressing the people in the forum for resolving disputes outside the court system at the public hall of Kampot Provincial Hall on June 17, 2024, Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, said that resolving disputes if we only want Winning and losing are never the end, open your heart to accept the end.
Mr. Mao Thunin continued that if all of us who have conflicts and only want to win or lose, regardless of right or wrong, the resolution of this dispute will not be successful, which will prolong the time and pass. Reaching out to the judiciary is a waste of time and money.
The provincial governor also asked all the people in Kampot province who have conflicts or disputes with each other to be open-minded and tolerant of each other if the people take their things, because if we take their things It hurts, and if they take ours, we suffer the same, we are the same Khmer, survive after the second birthday, the day after the liberation on January 7, 1979, the same, so we must know how to love and understand each other.
The Provincial Governor emphasized that under the wise leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech has always taken into account the well-being of the people at all localities, regardless of political affiliation, race, color, especially Samdech always put Issue various policies and strategies to help people in need.
At the same time, Samdech also established and organized the process of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the judiciary in order to jointly resolve the disputes of all citizens at the local level to avoid filing a complaint to the court, which causes people to lose time because of the case. There are many things in court, especially the loss of financial resources.
It should be noted that Kampot Province, under the leadership of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, for more than 2 years, the Provincial Governor has resolved nearly 3,000 disputes out of court, with the Governor visiting the municipality. The nine districts in the province work directly with the participation of the authorities, elders, relevant departments, and the solution must be applauded and supported by the people throughout the province.
