President of the Constitutional Council: Traditional and Modern Constitutional Values at the Core of the Cambodian Constitution
(Phnom Penh): Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, stated that the values of the traditional constitution and modern values are the core of the Cambodian Constitution, which is a special point, while the constitutions of other countries in the world do not exist.
During the ceremony, Dr. M. Chhun Lim summed up the evaluation of the implementation of the Constitution over the past 30 years, focusing on modern values and Khmer values contained in the 1993 Constitution. These two are the main foundations that have led the Kingdom of Cambodia to peace until now.
Dr. M. Chhun Lim stated that the 1993 Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia is the sixth constitution since Cambodia adopted a Western-style system of governing the country, announcing the first modern constitution in 1947. The fundamental values of constitutionalism include: (1) democracy, (2) human rights, (3) the separation of powers, and (4) the rule of law, which has been integrated into Cambodian society ever since.
According to the President of the Constitutional Council, the 1993 Constitution also inscribed the values of Cambodian society in relation to the historical, cultural, traditional and religious factors of Cambodia. Thus, the 1993 Constitution is a pluralistic constitution that mixes the modern values with the traditional values of Cambodian society itself, inseparable from the historical factors and traditions of Cambodia's long past.
Dr. M. Chhun Lim also stated that in order to bring together the spirit of constitutionalism, the Constitutional Monument has been built in accordance with the values of the Constitution and will be completed and inaugurated under the supreme presidency of the King. The Kingdom of Cambodia on September 24, 2024, as expected.
At the end of the ceremony, the President of the Constitutional Council also stated that through his past duties, the Constitutional Council is very proud of the results of this work, which is a joint effort, especially the belief in The potential of human resources and the experience of the officers of the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council, both old and new, to achieve new goals.
Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor: The 7th National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training was organized with fruitful results beyond expectations
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kata On, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, on June 17, 2024, said that the 7th National Technical and Vocational Education and Training Day 2024 under the theme "TVET Learn To finish the job "was successfully organized and achieved more fruit than expected, with more than 60,000 people participating in two days.
The Secretary of State added that this National Day is organized to promote the quality, value and reputation of technical and vocational education and training by promoting and encouraging students, youth, parents, guardians, workers, employers and the private sector as well as the public. Actively participate in the development of a skilled workforce to meet the needs of the current domestic and foreign labor market.
He appealed to all workers, youth and the public who have not yet come to enroll in technical skills to take the time to enroll in technical and vocational skills to ensure that a young person has a clear skill in life. In that, the guardians of the youth must encourage their children to register for vocational training for everyone.
The Secretary of State encourages the private sector to continue to accept professional graduates, to provide appropriate salaries according to the ability of the trainees, including the public, authorities at all levels, to participate in the promotion and mobilization of young people. Learn more technical and professional skills.
