Mr. M. Chhun Lim: 70% of the Constitutional Monument is completed and is scheduled to be inaugurated on the day of promulgation of the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, stated that 70% of the Constitutional Palace has been completed and is scheduled to be inaugurated on the day of the promulgation of the Constitution on September 24, 2024.
Mr. M. Chhun Lim said this on the occasion of presiding over the 26th birthday celebration on the morning of June 17, 2024 with the participation and participation of members of the Constitutional Council, leaders and officials of the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council. Class order.
According to the President of the Constitutional Council, the construction of the Constitutional Palace has been completed according to the plan, that is, in about three months, the Constitutional Palace will be completed.
Please be informed that on June 12, 2023, at the park west of the Independence Monument, the Constitutional Council held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Constitutional Monument under the presidency of Dr. M. Chhun Lim, former representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, spokesman for the Constitutional Council, said that the construction of the Constitution Palace would take 12 to 15 months. Dr. Ly Raksmey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, was selected as the Architect.
