So far, there are some species of wild animals such as wild cows and rhinos, which naturalists have not yet dared to confirm their continued existence. Currently, zoologists use a number of methods, such as interviewing people who have experience living in forest and wildlife areas, using transgender methods, and installing automatic cameras.
* Mammal species naming in Khmer
This problem is caused by two factors:
The understanding and use of existing animal names often focuses on large species and some of the most frequently encountered species, making it possible for people to name or refer to one another. A large number of species in this book of mammals have been named by a group of Khmer zoologists to complement the Khmer naming conventions of all species found to be present in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
