Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Prey Veng Province Celebrates the 88th Birthday of Her Majesty the Queen Mother of the Cambodian Red Cross
(Prey Veng): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Prey Veng Province on June 17, 2024 celebrated the 88th birthday of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, the Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The ceremony included blessings of the Preah Ratanatray, worship of the Preah Ratanatray, almsgiving, and the offering of relics to nine monks from five pagodas in Prey Veng to bless Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia. Dignity and Happiness The Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross is the highest shrine on the 88th anniversary of his death on June 18.
The ceremony was held at the branch office of the Cambodian Red Cross in Prey Veng province, presided over by Mr. Suon Somalin, Chairman of the Prey Veng Provincial Branch Committee, with the invitation and participation of the Khmer Rouge, Prey Veng Municipality and Honorary Vice President of the provincial branch and stakeholders. A total of 210 people.
