According to Eng Hee, Kong Satharin is an officer under the hierarchy of the army. Ms. Tith Tara, the wife of Mr. Kong Satharin, filed a complaint with the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie Command against Phum Thiep, a 41-year-old male, and her accomplices for using violence against a real estate occupant in Phnom Penh last year. The beginning of June 2024 is a right as a citizen.
As for the implementation of the procedures of the judicial police officers of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie in accordance with the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
The Brigadier General stated that the right to protest in this case is as follows:
First, Phum Thieb has the right to protest at all stages of a criminal case, to present evidence in the presence of a judicial police officer or a representative of the prosecution, or to appeal to the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal or the investigating judge and to protest at all levels of the tribunal.
Second, the Gendarmerie, upon receipt of the complaint, must immediately proceed with the procedure under the coordination of the Prosecutor of the Court of First Instance. In the event that a judicial police officer misbehaves or misbehaves, the prosecutor may transfer the case to another judicial police officer.
Third, Article 3 of the Code of Criminal Procedure states that "Prosecution applies to all persons, both physical and legal, without regard to race, color, sex, language, creed, religion, national origin, social status, resources or status." Two killed, several injured in Texas shooting
