This twin flyover is the first flyover to be built during the 7th term of the National Assembly of the National Assembly under the leadership of the Prime Minister.
The project will build twin flyovers as a one-way street, with the first bridge along Samdech Techo Hun Sen Boulevard crossing National Road 2 towards Techo International Airport and the second bridge from Techo International Airport crossing. National Road No. 2 along Samdech Techo Hun Sen Blvd.
In addition to the construction of the bridge and the road connecting the bridge, the twin flyover project also has a number of infrastructure to be installed in the project, including the installation of street lighting poles, traffic signs, traffic signs, Drainage network on both sides of the road, improvement of sidewalks in the construction site, planting of trees and flowers and design of a green garden with a distance of 9 meters between the first bridge and the second bridge.
It should be noted that in order to solve the problem of traffic congestion that occurs incessantly from year to year, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already built flyovers at many intersections in Phnom Penh.
In addition to the flyover as mentioned above, there is also a flyover under construction. The flyover under construction is the "Techo Heritage" flyover. "Morakot Techo" flyover is a bridge at the intersection of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Blvd. and Monivong Blvd. and Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Blvd., called Street 271.
On April 1, 2024, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration temporarily opened this flyover on the second floor, the first phase, connecting traffic between Samdech Techo Hun Sen Blvd. and Monivong Blvd. in Meanchey District and Khan Chamkarmon in Phnom Penh. Do not violate the speed limit! 1 killed, 3 injured in road accidents nationwide on June 16
