The following is a message of thanks to the King: Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun: Direct flights between Cambodia and India are a major force in boosting tourism and trade between the two countries.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Civil Aviation Security, said that the inauguration of the first direct flight between Cambodia and the Republic of India and the first 2024 Tourism-India event is An important driving force in boosting tourism and trade between the two countries.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun made the remarks on the afternoon of June 16, 2024, presiding over the inauguration of the first direct flight between Cambodia and India (Phnom Penh and New Delhi). . The ceremony was held at Phnom Penh International Airport.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun said, "The historic launch of the first direct flight on direct flights between Cambodia and India and the first 2024 Cambodia-India tourism event on this occasion are a strength. "An important driver in helping to boost tourism and trade between our two countries."
According to Dr. Neth Savoeun, trade between Cambodia and India has grown significantly in recent years after the global Kovid-19 crisis.
He said that Cambodia's exports to the Indian market will reach more than 300 million US dollars by 2023, an increase of about 50% compared to 2022, and the bilateral trade volume has reached nearly 485.7 million US dollars. This is an increase of about 10.4 percent in 2023 to about $ 440 million in 2022, making India the 17th largest trading partner for Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun expressed strong optimism that the people of Cambodia and India will benefit greatly from this flight and hoped that the first flight, which will be launched soon, would be a symbol of success. Fruitful of closer ties and cooperation in all fields of our two countries.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun requested the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation to continue to cooperate with relevant institutions at all levels to establish new direct flights from all regions to the Kingdom of Cambodia to continue to implement the open skies policy of the Head of Government. Cambodia. Minister Mao Havanal: This year, Cambodia has 31 domestic and foreign airlines re-connecting flights from 8 ASEAN countries
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, confirmed that in 2024, Cambodia has 31 domestic and foreign airlines that are reconnecting flights from eight ASEAN countries.
"In 2024, we have 31 domestic and foreign airlines resuming flights from eight ASEAN countries, China, South Korea, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Qatar and the United Arab Emirates," said Dr. Mao. And from the beginning of May 2024.
According to Dr. Mao Havanal, during the period from January to May 2024, Cambodia received more than 2.5 million air passengers, an increase of 22% compared to the same period. In 2023, there will be just over 2.1 million people.
From these figures, Dr. Mao Havnall highlighted that we can generally say that air transport activities in Cambodia have gradually recovered after the Kovid-19 crisis and are moving forward. Proud of.
Dr. Mao Havanal also said that June 16, 2024 is a new historical day for Cambodia, the Secretariat of Civil Aviation in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, the Embassy of India in Cambodia and the National Air Cambodia Angkor Air. Relevant private sectors are holding the inauguration of the first historic flight on direct flight connection between Cambodia and the Republic of India from today.
