The first direct flight between Cambodia and India has officially launched!
The event was held at Phnom Penh International Airport under the chairmanship of Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister, Chairman of the National Committee for Civil Aviation Security and High Representative of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to address the event.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation (SSCA) emphasized that the launch of this flight will significantly strengthen the social, cultural and economic ties between Cambodia and India.
As the only national carrier, Cambodia Angkor Air is leading the way in promoting tourism and socio-economic development through the launch of this new flight.
This connection will enable Indian tourists to visit more Angkor Wat temples and increase the popularity of tourists as well. In addition, this flight provides Cambodian patients with access to high quality and affordable treatment in India. In the future, there are also plans to expand the network with more flights to support economic activities and cultural exchanges.
During the Corruption-19 outbreak, Cambodia Angkor Air demonstrated its social responsibility by maintaining major domestic flights between Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville, ensuring continuity. Despite the low demand for flights, the company has maintained its motto, "Proud to provide services to the Kingdom of Cambodia."
The new flight is ready for success through a shared religious heritage, health care needs and historical ties between Cambodia and India.
This connection will not only boost tourism, but also deepen cultural and economic ties. With the rich history of both countries and mutual benefits, Cambodia Angkor Air is optimistic about the potential and positive impact of this new service.
For Phnom Penh-New Delhi flights, the company offers four flight options each week, with flights from Phnom Penh to New Delhi at 16:45 with a duration of 4 hours and 35 minutes. And from Phnom Penh to Phnom Penh at 20:50 at the same time, which will be launched at the end of October 2024.
In addition, Cambodia Angkor Air also has many domestic and international flights such as Phnom Penh-Siem Reap, Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville, Siem Reap-Sihanoukville, Phnom Penh-Hanoi, Phnom Penh-Ho Chi Minh, Phnom Penh-Da Nang, Phnom Penh-Da Nang and to major destinations. Many more.
