Wildlife Alliance donates 197,000 saplings to 1 million tree planting campaign
The Wildlife Alliance has planted 18 species of tropical forest seedlings at the Chi Phat Nursery in Koh Kong province, where the seedlings are now ready to be planted.
Out of 197,000 seedlings, the organization plans to donate 82,000 to the Ministry of Environment, 20,000 to the Koh Kong Provincial Department of Environment, 20,000 to the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment. To the Department of Environment of Kampong Speu Province and 20,000 trees to Veal Veng District Administration. The remaining 5,000 saplings will be stored for planting in the eel area along National Road 55.
Seedlings include Thnong, Kranhong, Beng, Neang, Nuon, Phteah, Koki, Chheuteal, among many others.
"I would like to officially announce that the campaign to plant at least one million trees a year starts today." This is a post on social media by Dr. Eang Sophalleth on October 10, 2023.
"This donation is in response to the 1 million tree planting campaign set up by the Ministry of Environment," said Dr. Sou Vanna Gonlet, Executive Director of the Wildlife Alliance. We hope that the donated saplings will help restore the cardamom rainforest landscape. ”
"We would like to thank HE Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Environment, for his strong support of afforestation and reforestation in Cambodia. "Reforestation initiatives will have a positive impact on the climate as well as contribute to raising the Royal Government's reputation on the international stage." Ms. Bandith added.
The first shipment of 13,730 seedlings took place on June 8, 2024 to Koh Kong province. These species include Thnong, Kranhong, Koh Beng, Phteak, Phnom, Trasek, Maphet, and Cheung Chev Moul.
Then, on June 10, 2024, 13,120 seedlings were delivered to Kampong Speu province. Those species include Thnong, Kranhong, Koh, Beng, Phteak and Neang Nuon. The remaining saplings will be distributed to designated locations during August 2024. Drug trafficking crackdown detains a Vietnamese man with more than 5 kilograms of drugs
