Institute of Electrical Sciences: Electrical skills are in high demand in the Cambodian labor market
(Phnom Penh): According to a representative of the Institute of Electrical Science, electricity skills are in great demand in the Cambodian job market, while the first five-year bachelor of electricity to work earns from $ 500 to $ 750 per month.
Mr. Chin Phim Sokha stated that the demand for electrical and engineering skills is due to the fact that Cambodia is in great demand and growth in the electric power sector, resulting in a shortage of highly skilled human resources.
Mr. Chin Phim Sokha claims that after graduating with an associate degree and a bachelor's degree, they will get more job opportunities and a salary of $ 500 to $ 750 per month.
Solina, a fifth-year student at the Institute of Electrical Sciences, said that the decision to study electricity was due to the need for a job market in Cambodia, which is in great demand for the development of many buildings and infrastructure. There is also high money.
She said that studying and learning this skill is able to study and work both men and women without any risk after training from teachers and professors who have this skill clearly.
Please note that the Institute of Electrical Sciences is a public higher education institution that provides training in electrical sciences for undergraduate, associate degree and special skills for electrical staff. The conditions that can be studied at the Institute of Electrical Sciences are through a selection exam.
