(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, led a team to inspect the Prek Po Irrigation System, which has the capacity to irrigate more than 8,000 hectares in Prek Po Commune, Srey Santhor District, on the afternoon of June 14, 2024. .
According to the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, Prek Po Irrigation System has 12 main canals and 46 secondary canals with a total length of 105.37 km, including 27.19 km of concrete canals and 78 canals. , 17 km, 195 small and large art buildings, as well as a modern pumping station equipped with 7 motors.
This irrigation system has the capacity to irrigate more than 8,000 hectares, stretching from Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province to Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province and parts of Pearang district, Prey Veng province. Utilizing water from the Mekong River, the Prek Po Irrigation System has a large-scale pumping station equipped with modern technology to pump water from the river, which has the potential to supply water in all areas, both dry season and rainy season.
