(Pursat): The Kampong Lvea bridge across the Pursat River connecting Samrong commune to Leach commune in Tanok village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, with a length of about 160 meters, is being rebuilt by the solidarity of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party and the people. Local people to serve the people in Leach commune, Samrong commune, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district and Talor commune, Talor Sen Chey district, the bridge is scheduled to be completed in August.
It should be informed that the Kompong Lvea bridge was flooded and completely destroyed on September 20, 2020 and was buried by Mr. Suy Sem, former Minister of Mines and Energy and former Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Pursat Province. The foundation stone of this bridge was rebuilt on March 27, 2022.
Currently, about 70 to 80 percent of the Kampong Lvea bridge has been completed. This bridge will facilitate the transportation of agricultural products and re-travel in part for the people in Phnom Kravanh and Talo Sen Chey districts.
