China, which claims almost complete control of the South China Sea, including those in dispute with the Philippines, Brunei, Malaysia, Taiwan and Vietnam, has issued a new law enforcement measure in 2021 that allows its coast guard. Use the armed forces against foreign ships or vessels that encroach on the waters that Beijing claims as its own.
"Our message to our fishermen is that they should not be intimidated," Philippine Armed Forces chief Romeo Brawner told reporters on Friday. And continue to fish normally in our exclusive economic zone. "Because we have the right to exploit the resources in the area, so our fishermen have no reason to be afraid."
Under China's new measures, which take effect on June 15, the Chinese Coast Guard has the right to detain violators for 60 days without trial.
