Russia rarely mentions the number of troops killed and wounded in the Ukrainian war, with Moscow saying in September 2022 that 5,937 troops had been killed on the battlefield. But Western analysts believe that hundreds of thousands of Russian soldiers have been killed and wounded. On the Ukrainian side, President Zelensky said in February 2024 that 31,000 Ukrainian troops had been killed in the protracted war for more than two years.
