(Siem Reap): On the afternoon of June 14, 2024, the Anti-Corruption Unit signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Angkor International Investment Corporation (Cambodia) to implement the Royal Government of Cambodia's deep reform policy.
In particular, the fight against corruption in both the public and private sectors aims to ensure efficiency, transparency, accountability in business and the provision of better public services in order to promote a favorable investment environment for fair competition and sustainable growth in Cambodia. .
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed by Honorary Minister Dr. Senior Minister Om Yentieng, Chairman of the Anti-Corruption Unit and Mr. LU WEI, President of Angkor International Investment Corporation (Cambodia), and was attended by a delegation of the Chinese Communist Party and Discipline Inspection Committee. Supervise the affairs of the Chinese state of Yunnan Province and the relevant departments and units around Siem Reap.
Senior Minister Om Yentieng said that today's signing of the MOU is the 106th Memorandum of Understanding between the Anti-Corruption Unit and the private sector, which aims to jointly prevent corruption and cover more than 1,000 companies. Members from chambers of commerce, private institutions, national and foreign public institutions.
