MOSCOW, June 14 (Xinhua) - Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Friday that Western plans to lend money to Ukraine using interest on frozen Russian assets abroad were stolen. And will not be forgiven. According to a release by Reuters.
"The approach that Western countries have taken to Moscow shows that any country could fall into the same trap of Western asset freezes," Putin said in a meeting with foreign ministry officials. .
At the same time, Putin stressed that "it has now become clear to all countries, companies and public funds that their assets and capital are not secure, both legally and economically ... anyone can become "Next to the seizure of property by the United States and the West."
Putin's remarks come a day after G7 leaders agreed on a plan to provide $ 50 billion in loans to Ukraine, using interest on Russian assets frozen after Moscow. Send tens of thousands of troops into Ukraine by 2022 in what it calls a special military operation.
