Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Chakrapong announces his full support for the historic project "Prek Chik Funan-Techo"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Chakrapong, Supreme Personal Adviser to the King, has announced his full support for the Funan Techo canal project, which will greatly benefit the society and the people of Cambodia.
Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Chakrapong stated, "I and my family would like to express our full support for the implementation of the Funan-Techo Canal Project, the first historic canal in Cambodia under the highest initiative of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King in the implementation of the Funan-Techo canal project to achieve in the future.
The Funan-Techo canal project, which connects the river between the river and the Cambodian sea, is 180 kilometers long, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, which will provide great benefits and wealth to Cambodia and its people. Cambodia, especially in the field of transportation, such as reducing transportation costs, reducing time, distance, road damage, traffic congestion, traffic accidents, reducing procedures for transporting goods from Cambodia to the sea.
The project also helps to establish commercial and special economic zones, as well as the development of new satellite ports, as well as to increase irrigation, agricultural development, aquaculture, tourism, flood relief during the rainy season, and increase fish production. Fresh water in canals and expansion of real estate and other investments. Five Gangsters Threaten to Take a Motorcycle in Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Major General Heng Vuthy, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, ordered a specialized force to search and arrest five gangsters from Phnom Penh and used knives and knives to threaten motorbikes in the area. Kampong Cham at midnight on June 14, 2024.
Immediately after the incident and receiving the complaint, Major General Heng Vuthy ordered the specialized force of the Criminal Police Plan and the specialized force of the Kampong Siem District Police Inspectorate in cooperation with the specialized force of the Criminal Police Department to launch a search operation to arrest the person. Five suspects and confiscated exhibits, including three motorcycles, two motorcycles as a means of crime and one motorcycle of the victim.
According to the confessions of the five gangsters, the group traveled from Phnom Penh to Kampong Cham province and used a machete and a machete and two motorcycles to chase the victims. The accident of threatening to take a motorbike at midnight on June 14, 2024, at a point on the road in O Chleung village, Koh Roka commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province.
The five suspects are currently being held at the Kampong Cham Provincial Police for questioning and case processing by order of Mr. Vong Bunvisoth, Prosecutor of the Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
