Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Analysis: EU action to impose tariffs on Chinese cars destroys the interests of both others and oneself
Why is the European side ignoring the opposition and insisting on cracking down on Chinese electric cars through tariff increases? Behind this is not only the complex competition of interests within Europe, but also the connection with the three mindsets of some people in Europe.
First, the mindset that wants to suppress China's development. In Europe, initiatives for cooperation between China and Europe are important voices, but also anti-China forces. These people do not want to see China's development and find ways to prevent the deepening of political mutual trust and pave the way for practical cooperation between China and Europe.
Second, a mindset that fears fair competition. Europe has long had a clear dominance in the field of gasoline-powered cars, but as China's new energy car industry develops rapidly, some Europeans fear that China will overtake them.
Third, the American mindset. Europe used to be a victim of US trade protectionism, but this time it has become a trigger for trade disputes. The main reason behind this is pressure from the United States. But the European side needs to keep calm and think about whether or not it should follow the US to put pressure on China by abandoning China-EU cooperation.
In fact, China and Europe have broad common interests in the new energy vehicle industry. The positive competition and cooperation of electric vehicles between China and Europe, it is conducive to enhancing the competitiveness of European industry and also in line with Europe's vision of seeking energy innovation and development. Reduce carbon as well.
