(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, June 14, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, inspected the construction site of the irrigation system for diversifying the Prek Tnaot River to prevent flooding in Phnom Penh and its geography. Next to Stung Prek Tnaot.
The construction sites inspected this morning include the Stung Touch site in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, the Choeung Ek site in Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, and the Prek Ho site in Takhmao city, Kandal province.
The Prime Minister said that in order to reduce the water level of Stung Prek Tnaot and avoid flooding Phnom Penh and the area adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot, the Royal Government has released a national budget of 400 million USD to build 10 irrigation systems with a total length of 260 km. M.
Samdech Thipadei said that through these irrigation systems, about 300,000 hectares were flooded. The irrigation system not only saves the flooded area, but also serves as a source of water for agriculture, people's daily use as a means of transportation and for tourism.
