The signing of the MoU took place on June 12, 2024. During the ceremony, Dr. Keo, a representative of the University of Specialties of Cambodia, spoke about the history of the university, originally called the "Institute of Specialties of Cambodia", which was established in 2002 and strengthened and expanded into a "specialized university". Of Cambodia ”in 2004.
The University has training from Associate Degree, Bachelor Degree, Master Degree and Doctoral Degree, has a total of 40,458 students / student and has already graduated 10 times. From 2003-2004 to the academic year 2021-2023, a total of 50,346 students (16,758 females) successfully graduated from Cambodian specialized universities.
At the same time, there are a total of 11,747 students studying at all levels and locations (5,788 females) and have actively contributed to the university in participating in various social activities, including the youth activities of S. Cambodian Youth Scouts and Cambodian Red Cross Youth Activities.
According to Dr., in order to strengthen entrepreneurship skills for students, the university always invites experts in the field of employment to give lectures, conferences, seminars to students regularly and also send students to internships to the actual work site. Specific applications.
