Borey Kamakor village chief Se Sony said the blast damaged more than 150 houses near the scene. Some houses were slightly damaged, some houses were severely damaged. Five houses next to the 3rd Military Command were almost completely damaged.
The blast damaged people's homes, roofs, ceilings, doors and windows. The houses of the people who were damaged were all military families who served in the 3rd Army Division.
To alleviate the hardships of the people whose houses were damaged, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, has come forward to repair the damaged houses. Samdech Hun Sen has appointed General Kheng Someth, Commander of the Siem Reap Techo Hun Sen Engineering Corps, to lead the renovation work.
By now, the damaged houses have been repaired. Ms. Chan Sokhom described that her house was badly damaged, including the roof, ceiling, doors and windows. When the damage was done, she was upset and worried about the cost of renovating the house.
But when she saw General Kheng Someth go down to the house and provide information, Samdech Maniphea Hun Manet helped to repair the house, which eased her worries. She expressed happiness when the house was renovated and did not spend money.
She considers the help of Samdech Thipdey to repair the house shows the Samdech Thipdey's concern for the well-being and hardships of the people.
Another resident, Keo Leng, also lost his home in the incident. Keo Leng's house suffered extensive damage, including roofs, ceilings, windows and doors. Now his house has been restored to its former glory.
Mr. Keo Leng also expressed his happiness and deep gratitude to Samdech Hun Sen for considering the difficulties of the people and helping to repair the houses for the people.
