(Banteay Meanchey): The Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, cracked down on drug trafficking and illegal use at a building in Palilei 2 Village, Poipet Sangkat. Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, arrested two suspects.
* First name: Thy Phat Ramana, alias Bass, 27 years old, Thai, Occupation: Casino worker, Temporary residence: Kbal Spean 1 village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province (Trafficking and consumption) Occupation: Casino staff, temporary residence: Kbal Spean 1 village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city (use).
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that prior to the crackdown on local forces, the Municipal Gendarmerie had received reports of drug trafficking and illegal use at a building in Palilei 2 Village, Poipet Sangkat. Poipet City. Immediately after receiving the information, he led the force down to the scene and arrested the two suspects along with the exhibits and brought them to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect confessed that he had actually bought and sold drugs and used them himself. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Force has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated. Proceedings from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court. Currently, the suspect and the exhibits have been sent by the Anti-Drug Bureau to the provincial court to follow the procedure.
