This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet inspecting the irrigation system to liberate and diversify the water of Stung Prek Tnaot River from flooding Phnom Penh and the area adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot this morning, June 14, 2024.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that "Stung Prek Tnaot is important not only to release water from Phnom Penh, but according to the report, the result is to save more than 300,000 hectares of flooded areas and affected fields. "Houses and affect the factory area."
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet also pointed out that if this place is not prepared for canals and water stations, there will be a lot of flooding.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet added that the irrigation system to liberate and diversify the Stung Prek Tnaot water will provide water for the rainy season for tens of thousands of hectares because there are 50 hectares that can be harvested.
In addition, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet also said that in the past, some canals and some small canals were not connected from Prek Tnaot, but now we are connected from the water station so we can get water for use.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet confirmed that Stung Prek Tnaot is very productive and also a place to connect more nature, because along the small river and some canals are planned to set up tourist attractions and most tourist places connect nature with children .
According to Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet, the irrigation system to liberate and diversify the Prek Prek Tnaot River from flooding Phnom Penh has a total length of 260 kilometers with a budget of 400 million US dollars.
Please note that in recent years, the geography of Phnom Penh, especially the territory of Khan Danghor and some other areas in Kandal, Kampong Speu, adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot has been severely flooded.
Floods due to runoff from the Oral Mountains, Cardamom Mountains and rainfall in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu are shrinking due to the growth of residential and commercial areas.
In order to solve the flood, which is a serious challenge for the people and other economic activities, His Excellency Hun Manet decided to release a budget of about 400 million US dollars to build irrigation systems to liberate and divert the floods. Mr. Say Ean donated 500,000 Riel to support the "10,000 Riel 10,000" campaign of 2024 of Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia
