Samdech Hun Sen Manet: The 260-kilometer-long Phnom Prek Tnaot Water Relief System to Avoid Flooding Using $ 400 Million (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Diversion of Stung Prek Tnaot, which falls from the Oral Mountains to prevent flooding in Phnom Penh and the area adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot, is more than 260 kilometers long, with a budget of $ 400 million.
This morning, June 14, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathipadei Hun Manet said this on the occasion of Samdech's visit to inspect the irrigation system to liberate and diversify the water of Stung Prek Tnaot so as not to flood Phnom Penh and the area adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot.
"At the beginning of this mandate, I have decided to launch a major project with a budget of over $ 400 million, which is larger than the road infrastructure project due to the need, we have implemented this project," he said. "In the last six months we have been very successful. In the last six months we have been very fast."
Samdech Hun Manet added that the project to build a drainage canal is aimed at solving the problem in Phnom Penh, which is to adjust the drainage system to put more sewers, but a large part is outside Phnom Penh to avoid the river. Prek Tnaot, which falls from the Oral Mountains, where we passed 10 canals of more than 260 km, which is 80 km longer than the Funan Techo canal.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet also stated that this canal is very important to avoid water from Phnom Penh and help save the flooded area of more than 300,000 hectares, both the impact on farms, affect people's houses and affect factory areas. The canal is also intended to be an irrigation system that guarantees water for the rainy season for irrigating tens of thousands of hectares of crops.
Please note that in recent years, the geography of Phnom Penh, especially the territory of Khan Danghor and some other areas in Kandal, Kampong Speu, adjacent to Stung Prek Tnaot has been severely flooded. Flooding due to runoff from the Oral Mountains, Cardamom Mountains and rainfall in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu is shrinking due to the growth of residential and commercial areas.
In order to solve the flood, which is a serious challenge for the people and other economic activities, His Majesty the King Hun Manet decided to release the budget to build irrigation system, liberate and divert the flood.
Nine major projects are currently underway to address the floods, including:
1: Stung Toch project is a project to divert a large amount of water from Stung Prek Tnaot to Tonle Bati, with a length of 51 km and a width of 100 meters, including the back. The project consists of the construction of a small dam in Samrong Tong district in Kampong Speu province, which is 8 meters high and 51 meters wide, and has five sluices, each 8.5 meters wide and 7.5 meters high.
2: Stung Krom Bati project is a project to divert some water from Tonle Bati to Boeung Cheung Long near the new airport with a length of about 7 km and a width of 100 meters, including the back on both sides.
5: Prek Kong This project has the function of relieving tears below the new airport, bringing water from Canal 96 around Saang Phnom, Saang area, Koh Khel area, flowing into Prek Ambel and to Vietnam, with a total length of 20 km and a width of 100 Meters, including the back on both sides. The project receives water from Canal 96 and the surrounding area up to Prek Ambel and into the sea, and connects the communication network through its backs.
6: Prek Peam Satha This project consists of Prek Peam Satha and Boeung Ta Mok canal, two lines that carry water from Boeung Ta Mok to Tonle Sap at Peam Satha bridge in Ponhea Leu district with a total length of 18.7 km and a width of 100 meters, including the back. Well. The project collects water from the Borey along Samrong Boulevard and connects the transportation network through both sides.
7: Roleang Chrey-Slaku Canal This project diverts part of the water from Stung Prek Tnaot in order to reduce the flooding of Phnom Penh, the area flooded by the canal. In particular, save National Road 3 to Stung Slaku and can irrigate about 7,500 hectares and can supply water to produce safe water for use and connect the transportation network in the project area through the back.
8: Canals 59 and 90 This project has the function of releasing water from the upper part of the new airport and partially releasing water from National Road 2 with a total length of 18.8 km and a width of 32 meters to 40 meters, including the back of the canal on both sides .
