Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Sends Thai Man to Court Over Illegal Transit, Drug Trafficking
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie on June 14, 2024, sent a Thai national to court in connection with a case of illegal border crossing, drug trafficking and use.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that before the crackdown, the Municipal Gendarmerie patrolled along the Cambodian-Thai border until the Ta Prohm factory found a black backpack stolen. Illegal crossing from Thailand to Cambodia.
The force immediately arrested and searched the body and found 3 large packages of gram powder (ketamine) and 2 small bags weighing 3156.40 grams (in a black backpack). The force then immediately detained the suspect and confiscated the evidence and brought it to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for processing.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect confessed that he had illegally crossed the border and was transporting, trafficking and using illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has built a case and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
