More than 4 tons of drugs to be destroyed, market value more than 66 million dollars, origin from the Golden Triangle (Phnom Penh): More than 4 tons of pure drugs that were cracked down in the past by the committee decided to burn This morning, June 14, 2024. The burning took place at a brick kiln in Sangkat Samrong Khang Tbong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
The cremation ceremony was presided over by General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Among them were Mr. Nguon Nara, President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Lt. Gen. Bun Pa Marilux, Deputy Commissioner for Planning, and Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Anti-Drug Department. General Commission of National Police.
According to the report, 54 cases of drugs have been incinerated so far, including a final verdict and a pre-trial decision. A total of 4 tons, 100 kilograms, 108.76 grams are currently being prepared for incineration, and the next stage is the destruction by 3 tons of 254 kilograms of chemical compounds, which are non-destructive acids by incineration. Yes, by waiting for neutralization.
General Meas Virith, secretary-general of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that the more than four tonnes of drugs that have been burned so far are worth about $ 22 million, which is the market value. In terms of distribution value to consumers, about $ 66 million.
According to General Meas Virith, about 85 percent of the drugs that Cambodian police have cracked down on in the past have originated in the Golden Triangle, while Cambodia is just a transit area. He said that the perpetrators who were cracked down on in previous operations were part of a group of well-organized criminals, and this crackdown was like cutting off parts of a group of criminals.
He added that over the past 160 days, both the National Police and the Royal Gendarmerie have launched joint operations to crack down on more than 4,000 drug offenses, arresting about 10,000 people, including civilians. Cambodians and foreigners, and most foreigners are Vietnamese and Chinese.
At the same time, the Secretary-General emphasized that Cambodia will also organize the International Day Against Drug Abuse under the theme "Joint Investment in Prevention, Prevention and Promotion of Education for a Drug-Free Community" under the chairmanship of Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Director General. Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs on June 22, 2024.
General Meas Virith claims that the burning of drugs and the celebration of the International Day Against Drug Abuse today is like sending a message and warning about the devastating effects of drug trafficking around the world. He will be in Cambodia.
