7 dead and 1 seriously injured in traffic accident, 2 trucks collided head-on on National Road 71C, Tbong Khmum District
(Tbong Khmum): On June 14, 2024, at 4:30 AM, on National Road No. 71C at Andong Khouch point in Preah Ang village, Rokap Pram commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province, there was a traffic accident between heavy vehicles. Two heavy vehicles collided head-on, killing seven people and seriously injuring one.
According to the police, a white Hyundai car driven by Chheang Heang, 18 years old, living in Samrong village, Tamring commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province, collided with a silver Hyundai car, the driver's name and address were unknown. Immediately the scene.
According to the measurement from Tbong Khmum district authorities, the two vehicles driving in opposite directions arrived at the scene and collided head-on, leaving five people dead at the scene and three seriously injured. Two more died at the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital, leaving a total of seven dead and one seriously injured.
