There are three irrigation systems that liberate the Stung Prek Tnaot River, which will be inspected by Samdech Hun Sen this morning, including:
Stung Toch Project: This project consists of the construction of Stung Toch Reservoir in Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, which is 8 meters high, 51 meters wide and has 5 sluice gates, each 8.5 meters wide and high. 7.5 meters of small river drainage sub-project.
The project includes the rehabilitation of a 51-kilometer-long small river, 100 meters in size, including the back of the dam on both sides and 40 meters below, and the construction of a total of 68 art sites, including 54 sewers of all kinds, repairing 13 bridges and constructing a sluice. Place.
The small river system has the potential to divert water from Stung Prek Tnaot in Kampong Speu province at about 300 cubic meters per second to Tonle Bati and fall to Tonle Bassac. So far, the work progress has reached about 70%.
In one station, there are 6 motors, 1 meter in diameter, which can pump 15 to 20 cubic meters of water per second. This canal system can drain water from one part of Kambol district, one part of Dangkor district and some part of Meanchey district.
In order to solve the flood, which is a serious challenge for the people and other economic activities, His Excellency Hun Manet decided to release a budget of about 300 million US dollars to build irrigation systems to liberate and prevent the flood.
9: O Khsach is a project to connect the northern Chrey River to Ta Mok Lake through O Khsach to divert part of the water from Stung Prek Tnaot to solve the goal of reducing flooding in Phnom Penh along National Road 4 and floodplain. Rain parallel to the canal. In particular, this project connects the communication network in the project area through both sides.
