General knowledge: The power of the three rivers in mainland Southeast Asia
(Phnom Penh): Inland Asia, there are many long river networks, including the Mekong River, the Issaravati River, the Salween River, the Jindwin River, the Red River, and the Chao Ponhea River. In this article, we would like to mention the power of the three main rivers, the Mekong River, the Red River and the Chao Ponhea River, because these three river valleys suffer from the season of flowing water together.
The Red River Delta used to be covered with low clouds, heavy rainfall and cold weather. Currently, the western Annam Mountains receive less rainfall, and during the long dry season, the lowlands west of the Mekong River receive heavy snowfall, cloudy skies and cold at night and hot during the day. The highlands are less affected and have experienced shorter summers.
Source: Royal Academy of Cambodia's first book of mainland Southeast Asian culture
Analysis: China remains an indelible market for foreign investors
From January to May 2024, China's total car exports reached 2.4 million units, up 27 percent, according to data released by the China Passenger Car Market Information Association on May 11. Percentage compared to the same period last year. In particular, new energy vehicles will be exported to foreign countries, which will become an important driving force for boosting China's foreign trade.
According to the latest survey by the Chinese government, 81.6% of foreign trade enterprises estimated that exports in the first half of the year will be better or equal to last year, confirming the confidence of You also say that as China's economy continues to improve, favorable factors for China's foreign trade development will continue to grow, which will bring more dividends to the world.
Analysis: The establishment of the International Day for Dialogue between Civilizations is an age-old initiative that is the common aspiration of the people and a common trend of the international community.
Following the adoption of the UN General Assembly resolution, 14 countries participated in the core working group of the resolution, and 83 countries participated in the signing of the petition, which fully demonstrates that the Global Civilization Initiative adapts to the current. The era will be in line with the needs of the times, and more and more Chinese initiatives and Chinese plans are becoming international consensus.
Maher Ihsan, a Syrian political expert, noted that the UN General Assembly's adoption of a resolution establishing an International Day for Dialogue between Civilizations "reflects China's global civilization initiative." "It is bearing a lot of fruit relentlessly and has become a public product that serves the whole of humanity."
After all, although human civilization has progressed to the highest level in history, war has never been far away, regional conflicts are frequent, and global challenges such as terrorism and climate change occur one at a time. Faced with the common challenge, the only way out for mankind is to unite and overcome obstacles together.
On May 15, 2019, 47 Asian countries gathered in Beijing to hold the first Dialogue on Asian Civilization. Lay the foundation for some practical cooperation, such as operations to preserve Asian cultural heritage.
In March 2023, through dialogue and negotiation, Saudi Arabia and Iran ended more than a decade of political opposition and reached a "century-long reconciliation" that established a "Saudi-Iran formula" that could Provides experience for resolving other local issues.
These active activities add more stability and confidence to a world of extreme change and turmoil, enabling you to see the potential for peace through dialogue and development. The transition period between different civilizations.
In particular, China initiated the UN General Assembly to establish the International Day for Dialogue between Civilizations, to fully expand the important role of civil society dialogue in eliminating discrimination and bias, to increase understanding and confidence, and to promote connectivity. The hearts of the people will increase unity and cooperation, as well as complement the positive energy for human society, increase unity and respond to common challenges.
