(Kiev): The world is turning a blind eye to the preparations for a peace summit in Ukraine scheduled for June 15 and 16 this weekend in Switzerland. The upcoming Ukraine Peace Summit has rejected the invitation of Russia, the most important party in the ongoing conflict. So what are the benefits of the upcoming peace summit?
But the upcoming Ukraine peace summit has rejected the invitation of Russia, the most important party in the ongoing conflict. So what are the benefits of the upcoming peace summit? Zelensky traveled to countries in Europe, to countries in Southeast Asia, as well as countries in the Middle East.
*** How many countries will attend the Ukraine Peace Summit in Switzerland?
While some countries have refused to attend the Ukraine peace summit, Zelensky has accused China and Russia of trying to use diplomatic means to prevent some from participating in order to disrupt the summit process. This more. About 4,000 security personnel will be deployed at the summit in Switzerland.
*** Who will benefit from the peace summit in Ukraine in the absence of Russia
With Russia absent from the summit, peace talks are said to be unlikely, but the meeting is expected to benefit at least two major points for Ukraine.
The forthcoming meeting will focus on three of the 10 points of Ukraine's peace process: nuclear security, food security and the release of prisoners of war and the release of abducted Ukrainian children.
