Koh Thmor Document Center Distributes Wheelchairs and Earphones to People with Disabilities in Tbong Khmum and Kratie Provinces
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Long Dany, Director of Koh Thmor Documentation Center and a working group in cooperation with village authorities organized a program to distribute wheelchairs and earphones to four Khmer Rouge survivors with disabilities in Tbong Khmum and Kratie provinces. From 12-13 June 2024.
Yin San, a 87-year-old survivor of the Khmer Rouge regime, now lives in Satum village, Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. He said the wheelchair was very important to him and his family. He has been paralyzed since the war and has affected his family life because he could not go out to work like ordinary people, no one hired him. He has been paralyzed in his left leg and blind in both eyes for five years.
Mr. Yin San said that when he received the wheelchair, he could travel to visit relatives and friends in the village because he had not been anywhere for a while. As for his health, every day is not good, he has regular illness because his body is deteriorating and old. Because of the war and the Khmer Rouge era, it was difficult for him and he thought a lot every day.
He is very happy that DC-Cam has provided him with a wheelchair, which is both disabled and blind. He has nothing but thanks to the team and the Koh Thmor Documentation Center of the Documentation Center of Cambodia for bringing him a wheelchair.
Mr. Em Panh, 84 years old, living in Satum Village, Choam Kravien Commune, Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, expressed his happiness and satisfaction with the hearing aid because he could not hear for 6 years, but for the first 2 years he could hear Can't speak loudly.
Mr. Em Panh thanked the Documentation Center of Cambodia and all the team for giving him the earphones. Thank you for caring for the disabled and the elderly.
Mao Chin, 90, a resident of Khsem village, Khsum commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, said that he began to be deaf and trembling in 2020, five years ago. It is very difficult for him to live because when his children talk, he does not hear, it is difficult in his heart to sleep waiting for the day of death. Today, he is very happy that the Documentation Center of Cambodia team has given him an earphone.
