(Phnom Penh): Traders in the garment sector said that the situation of the garment, footwear and travel products in 2024 shows a good momentum, with exports reaching more than 5 billion US dollars, an increase of more than The next 20% of exports fell in 2023 due to the global crisis.
Tycoon Ly Khun Thai, President of the Federation of Cambodian Investors, told Fresh News that production, exports and orders for garments, footwear and travel products in 2024 have improved significantly. Exports of footwear and travel products in the first five months of 2024 increased by 25.33% compared to 2023, while garment exports increased by about 23%.
He pointed out that the good growth of the garment, footwear and travel products sector in 2024 is due to Cambodia's political stability and complete peace. And most importantly, there is the wise leadership of the Prime Minister, who has good leadership, confidence in investors and buyers.
"Orders have increased significantly in 2024," he added. The factories are happy. "With more orders compared to 2023."
Neak Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, also noted that the reason for the improvement of the garment sector in Cambodia is due to the new mandate, Cambodia has received investment from many factories, while Cambodia has a system. EBA preferential tariffs on exports to the European Union.
At the same time, as some countries in the region face political and economic crises, some factories from those countries come to Cambodia to produce and export.
