(Phnom Penh): Leaders of the Ministry of Labor, as well as TVET training schools and the private sector have reaffirmed that at present, factories, enterprises, investment companies are increasingly in need of technical and professional staff, making the job market more open. Therefore, young Cambodians should seize the opportunity to learn TVET skills for everyone to build their future.
This good point was mentioned in the press conference related to the organization of the 7th National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training on June 12, 2024 at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
In addition to the information related to the National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training, the public, private and TVET parties also called on parents, communities, stakeholders to encourage young people, students, especially vulnerable youth to turn to technical and vocational training. Profession, because it is a necessary bridge to find a job, is also to create your own business to improve your life.
As Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, Mr. Kata On called on young people to turn to Technical and Vocational Education (TVET) to meet the needs of the current labor market, as it is easier to find a job. Make a high income, especially at a time when the Royal Government is paying close attention.
He said that the technical and vocational training program for 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families is the best opportunity for young Cambodians to come and receive TVET training at schools near them. Most.
Mr. Hing Sideth, Government Representative in charge of Technical and Vocational Education and Training, said that the current job market for technical and vocational skills is very wide for skilled and high-income youth.
Mr. Say Rattanak, Representative of RMA, said that this technical and vocational training is very important for promoting local human resources to have real skills to be able to fill the job market. As Cambodia's skilled workers become more abundant, companies are encouraging the use of more local labor than foreign workers, in other words, better positions and higher salaries are always waiting for Cambodian professionals.
Not only RMA, other investment companies also need more skilled workers, skilled staff, while in Cambodia there are new investment companies open almost every day, which is an opportunity for young Cambodians to seize any professional job opportunities that they enjoy. , According to Mr. Say Rattanak.
The conference also called on young people to come and enroll in TVET through technical and vocational training programs for 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families, which is a very good program to provide. Opportunity for all young people to have the skills to work or create their own business and meet the needs of the skilled workforce for new investment in Cambodia.
