Ministry of Agriculture Spokesman: Formation of a modern agricultural community will automatically become an import barrier
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khim Finang, spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the establishment of a modern agricultural community of farmers will be an automatic import barrier that protects both growers and consumers and supporters of local products. Well.
This statement was made by the spokesman of the Ministry of Agriculture during his visit to the agricultural community in Tram Kak district, Takeo province on June 12, 2024.
Mr. Khim Finang observed the strong potential of Tram Kak community for leafy vegetables, which is already the foundation, only the integration of a modern agricultural community by stopping competition and turning to joint production and joint management to Supply of vegetables at a reasonable price, there will be a large-scale vegetable growing location in Takeo province that can compete with imported vegetables.
He said that initially, 42 vegetable growing families had volunteered to register together to form a modern farming community, and the team needed time to study in more detail, hoping to establish a large vegetable community. Here soon.
In addition, a spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture stated that vegetable farmers in Tram Kak, Takeo province, could have the potential to compete with imported vegetables if the modern agricultural community wanted to grow local vegetables instead of imported vegetables required Prepare in advance, otherwise it is no different from hurting our buyers like that, especially for those who are still poor.
