Cambodia, Korea vow to strengthen and expand tourism cooperation, especially with Jeju Autonomous Prefecture
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the Republic of Korea are committed to further strengthening and expanding tourism cooperation by promoting cultural and economic exchanges, building stronger people-to-people contacts and enhancing mutual trust. Better between the two countries, especially with the autonomous province of Jeju.
This commitment was made during a meeting between Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. OH YOUNG HUN, Governor of Jeju Autonomous Prefecture of the Republic of Korea, on June 12, 2024 to discuss potential opportunities for Cooperation in promoting tourism and developing tourism between the two countries by strengthening the flow of tourism to each other even more.
Minister Sok Soken and Governor of Jeju Province are committed to further strengthening and expanding tourism cooperation by promoting cultural and economic exchanges, building stronger people-to-people contacts and enhancing trust. Better exchanges between the two countries, especially with Jeju Island.
On that occasion, the Minister highlighted the factors of peace, stability and development in Cambodia today, in which the tourism sector is also highly focused on the rehabilitation and recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Minister highlighted the five pillars of the Five Strategies (BUILD) and the three priority work support projects (3Ds) to contribute to enhancing positive public-private partnerships as well as promoting Elevate the competitiveness, sustainability and environment of Cambodian tourism.
The governor of Jeju Province said that Jeju Island and Cambodia have many similarities, including history, natural resources and cultural heritage, which prompted the signing of a memorandum between Siem Reap and Phnom Penh with Jeju Island.
Minister Sok Soken and the provincial governor agreed to study the potential for boosting direct flights between Jeju Island and Siem Reap-Angkor.
