Five former Stung Treng CNRP leaders ask to join the CPP (Video inside) (Stung Treng): Five former Stung Treng CNRP leaders have asked to join the CPP after They saw that the CPP had the will, the conscience, the patriotism and the ability to lead the nation to prosperity and prosperity.
The leaders of the former Stung Treng Provincial CNRP who asked to join the political life with the CPP include: 1) Mr. Som Meng, Director of Stung Treng Provincial Executive Administration, 2) Mr. Phin Leak, Executive Member of Stung Treng Province, 3) Mr. Iv Leji, President Executive of Siem Pang District, Stung Treng Province, 4) Ms. Hak Rachana, Deputy Chief of Youth of Stung Treng Province and 5) Mr. Chheng Lok, Executive Vice President of Siem Bok District, Stung Treng Province.
These five individuals are sincere volunteers and active in serving the CNRP in Stung Treng province. After the party was dissolved by the judiciary in 2017, the five CNRP loyalists did not engage in political activities with other parties, although many new ones were formed.
But now they want to join the political life with the CPP because they see that the CPP is the only political party that has a clear policy to lead the nation to build a prosperous nation. In particular, the Cambodian People's Party is the support and trust of the people to ensure the maintenance of peace and social stability, which is a necessary condition for ensuring the happy life of the people.
The five former opposition loyalists have declared their allegiance to the CPP, not foolishly believing in the opposition, especially not being deceived by Sam Rainsy.
