How do young people benefit from participating in the National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training?
(Phnom Penh): Young people, students who are looking for a job or want to know market information or information from the field of technical and vocational training (TVET) should participate in the National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training in the middle of this month.
How do young students benefit from participating in this National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training?
In a press conference held on the morning of June 12, 2024, Mr. Kata On, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor, encouraged young people, students should participate in the upcoming 7th National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training. To interview for a job or find out about current and future market information, find out about technical and vocational training.
He added that young people, students as well as the public will receive more comprehensive information about education, technical and vocational education, information on scholarships in enterprises, especially technical and vocational education and training programs for young people from poor families. And 1.5 million people are at risk to match their own situation, how to choose, how to prepare, what skills.
In addition, young people, students, as well as the public will also receive information from the labor market that is in demand, because on the National Day, there are also exhibition booths of many companies, with colleagues waiting to receive applications, job tests, live competencies provide information. From the job requirements for the participants as well, so that the participants can have a face-to-face conversation with those companies.
This National TVET Day will also help promote and introduce priority sectors and professions that are in high demand in the market and in technical and vocational education and training institutions.
The Secretary of State said that as of June 10, 2024, ministries, institutions, technical and vocational education and training institutions and private companies have registered to participate in the exhibition of production chains and products, including 104 national sub-national units. 280 units.
Mr. Say Rattanak, Representative of RMA, said that every time the National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training is organized, RMA always participates, in which the company organizes large booths with company colleagues waiting to provide information related to job requirements. Training as well as job application and competency test in the booth.
Mr. Bun Phearin, Director of the Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) also confirmed the organization of the booth to provide information related to technical and vocational training to participants in the National Day of Technical and Vocational Education and Training. Is a leading school in training TVET skills for young people.
