(Phnom Penh): The leaders of the Cambodian Alumni Association from Vietnam on Wednesday afternoon, June 12, 2024, met and had a solidarity meal with Vietnamese alumni who graduated in Cambodia and came to work in Cambodia.
During the meeting that day, alumni of the two countries strongly believe that in the future they will be able to contribute to the promotion of friendly relations and solidarity between each other, as well as help to connect to find jobs for alumni. Of the two countries that have just graduated to have jobs to follow everyone's skills, especially Cambodian alumni from Vietnam.
Please be informed that every year, both countries regularly provide long-term and short-term training scholarships to students of both countries. Cambodia provides 35 scholarships per year to Vietnam, including 15 undergraduate and postgraduate scholarships and 20 two-year Khmer language and culture training scholarships per year.
Please be reminded that the Cambodian Alumni Association from Vietnam was officially registered with the Ministry of Interior according to Prakas No. 440, dated January 31, 2024. So far, the association has been in shape for more than four months and has more than 700 members.
The Cambodian Alumni Association from Vietnam was established with the aim of strengthening and expanding the bonds of friendship and solidarity to become closer and stronger, as well as mutual support between Cambodian alumni who have studied at Socialist Republic of Vietnam
