Cambodian, Australian Home Ministers Hold Meeting on Strengthening Bilateral Cooperation
(Melbourne): Bilateral cooperation between the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Immigration, Nationality and Cultural Affairs of Australia is further strengthened and enhanced.
On the morning of June 12, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Interior, Dr. Sar Sokha, led a high-level delegation to hold a bilateral meeting with Andrew Giles, Minister of Immigration, Nationality and Multicultural Affairs. At the Australian Parliament.
To begin with, Andrew Giles welcomed and thanked the Deputy Prime Minister for leading a high-level delegation from the Ministry of Interior to visit Australia on this occasion. The Minister expressed his confidence that this important visit will definitely bear fruit as planned, especially the exchange of ideas and experiences with the specialized units on immigration, crime, technology and police work.
In response, Dr. Sar Sokha thanked the Minister and the Australian side for facilitating the visit and warmly welcomed the Cambodian delegation. This is the third visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the second to the Swiss Confederation and the German Republic since he was appointed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
The head of the Ministry of Interior also stressed that the visit will provide additional experience to Cambodia on immigration, prevention and suppression of technological crime, human trafficking, security and sub-national administrative reform.
The Deputy Prime Minister also shared with the Australian side some important information related to immigration in Cambodia, including the work of revising the relevant laws and regulations to respond to the new context in Cambodia and also to facilitate the establishment of clear procedures and conditions. On immigration work, while the Australian side has more in-depth experience than Cambodia on this work.
At the same time, Dr. Sar Sokha also confirmed the cooperation with the Australian side on the work of repatriation of Cambodian citizens who do not have a legal basis to stay in Australia. In addition, Abhisit praised the successful results of the Cambodia-Australia Immigration Forum, which the Cambodian side organized in 2023 in Siem Reap under good cooperation with the Australian Government.
Andrew Giles, Minister of Immigration, Nationality and Multicultural Affairs, acknowledged Cambodia's efforts and agreed on the fight against immigration and other crimes, including technological crimes, to maintain security and order between the two countries and the region.
He also confirmed the acceptance of the request from the Cambodian side to train skills to fight technology crime, as well as examine the possibility of promoting cooperation in the field of the two ministries to deepen.
Remarkably, Mr. Andrew Giles confirmed his readiness to pay a working visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia at the appropriate time at the invitation of the Prelate and wished the Prelate and the delegation success in their visit. We hope that the delegation will meet, exchange and exchange good experiences with Australian professional institutions tomorrow and the following days.
