(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, on June 12, 2024, recommended three important principles for recruiting officials to work in 2025.
The issuance of this principle took place on the occasion of the second meeting of the National Committee to promote the implementation of key measures to reform public administration of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly. This is according to the press release of the meeting.
He said that in order to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of the recruitment of civil servants in 2025 to be more compassionate, transparent, fair, environmentally friendly and highly effective, a number of principles must be implemented:
* The number of officers to be selected should be as large as the number of retired officers in 2024 and only if necessary, which can be explained with reasonable and clear reasons,
* All functional analysis and requirements for the recruitment of new officers must be approved by the Ministry of Public Function,
* Encourage Ministries and Institutions to transfer the remaining funds from savings to reduce the framework to be used for incentives to officials and / and increase expenses in addition to staffing if necessary and with a reasonable and reasonable explanation.
The Prime Minister further stated that the implementation of the recruitment system must continue in accordance with the "recruitment to be used" approach.
The Prime Minister requested and encouraged all ministries, institutions and administrations of the capital and provinces to continue to work in a proactive manner and to strengthen better cooperation between each other under the "Livelihood" approach. Of a single character system. ”
