21 Baray District Councilors of the 4th Mandate Officially Announced
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Reasey, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, on the afternoon of June 12, 2024, officially announced the inauguration of 21 members of the 4th Mandate Baray District Council at Baray District Hall.
On that occasion, Mr. Nguon Reasey stated that the election of councils of all levels of administration at the sub-national level is a process for democratic development at the sub-national level, which aims to include:
First, to strengthen the process of multi-party liberal democracy to lay the foundation at the grassroots level.
Second, change the structure and management system of sub-national administrative administrations through decentralization and deconcentration policies by establishing a unified administration with autonomy, authority and appropriate resource functions transferred to sub-national administrations to provide public services. And local social services to meet the needs of the people.
Third, to promote people's participation and ownership in local development in order to reduce poverty and improve the quality of life of local people.
In that, the Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province introduced and provided some tips for the Baray District Council to use as a basis in implementing the following important tasks:
1. Pursuant to the provisions of Article 70 of the Law on the Administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans, the Council shall be required to hold its first ordinary meeting not later than 15 days after taking office.
2. After the first ordinary meeting, the Baray District Council shall hold its second ordinary meeting not earlier than 25 days or more than 35 days after the first ordinary meeting.
3. Based on the Anti-Corruption Law, all council members have an obligation to declare assets and liabilities.
