Unions Please note that the report presented by Central on Freedom of Association in Cambodia does not reflect the realities of the union situation in Cambodia. The employment sector in Cambodia has improved, the freedom of association has improved, and our workers have received better and more reasonable working conditions, both in terms of wages and other conditions. Minority opinion and no general conclusion.
Central's report is unacceptable and assesses the situation of unions in Cambodia as a whole. Please note that according to the current report of the Ministry, the number of local unions in Cambodia has increased from more than 3,000 in 2016 to more than 6,000 last year. 2024 With the doubling of trade unions in Cambodia in the short term, it is seen that Cambodia has full freedom of association without discrimination, in stark contrast to Central's report.
On the other hand, Central is a civil society organization registered with the Ministry of Interior, not a professional organization registered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. In contrast, civil society organizations (Central) have in the past carried out many activities in violation of the labor rights of professional organizations called trade unions registered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
