Therefore, it makes it difficult to study and protect them because it is not easy to understand the number trends on a scale of just a few years. In particular, when we have decades of data collection, it is easy and can show the trend of the number of animals, whether it is increasing or decreasing.
It is always encouraging to see the presence of dolphins, but there is nothing better when we are working with the conservation of this endangered species !!!
In general, animals can breed only if there is a suitable environment that allows their young to survive, and the mother dolphin is very self-sacrificing from birth to conception. Its body properly during pregnancy, then takes care of the baby from birth by breastfeeding, protecting the baby and teaching the baby until the baby is independent.
Dolphins will not want to add to the burden of foraging if they have difficulty finding food to survive. Therefore, the presence and absence of dolphins is the first indication of the health of their numbers, and by expanding the health of ecosystems, it can contribute to an increase in the number of predators such as dolphins.
