(Phnom Penh): Economic experts and social observers in Cambodia have seen that starting from steel friends, more Chinese investors are investing in business in Cambodia, while in May 2024, the latest investment From China ranks first, contributing nearly 50% of total investment.
Keo Piseth, a social observer and candidate for the Doctor of Political Science, said that Cambodia-China relations have reached a high level in all areas, such as politics, diplomacy, economy and trade. He stated that the reasons for Chinese investment in Cambodia are many factors:
First, Cambodia and China are steel friends and are always committed to promoting strategic partnership in all aspects. The friendship between the two countries is considered to be the best example in this new era.
Second, in Southeast Asia, countries all want investment from China, a dragon that has just woken up and has a population of billions. However, due to its favorable geographical location and economic expansion, Cambodia has been able to attract a lot of attention from China, which has influenced Cambodia's integration into the global supply chain.
In a recent interview with Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, HE Dr. Ky Sereyvath, an economist and president of the Chinese Studies Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that China and Cambodia are good economic and trade partners. The two sides have continued to step up their efforts to expand their influence, turn into steel allies and expand diamond-hexagonal cooperation for the greater good of the two peoples.
"If we talk about the relationship between the two countries, Cambodia has become a strategic partner in all aspects, has become a friend of steel and now a friend of another diamond hexagon, cooperating in six areas," he said. Thus, the economic cooperation of the two countries, first, in terms of Chinese investment in Cambodia, has created domestic production jobs, tourism has all helped boost Cambodia's economic growth.
