Ministry of Environment Spokesperson: Participating in protecting natural resources, proper waste disposal, reducing the use of chemical fertilizers and plastics have encouraged clean land, clean water and fresh air
(Pailin): Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, said that to participate in protecting natural resources, proper waste disposal and reducing the use of chemical fertilizers and plastics to promote clean soil, clean water and fresh air. Sustainable development ensures food security, poverty reduction and adaptation to climate change, and promotes sustainable growth.
This was stated by Mr. Khvay Atiya on the occasion of presiding over the National and World Environment Day on 5 June under the theme: "Improvement of soil quality, wilderness and drought resistance" on Tuesday, June 11. 2024 in Pailin City, Pailin Province.
On this occasion, Mr. Khvay Atiya encouraged the planting of trees to prevent erosion, topsoil quality, climate change mitigation, biodiversity conservation, cropping, reduction of pesticides and fertilizers, management and Proper use of water, strengthen management of natural resources, stop clearing forest land, use land that is not replanted with trees or crops, and leave agricultural land vacant.
Mr. Khvay Athiya once again encouraged environmental officials to cooperate with the Capital, Provincial Administration, Departments, Relevant Units, especially with the authorities of municipalities, districts, villages, communes, sangkats, as well as the general population, to make Cambodia, which is our home, clean and hygienic. Dignity, famous on the international stage.
