(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province and Chairman of Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, this morning, June 11, 2024, paid a courtesy call and brought donations from Provincial Red Cross Branch to distribute to the people. Affected by strong winds 146 families in Tonlong commune, Memot district recently.
The ceremony took place at Wat Sattavithy Chotyaram, also known as Wat Sla, in Pong Teuk village, Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan emphasized that please trust the Royal Government of Cambodia, that in times of trouble, only the Prime Minister's Cabinet, the provincial authorities, the Red Cross branch, which is close to visit to help you, unlike the extremist group. Some, as the election neared, only made faces and promised air.
Donations for the families of the severely affected received 40,000 Riels, the victims of the average victim 20,000 Riels, the victims of the victims received 50,000 Riels, and each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 can of fish sauce and 1 portable soy sauce.
With generosity, Dr. Cheam Chansophorn presented the suffix of the Chief Inspector of Wat Sattavithi Chotyaram, also known as Wat Sla, for the use and construction of achievements at this temple.
