Dr. Chea Samnang: Children with stunting are caused by a chronic malnutrition and difficult to treat
(Siem Reap): Dr. Chea Samnang, Vice Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and Co-Chair of the Sub-Working Group on Water, Sanitation and Nutrition, said that children with stunting are caused by a chronic malnutrition problem. It is difficult to get back to normal.
Dr. Chea Samnang confirmed this on June 10, 2024 on the occasion of Plan International Cambodia led more than 10 journalists to study health and hygiene in Siem Reap.
Dr. Chea Samnang stated, "Children with stunting are caused by a chronic malnutrition that makes it difficult for us to return to normal, so we need to protect ourselves." "Do not let children with emaciation become infected with stunting. If we prevent emaciation well, timely treatment will not progress to stunting."
Dr. Chea Samnang continued that malnutrition in all its forms does not include thin and stunted children, and even overweight children are considered malnourished, which has serious health consequences. Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, a woman with dehydration that causes a large belly up to 25 kg was successfully operated free of charge at Calmette Hospital
Unfortunately, the woman fell seriously ill due to a chronic illness and decided to come to Calmette Hospital for medical check-ups. Doctors required regular check-ups to determine the condition, but due to the lack of Due to the pain, the widow did not go to see the doctor by appointment, although the medical examination using the equity card was the responsibility of the Royal Government.
After receiving the news of the above hardships, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, contacted the authorities in Sen Sok district to investigate the above case and reached the same finding. Kittipritbandit also sent a representative to bring humanitarian donations to the patient's family, then Sen Sok district authorities sent the patient to Calmette Hospital for treatment.
Under the recommendation of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, also assigned a team of doctors at Calmette Hospital to receive patients and provide free treatment to the above poor women. Including the diet of the patient's family.
The patient arrived at Calmette Hospital on the afternoon of June 6, 2024, after being evaluated by a team of doctors and was referred to a gynecologist. On June 7, 2024, at 12:30, the patient was sent to the operating room. After 3 hours of surgery by the team of doctors is very successful.
