(Kampot): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, requested the council and district authorities to fulfill their role in ensuring the harmony and permanence of the local people.
This proposal was made by Mr. Tak Hab, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Governor of Kampot Province, Mao Thunin, presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the Angkor Chey and Banteay Meas District Councils of the fourth mandate on June 11, 2024.
The Governor of Kampot Province also stated that the role that the officials receive is a burden and the role that came now is due to the love and satisfaction through the votes of the people. Therefore, the newly appointed district councils as well as the district authorities must use this role properly to provide warmth and benefit to the local people who own the vote.
The provincial governor said that as servants of the people, we must not take the role assigned by the people to oppress, exploit or abuse the people, because those factors cause people to lose confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government.
The provincial governor also urged the newly appointed councils and local authorities at all levels at the local level to work closely together to serve the people with heartfelt satisfaction, especially to reach the backs of people's houses. In their locality to know their well-being and actual needs and to solve all issues, requests in a timely manner, with the welfare and interests of the people as a whole.
