(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, on June 11, 2024, at the Judicial Forum in Pursat Provincial Hall, allowed more than 60 fishing families to meet to discuss solutions. Request for mechanical trawling in Tonle Sap Lake in Kampong Luong commune, Krakor district, Pursat province during fishing closure.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida said that on behalf of the provincial administration and on behalf of the chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, he was very concerned about the lives of the people. As in the case of fishermen who apply for trawling with mechanical force during the closed season, it is not allowed, that is, for the common good.
The provincial governor said that if there were any law enforcement forces or professional officials who came to extort money from relatives, he would deal with them without exception. He asked you to accept the decision as well as the explanation from the professional officials about the fisheries law and to consider for the benefit of our descendants.
On that occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida also donated rice to more than 60 families, each family received 20 kg of rice.
Prey Veng Provincial Governor Provides New Uniforms to 172 CRC Youths from Two High Schools in Sithor Kandal District
(Prey Veng): Mr. Suon Somalin, Governor of Prey Veng Province and Chairman of the Provincial Branch Committee, on June 11, 2024, invited 172 Cambodian Red Cross youths from Hun Sen Prek Sandek High School and Prey Deum High School. That is in Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province.
The event was attended by Provincial Branch Committee Members, Branch Executives, District Sub-Committees, District Sub-Branch Officers, District Education Officers, High School Principals, Teachers and Youth of the New Cambodian Red Cross at the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, Sithor Kandal District. 210 people, 170 women.
At the same time, he urged to continue to strengthen and expand the Red Cross youth network among high school students to give them the opportunity to participate in humanitarian work on a regular basis. Please pay attention to help the students and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross who are living in poverty and are studying in schools and orphans as well as the people in their communities.
The provincial branch of the Cambodian Red Cross also donated 15,000 Riels to each youth from Hun Sen Prek Sandek High School and 10,000 Riels to Prey Deum Thnong High School.
Please note that as of June 11, 2024, the provincial branch has equipped the CRC youth uniforms in 4 high schools, a total of 379 youths in Pearang district 1 high school, Po Rieng district 1 high school, and Sithor Kandal district 2 high schools.
Deputy Governor of Siem Reap urges stakeholders to jointly prevent violence against women and girls in all forms
(Siem Reap): Ms. Mony Rings, Deputy Governor and Chair of the Working Group (GBV), urges all stakeholders to work together to prevent all forms of gender-based violence, including: domestic violence, sexual assault, and sexual harassment. Trafficking in women and children, especially in the 13 districts of the province must work together to increase work efficiency.
Ms. Mony Rings made the call in the first half-year meeting of 2024 Multidisciplinary Response Working Group on Gender-Based Violence to promote and expand multidisciplinary services in response to violence against women and children Effective and timely girl on June 11, 2024 at Siem Reap Provincial Hall.
The meeting also focused on promoting and strengthening the provision of multidisciplinary services to respond to violence against women and girls effectively and in a timely manner to the working groups and stakeholders who provide protection services to victims. To respond in a multi-sectoral manner to gender-based violence.
The meeting also reviewed the report on the results of activities in the first half of 2024 of the Multi-Sectoral Response Team (GBV) on gender-based violence at the provincial level, in good cooperation with institutions, relevant departments, competent authorities, local authorities. And partner organizations to facilitate the provision of timely response services to victims.
She said that the Multi-sectoral Response Team to Gender-Based Violence (GBV) at the provincial level has good cooperation with institutions, departments, relevant units, competent authorities, local authorities, GBV working groups at all 12 districts and relevant partner organizations. In coordinating the provision of timely response services to victims of gender-based violence.
According to the report, in the first half of 2024, the provincial GBV team intervened in 86 cases of gender-based violence against women and girls, including 26 cases of rape of minors; Sex with minors under the age of 15 08 cases, 1 case of sexual assault and 1 case related to child prostitution, 1 case of rape of minors and 1 case of child prostitution and 49 cases of domestic violence.
