During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol briefed the Secretary of State on Cambodia's positive potential, including political stability, macroeconomic stability, a young, energetic and dynamic Cambodian workforce, and a Royal Government that supports business, investment and investment. The favorable and interconnectedness of Cambodia's interdisciplinary infrastructure, which has been providing opportunities for investors to invest as well.
The Deputy Prime Minister expected that Cambodia and Spain could review the preparation of a bilateral investment treaty to facilitate investment and communication.
Ms. Amparo Lopez Senovilla welcomed the Deputy Prime Minister and the Cambodian delegation to visit Spain on this occasion and expressed interest that Spanish investors can invest in tourism, renewable energy, medicine, transport infrastructure, especially system infrastructure. Wastewater treatment and some other sectors in Cambodia as well.
