To know more, please watch the following discussion: Contrary to the claims of the newly registered Central Union, which claims that there is no discrimination and that the registration procedure is easy
(Phnom Penh): Local unions that have just been registered in 2024 claim that the union registration process is easy and non-discriminatory, contrary to the claims of Central that distort the fact that the union registration process is Lots of complexity on administrative forms.
The local unions' statement came after Central released a report on June 4, 2024, alleging that union registration was complicated, with administrative and judicial barriers making it difficult for unions. .
Mr. Sim Chit Udom, President of the Local Union at KRTive Factory, said that when he went to register the union, the Ministry of Labor took care to facilitate, explain and explain more places where he did not understand and even helped to verify the form. Documents as well. He said: "(The Ministry) helped to talk to him to help a lot, because we do not know much, so he helped from the information section is very easy."
He added that the practice in the field does not have the challenge of restricting freedoms or any concerns about his work activities, that is, unions and employers work well together to help fill the gaps. Space for the common good.
Ouch Sopheap, president of the local union at the Triumph factory, also said that the registration of the union was not biased or discriminatory at all. In completing the paperwork, Ministry officials paid attention by carefully reviewing the paperwork. He said that if there is a gap in any point, the Ministry has told the point to be corrected and the union has corrected according to what the Ministry has recommended and advised smoothly.
Mr. Sok Heng, president of the local union at the New Thagate factory, said that the exercise of his union rights was not obstructed or violated. In practice, both unions and companies work together in accordance with the law, when something happens, they always discuss and find a common solution, respecting each other's rights.
He said that for registration, if the union has enough information, documents and complete the correct form, there is no obstacle, that is, the Ministry has no restrictions, making any administrative difficulties.
It should be noted that in 2016, there were more than 3,000 unions in Cambodia, and by 2023, the number of unions in Cambodia has increased to more than 6,000. Separately, in the first 5 months of 2024, there are 70 new unions registered. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith announces the new mandate of Battambang Provincial Council
