New Adolescent Dolphin Dies in Kampot Province as Conservation Team Finds Cause
(Kampot): A new species of teenage dolphin was found dead on the morning of June 10, 2024 in Kampot province. This is according to the promotion of the Marine Mammal Conservation Technical Team of the Cambodian Marine Conservation Organization (MCC).
After receiving this information this morning, the Marine Mammal Conservation Technical Team of the Cambodian Marine Conservation Organization (MCC) cooperated with the Trapeang Rapov Community Fisheries Committee of Kampot Province to examine and judge this species of dolphin.
According to conservation groups, the presence of invertebrate dolphins in Cambodian waters is a new record, and it also results in an increase in biodiversity, especially in food sources, habitat and safety, which attract endangered species. Come and live in the Cambodian Marine Fisheries Conservation Area.
The technical team will also continue to research the new record for more detailed and detailed information and try to protect the new mammal.
