Battambang Agriculture Officials Investigate More Information on the Price of 1 Kilo 300 Riel
(Battambang): The team of the Department of Agriculture of Battambang visited Mr. "Horm Savoeut", the owner of a cucumber plantation in Battambang province, to ask for more information and to find out the reason for posting that the price of eggplant has dropped by 1 kg 300 Riel.
It should be reminded that on June 7, 2024, a Facebook account named Horm Savoeut posted about the price of eggplant, which confuses the masses of social media users that the price of eggplant is 300 riel per kilogram.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture, Mr. Khim Finang, pointed out that after receiving a response from Mr. Horm Savoeut, a team from the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture visited the plantation owner to ask for more information about the fall in the price of 300 R / kg. "We will continue to look for reasons why the price of eggplant here is so much lower than the market price elsewhere," he said.
According to Khim Finang, the owner of the plantation grows only 3,000 square meters of land and collects 200 kilograms at a time, so solving the problem for this plantation is not difficult. "But what we are trying to understand is that in Battambang, eggplant is sold at a lower price than the market, when the price of eggplant across the country is at least 1,000 riel per kilogram, this is What we are studying to find out more.
