Thailand to set new targets for economic growth and accelerate investment spending (Video inside) For economic growth this year as the government is trying to recover from a slower economy than other countries in the region. According to Reuters.
Pichai Chunhavajira was quoted by Reuters as saying at a meeting of economic ministers to discuss stimulus measures that the Thai government would like to see at least 70 percent of its investment budget released. Prepared in the current fiscal year ending September 2024.
As of June 7, about 38.6 percent of the investment budget had been spent, he added.
Pichai said Thailand plans to take short-term stimulus measures to start its economic recovery, which is expected to grow by only 2.5 percent this year. He added that the economy should grow at least 3.5 percent a year.
Southeast Asia's second-largest economy grew 1.5 percent in the first quarter of this year from a year earlier, down from 1.7 percent in the fourth quarter. 2023. According to Reuters.
