Lt. Gen. Hun Manit Distributes Raincoats of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to Troops in the 3rd Zone
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of June 10, 2024, Lt. Gen. Hun Manit, Director General of the General Department of Research and Intelligence of the Ministry of Defense and Deputy Commander of the Army, distributed raincoats, a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Senate President of the Senate and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the Armed Forces in the Third Zone.
The ceremony was attended by Lt. Gen. Yoeung Sokhon, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 3rd Army Division, and all 21 units of the 3rd Army Division received donations.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manit said that the rainy season has arrived and we have brought raincoats donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to prepare for the participation of the forces in rescuing people during the rainy season.
At the same time, the forces must have a strong position to protect the people, protect the peace after Cambodia liberated the motherland from the dictatorship, now the country has built a new page of history, starting from the leadership with a clear vision. These are absolutely necessary to protect the Royal Government, which is elected by the people to have a policy to lead the nation to progress in the future.
In our opinion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manit said, "We can not control people, but we can lead and educate people." Once again, he reminded all skilled soldiers not to increase the risk of accidents eventually, as in the case of bombings like in the past, which caused the deaths of up to 20 fighters, sadly, finally have to build skills. Proficiency.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manit stressed that the most worrying thing is that the opposition has always created false information through artificial intelligence (AI), causing serious confusion to many senior leaders and some citizens. There is still confusion over this fake information.
(Rattanakiri): General Chiang Am, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Ratanakkiri Province this morning, June 10, 2024, announced the new mandate of Ratanakkiri Provincial Councilors.
The ceremony was held at the meeting hall of Building D, Ratanakkiri Provincial Hall, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. Ratanakkiri Provincial National Team, Mr. and Mrs. Provincial leaders, heads of units around the province, Mr. and Mrs. District Governor, more than 100 people.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, said that in the past 5 years, the Board of Governors has cooperated well with the Council, achieving many great achievements in both Buddhism and the Empire, achieving a very effective indicator, especially taking action. To prevent various crimes and eliminate all inactive activities to ensure security and public order to the people well.
On behalf of the Royal Government, General Chiang Am, on behalf of the Royal Government, congratulated and highly appreciated the members of Ratanakkiri Provincial Council, who were elected by the people, the members of the Commune / Sangkat Council, who voted with confidence to continue to lead Ratanakkiri Province. More sectors. He advised to strive to serve the interests and needs of all people fairly, racially and politically.
(Battambang): Leaders and members of the opposition party are walking away from the party they live with like a dam after losing hope in the party leader.
Seven leaders of the Candlelight Party Executive Committee in Ampil commune, Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province, have decided to leave the party with which they used to engage in political activities.
The leaders of the seven opposition parties have all been active in helping the opposition's political affairs for many years. They decided to leave the party because they lost faith in the leadership and the way of life of the opposition, which is divided, partisan and lacks transparency in leadership.
In addition, the declaration of opposition to the Funan Techo canal project by Sam Rainsy was a major part of their decision to leave the opposition. They consider the opposition to the Funan Techo canal project a false idea, a betrayal of the nation as a whole.
For the above reasons, the leaders of the Candle Light Party in the 7 Ampil communes decided to respect the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, to participate in political life and political activities with the Cambodian People's Party to have Opportunity to serve the party as well as serve the nation and the people.
Six candidates for the district council of the Khmer Will Party in Sandan district, Kampong Thom province, announced their departure from the party and asked to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party (Video inside) (Battambang): Leaders and members of the opposition party are leaving The party he coexists with is like a dam after losing hope in party leaders.
Six members of the Khmer Will Party, a full-fledged candidate and a reserve candidate in Kampong Thom province's Sandan district, have decided to leave their former political party.
The leaders of the six opposition parties have all been active in helping the opposition's political affairs for many years. They decided to leave the party because they lost faith in the leadership and the way of life of the opposition, which is divided, partisan and lacks transparency in leadership.
For the above reasons, the full candidates and reserve candidates of Sandan District Council of the six Khmer Will Party decided to respect the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, to participate in political life and political activities with the party. Cambodians to have the opportunity to serve the party as well as serve the nation and the people. Senior Minister Ieng Moly Holds a Meeting on HIV / AIDS Response in Social Affairs
The purpose of this meeting is as follows:
The achievements of Cambodia in the field of HIV / AIDS and HIV / AIDS, especially in the field of social affairs, veterans and youth rehabilitation, present the National Strategic Plan for HIV Response for Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. Review and implement measures of the National Policy to End AIDS and Sustainable AIDS Programs in the Social, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation Areas.
Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National AIDS Authority, welcomed the working group and the meeting, praising the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation for their active participation in responding to HIV / AIDS, especially the provision of programs. Social protection for the vulnerable in the past.
With the approval of the Senior Minister, the Chairman of the Meeting, Mr. You Sopheak, Director of the Secretariat of the AIDS Committee, presented a strategic plan for responding to HIV and AIDS in the social sector, which included five strategies supported by the activities. 22 tips. He also pointed out that as of April, 431 people living with HIV have received funding for vulnerable people.
At the end of the presentation, the Secretary of the Secretariat requested the following: * Request for financial and technical support from the National AIDS Authority to develop a social service package to help poor families living with HIV and AIDS. * Request guidance from the National AIDS Authority to support the Strategic Plan for AIDS Response, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
The Royal Government provides free antiretroviral drugs to people living with HIV and provides equity fund certificates to people living with HIV. Although Cambodia has improved its response to HIV and its stigma and discrimination have been reduced, stigma and discrimination persist, so the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation must be involved in promoting it.
The King issued a Royal Decree to reduce the rank of Brigadier General Roeung Roen to the rank of "Sergeant" of the National Police
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree to reduce the rank of Brigadier General Roeung Roeun, a police officer working in the Land Border Protection Department, to the rank of "Sergeant". National Police, Ministry of Interior. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on June 10, 2024.
According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in May 2024, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved 24 new projects and one production expansion project with a total investment of more than 246 million US dollars and can create about 15,000 jobs. Place.
According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, the most prominent investment projects in May include:
A: Outside SEZ 1: Investment project to develop a 60-megawatt solar power plant with Kampong Chhnang province, located in Prey Chrov village, Kbal Teuk commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province with an investment capital of over 65 million US dollars and can create 35 jobs.
2: Investment project to establish a smelter and metal processing factory located in Tan village, Ta Nay commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province with an investment capital of more than 26 million US dollars and can create 317 jobs.
3: Investment project to establish a steel pipe factory located in O Tracheak Chet village, Samrong commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province with an investment of over 16 million US dollars and can create 229 jobs.
B: In Special Economic Zone 1: Investment project to establish an aluminum processing plant located in Jiangsu Special Economic Zone, National Road 6, with an investment of 25 million US dollars and can create 684 jobs.
On the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration, Samdech Hun Sen warned that there should be no interference in the process of selecting civil servants from those who are not involved. Ensure accuracy and guarantee reliability.
According to Hun Manet, the entrance exam for civil servants must start from the spirit of love and want to serve the people sincerely, not an investment. Of course, if there is an investment, it is not an investment in the budget, that is, you have to invest in strength, energy, and effort to learn, not to invest in investment lines to find money to bribe people.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia strives to ensure the accuracy and correctness of this exam, because this is a big task to encourage Cambodian children who want to become civil servants. Samdech continued that voluntary entry and dedication efforts increase the mindset of success through hard work.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet thanked all the candidates and their families for believing in the organization of the exam process in the past. While those who are not yet successful have to keep trying harder.
