* 250 Commune Agriculture Officers in 2023 * 100 Physical Education and Sports Teachers * 33 Anti-Corruption Unit Officers * 99 Officers of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport * 52 Officers of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Place * 343 secondary school teachers.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet: Civil servants are like serving themselves and their families, they need a better public service (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet stated that officials are not civil servants He is the master of the people, and the servants of the people are like the servants of themselves and their families, because the officials who are removed from office are also the people.
This morning, June 10, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathipadei Hun Manet said this on the occasion that Samdech presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration.
His Excellency Hun Manet said, "Every official is also a citizen, we only remove the position, only the workplace, we are also people living in the society, living in our village, commune, we need to retire from our civil servants. "Ordinary people, our children, our wives, our grandchildren are also people, so serving the people is like serving yourself and your family."
His Excellency Hun Manet also stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen had said that officials are servants of the people, not bosses of the people. There is support from the people, whether through elections or participation in creating economic growth, so that the state has the revenue to serve to solve their problems.
His Excellency Hun Manet added that if we want an environment that is comfortable to live with good public services for ourselves and our families, we should practice to provide good public services to officials and other people in The area where we work as well.
This statement was made by the Prime Minister on the morning of June 10, 2024, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet said that Cambodian children who want to become civil servants must invest in hard work, education and ability, not to rely on the party to become officials. And the Royal Government in the seventh mandate is aimed at reforming civil servants through the selection of civil servants based on meritocracy, accuracy, justice and environment, which is a very high priority.
Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet added that civil servants must start with self-confidence, not investment. You have to invest your energy, your physical strength, your hard work to learn, not invest in a line to find money to bribe. Therefore, the accuracy of the ability before becoming a civil servant is shown through the previous civil service selection exam organized by the Ministry of Public Function based on the principle of "who knows how to pass".
Samdech President Hun Manet also stated that the accuracy and correctness of this exam is an example, but it is a big task to encourage our Cambodian children who want to become civil servants.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that it is necessary to recruit competent officials who are not willing to have the skills to perform their duties, which means that if you recruit agricultural officials, you must not recruit professional officers in the field of civil engineering. Therefore, it is necessary to select officers based on the skills to be selected to be able to understand how to perform the roles and responsibilities assigned by superiors effectively.
As for the recruitment of officials to perform tasks that are not professional, the Prime Minister stated that it will cause the loss of national budget resources, human resources, which is the biggest point, and in some places, experts are not professional officers can go to help. Train the people and the excess officials do not have the opportunity to work full time or just take the framework, but do not have the opportunity to work to serve the people, which makes the government lose a lot.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that the Royal Government has set the conditions for the selection of candidates to be retained in order to select professional officers to serve the needs of the people at the local level to be more effective towards the goals of the people. The people want it.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration this morning, June 10, 2024.
"Our chair, our opportunity, our institution, our ability to serve the people depends on our people to build an environment for us, for our family in the future."
Samdech Hun Sen stated that it is not perfect, but we must work together to improve our environment to become a perfect environment on a regular basis. Together, recognize the first: create positive actions, add positive achievements to our society, and second: together reduce all negativity.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that these two points together, we can achieve the target group of a developed country, and especially a stable environment that we can get together with warmth, especially from Access to public services.
Samdech Hun Manet also reminded the public service officials to the people that "officials are the servants of the people, not the boss of the people" and the service to the people as well as self-service.
In front of more than 1,000 students and officials of the Royal School of Administration, the Prime Minister stressed that all people really do not want public services that require intervention or negotiation, but want a stable public service. Stable, reliable.
Samdech stated that officials are also people living in the community, and the families of those civil servants are also people, so serve the people as well as serve themselves and their families.
His Excellency's remarks were made on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration.
"We must work together to build a more efficient environment, a stable environment, clear access to public services from the current administration and in the future for convenience, it is the duty of every official to participate."
This statement was made on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the 2024 training course of the Royal School of Administration on June 10, 2024.
On that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen said, "The Royal School of Administration has taken care of many measures to strengthen discipline, but I think the school should be a school with high discipline standards, but measures to promote the implementation of discipline should not be too strict." .
The prince's words are "should!" Not a "must!" That no. Schools should have high standards of discipline, this is a big goal. Discipline starts with the responsibility of each student and the teacher in the school. This is what the President said that the Royal School of Administration should be a school with high standards of discipline, but should not have strict measures because civil servants as current and future leaders do not need to put pressure.
He added that the officials must have high standards, the leaders in the training here are all high-potential leaders, each student should understand the values and obligations. His Excellency Khuong Sreng's wife donated $ 2,500 to support the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia's "10,000 Riel 10,000" campaign in 2024
