According to the South Korean military, North Korea launched an additional 310 more balloons across the border on Sunday night into Monday. The North Korean balloons contained trash, such as scrap paper and plastic, but no hazardous materials have been reported so far.
Pyongyang on Sunday also launched about 330 garbage balloons into South Korean territory, claiming to be in response to the posting of leaflets criticizing Kim Jong Un's regime by a group of activists in Korea. South. At the same time, South Korea resumed its propaganda loudspeakers in the border areas after suspending a military agreement signed with North Korea in 2018.
The resumption of dumping in South Korea comes after North Korean leader Kim Jong Un's sister, Kim Jong Un, warned of retaliation if Seoul continued to use loudspeakers. Propaganda in border areas and posting anti-Pyongyang leaflets on North Korean soil.
Remarks by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Closing Ceremony of 2023 Training Course and Opening Ceremony of 2024 Training Course of Royal School of Administration
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, June 4, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 training course and the opening of the training course. 2024 of the Royal School of Administration.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet: Opportunity to close the training course in 2023 and open the training course in 2024 of the Royal School of Administration:
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet was pleased to attend the closing ceremony of the training course for students, officers and trainees who were successful graduates in 2023 and the opening ceremony of the 2024 school year training course of the Royal School of Administration.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet congratulated all the winners who worked hard to study until they achieved a proud achievement.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that this great success was achieved through the efforts of the winners and the active participation of the Board, Management, Professors, Academic Staff, as well as the support of spouses and families. .
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that today's winner is the additional human resources and human capital for Cambodia who have the ability, quality, knowledge and skills, through successful training at the Royal School of Administration.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that human resources with high human capital is a key factor for all development processes.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that everything can not work with quality, efficiency and productivity without high qualified human resources, both hard and soft skills, and efforts to implement the work in accordance with the code. High professional ethics.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that human resources are a priority for building a modern and strong Cambodian society through a market economy.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that a strong knowledge base will bring better work achievement and job success.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that in every mandate, the Royal Government of Cambodia always gives high priority to the construction and development of human resources and human capital in all fields for the purpose of sustainable social development.
* President Hun Manet stated that the core policy of the "Phase 1 Strategic Strategy" is to strengthen governance.
* President Hun Manet stated that in order to improve governance, two main factors are needed: mechanisms and people.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has led the Cambodian People's Party since the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime. .
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the modernization of services is a high priority of the current government.
* President Hun Manet stated that the plan will achieve 50%, but success depends on the implementation of flexible people.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that ministries, institutions of the state, both national and sub-national, without standards, codes of conduct and cooperation can not be effective.
* President Hun Manet stated that those who commit corruption in the selection of public servants will face action by the Anti-Corruption Unit.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal School of Administration should have a high standard of discipline.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the students of the Royal School of Administration, who are all officials, should not need the school to implement disciplinary measures. Students should have a high sense of discipline.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government does not want to implement the fifth approach, but officials must make efforts to implement the first four approaches.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that learning is not to get stamped, but to get knowledge.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the honor, discipline and value of the school depends on the quality of knowledge and practice of students at graduation.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that no one is perfect, but you have to work hard to make yourself perfect.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet reminded Samdech Techo Hun Sen that officials are the servants of the people, not the masters of the people.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that serving the people is like serving yourself and your family, you need a better public service.
* President Hun Manet stated that not everyone wants the provision of public services that require intervention or negotiation.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the role and chair of officials came because of the people.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that officials must adhere to the approach of responsibility.
* Samdech Hun Manet advised all ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations to provide opportunities and encourage leaders and professional officers to participate in providing training and knowledge sharing programs to students, officials, trainees and trainees of the Royal School of Administration.
* Samdech Hun Manet advised the Ministry of Public Works to continue to promote the development of a more complete and appropriate digital officer information management system to ensure the management and updating of data structures and the actual qualifications of officials in their units. Ministries-institutions and sub-national administrations to serve the purpose of managing and developing the capacity of officials.
* Samdech Hun Manet instructed the Royal School of Administration to continue to develop training capacity through the use of information technology, including the development of digital training nurseries to support and expand training capacity and provide additional new opportunities for capacity building officials.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that in the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, all ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations must pay attention to promoting and enhancing the capacity of leaders and officials at all levels to adapt and Use digital technology in public administration to increase productivity and efficiency, and to ensure the successful implementation of digital government policies and positive outcomes.
* Samdech Hun Manet advised the Royal School of Administration to continue to improve the quality and effectiveness of training by organizing training courses based on the assessment of clear and real needs of the work in the units of ministries-institutions and sub-national administrations and must have Regularly review and evaluate the results of training on unit performance.
Kim Yoo-jung's warning was made in a statement released by North Korean state media KCNA on Monday, June 10, 2024. "If the Republic of Korea (ROK) uses loudspeakers and launches leaflets to provoke cross-border incidents, it will prompt a new response from the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (DPRK)," Kim said. North Korea).
