Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center Holds 26th Japanese Speech Competition
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center on June 9, 2024 organized the 26th Japanese Speech Competition at the Institute of Foreign Languages (IFL) of the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
The Japanese Speech Contest was co-chaired by Mr. Ueno Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, Prof. Dr. Oum Ravi, Vice Chancellor of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, and Dr. Khim Leang, Director of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center. The participation of the presidium and students as well as the competition.
The competition is designed to give Japanese language learners in Cambodia the opportunity to demonstrate their Japanese language skills in writing short speeches, and is a program designed to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the Japanese language. Establish the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center of the Royal University of Phnom Penh and continue to strengthen the friendship and solidarity between the two countries.
On this occasion, Dr. Khim Leang encouraged all students to continue their efforts to study more professionally or professionally and in foreign languages, especially Japanese, due to the growing demand for Japanese language resources of Japanese companies. Grow every year as they are the bamboo shoots that must be ready to participate in the development of Cambodia to grow more now as well as in the future.
He added that the program will invite outstanding Japanese language learners from all over the world to the Japan Foundation Center in Kansai, Japan, located in Osaka for two weeks so that all participants have the opportunity to meet. Learn more about Japanese language and culture and society through training and visits, and this program is scheduled to take place from September 4 to 18, 2024.
He said that the successful candidates can also participate in a week-long study tour to Japan in the fall.
She hopes that the Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Japan, the Japan Foundation, the Japan International Cooperation Agency and other Japanese agencies, will continue to support human resource development through this program, training programs and other scholarship programs for Cambodia in the future. Coming soon.
It is reported that the Japanese Speech Contest has been held 26 times already, with the support of many private companies and institutions. Ukraine claims to have attacked the latest generation of Russian fighter jets for the first time.
