(Sihanoukville): A Thai container ship carrying cargo to the port of Sihanoukville met with strong waves and sank in the sea near Koh Rong, Sihanoukville at noon on June 9, 2024. The victims of the Thai ship were rescued by a fishing boat nearby.
According to the report of the authorities and port officials, the sinking ship was 49 meters long, 15 meters wide and more than 3 meters deep on a container ship (container) with 10 Thai people were rescued. Completely by fishing boat near the scene and brought to the mainland of Sihanoukville by the speedboat of Duke Tea Vichet safely.
The rescue operation involved the Front Line Command, the General Secretariat of the National Committee for Maritime Security and the Joint Task Force of the Sihanoukville Provincial Administrative Authority, as well as the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, told Fresh News: "After receiving this information, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administrative Authority, together with the relevant authorities and relevant departments, took care to rescue the ship's crew and crew. A total of 10 people were rescued and brought to the mainland of Sihanoukville safely, no one was injured.
He said that due to the timely rescue from the fishermen, together with the authorities as well as the volunteer rescue team of Duke Tea Vichet, and when brought to the mainland, the provincial administrative authority, together with the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, sent people The 10 Thai victims went for medical check-ups, accommodation and humanitarian food.
