SEOUL, June 9 (Xinhua) - South Korea on Sunday announced that it will re-launch the loudspeakers under its anti-DPRK propaganda campaign in the border area after Pyongyang launched a balloon. South Korea again. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
"We will install anti-North Korean loudspeakers today (June 9) and resume the campaign," the South Korean presidential office said in a statement. The statement added that North Korea was fully responsible for the escalation of tensions between the two Koreas. The decision comes after Seoul suspended a military deal signed with North Korea in 2018.
According to the South Korean military, from Saturday night until the morning of Sunday, June 9, more than 300 garbage balloons were launched into South Korean territory. The balloons were found in Seoul and several locations near the border. North Korea last week promised to resume the campaign if anti-North Korean leaflets were posted from South Korea into its territory.
A group of South Korean activists did not heed the warning and launched a balloon carrying leaflets criticizing Kim Jong Un, including a USB storage of K-pop music videos, movies and dollars, entering North Korean territory on Thursday. .
