SEOUL: North Korea has resumed launching a balloon into South Korean territory a week after promising to resume the campaign if anti-North Korean leaflets were released from South Korea. Its territory. This is according to a release by Reuters.
Dozens of balloons containing garbage were found in Seoul and several locations near the border area on Saturday night and Sunday morning, June 9, 2024, after the South Korean military said North Korea was launching them. Those trash balloons. The South Korean military has said it is paying close attention to the balloon and is preparing to take action if necessary. But did not specify what action will be taken.
South Korea has warned of "unconditional retaliation against North Korea" for launching a balloon into its territory, including the resumption of loudspeakers critical of Kim Jong Un's regime. In the border areas.
South Korean activists did not heed the warning and launched a balloon carrying leaflets criticizing Kim Jong Un, including USB storage of K-pop music videos, movies and dollars, entering North Korean territory on Thursday.
