(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, on the afternoon of June 9, 2024, the representative of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister, presided over the closing ceremony of the 31st National Examination. And the 5th Oral Quiz of the National Al-Qaeda in 2024. ” The ceremony was held at the 9th km mosque.
Speaking on the occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun expressed his pride and happiness with today's Al-Quran recitation ceremony under the theme "Islam Joins the Fight Against Illegal Drugs", which is very reflective and consistent. According to the policy, will and vision of the Royal Government is "Join together for a drug-free life and community."
After appreciating the efforts of Duke Sos Kamrey, Director General of the Cambodian Islamic Council, as well as Islamic leaders at all levels and the Ministry of Cults and Religions, who assisted in organizing the process, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun Shared some ideas and recommendations as follows:
* First, the Supreme Islamic Council of Cambodia must continue the spirit of preserving and promoting national and religious harmony, solidarity and brotherhood among Muslims, as well as among all Cambodians, in order to maintain the national pride that Cambodia does not Conflict with ethnic or religious conflicts and contribute to the maintenance of peace and sustainable development
* Third: All Muslims must study hard to turn the sacred and meaningful content of the Qur'an and the words of the Prophet Muhammad into practical action for the sake of good values and social morality. Both must work together in solidarity and brotherhood to participate in the prevention, eradication and use of illegal drugs to build a safe, secure and harmonious community.
* Fourth: The Supreme Council of Cambodian Islam, organizations, associations, philanthropists, please increase social activities through humanitarian work, education, development and beneficial activities based on the principles of respect for the Constitution, the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the fundamental principles of faith. Its religion
* Sixth: All Muslims who have the opportunity to continue their studies or missions abroad, please promote the achievements and successes that the Cambodian Muslim community has achieved so that the whole world can see the good example of Cambodia in living together, unity, brotherhood and national and religious harmony, all of which are the greatest pride of Muslims in Cambodia
* Seventh: Call on local authorities at all levels to facilitate the legitimate gatherings of the Cambodian Islamic community and continue to implement the policy of "safe villages, communes, sangkats" to build a community free of drug trafficking and use. No gangsters, no crimes that affect the safety and harmony of the people in the community.
