(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is considered the country in the third largest producer of cashew nuts in the world, currently producing more than 750,000 tons of cashew nuts per year.
However, of that yield, about 95% of the raw seeds are exported to neighboring countries, especially Vietnam, and only 5% are processed by local factories.
Mr. An Dara, President of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia, said that cashews are a crop with great potential and high value, and if it is a processed product, it will get more value added.
Answering the question of which is more profitable between opening a processing company and purchasing raw cashew nuts to a neighboring country, he said that if you want to make quick money, you should buy raw cashew nuts and export them. Encourage more processing, because processing, in addition to adding value, also contributes to the creation of local jobs for Cambodians.
He said the government has set a plan to boost mango processing by 25% by 2027, while the market for processed cashew nuts from Cambodia is remarkably large. However, the challenge that factory owners face is the high cost of production, which makes it difficult to compete with other countries.
He said that currently Cambodian processed cashews sell at a price higher than other countries, about $ 0.5 or 2,000 riel per kilogram.
He said that if the processed cashew nuts have low cost, the price can be competitive with them, then Cambodia will be able to export more and be more profitable, as well as be able to achieve the set plan. More than 10 kg of drugs and more than 30 kg of chemicals with 8 Vietnamese offenders were cracked down by the Anti-Drug Department
