Doctoral students of the Royal Academy of Cambodia: Why does Cambodia not participate in the "Ukraine Peace" conference?
"The decision not to attend the Cambodian conference is a Cambodian right, as Cambodia sees it as unsuccessful," he added.
The decision not to attend the "Ukraine Peace" conference came at a time when Cambodian leaders saw no solution as the conflicting parties were not present at the talks. The absence of Russia, a party to the conflict, made it clear that the conference was designed to support Ukraine, a party to the conflict, and to reject Russia's involvement in reaching an agreement to end this protracted war. .
In this regard, it is clear that in the Russia-Ukraine war, the superpowers, especially the West, refused to back down or soften their stance or make any concessions to the parties to the conflict. But the West is increasingly intent on raising the stakes - the conference has not yet been convened, and it can already be seen that the outcome of the conference is aimed directly at Russia.
For Cambodia, the decision not to participate in the Ukraine Peace Conference is a further affirmation of Cambodia's independence and neutrality as a sovereign state, especially a declaration of respect for the principle of non-alignment. In the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, "Cambodia will not join any alliance against another country."
The declaration of non-participation in the "Ukraine Peace" conference is an expression of the position of Cambodia, which has already voted against Russia's military intervention in Ukraine, that Cambodia has its own political position that does not belong to any superpower or party. Any alliance, as Cambodia is a pacifist country, attaches great importance to resolving issues through peaceful negotiations and does not support any intention to try to ignite further problems.
This may also be due to the Cambodian leadership's remarks on the resilient stance of some countries, some of which are US allies and the West, that continue to trade with Russia in response to development trends. Its economy as the United States and the West try to impose sanctions on Russia.
Overall, in line with recent developments in the world order and the current geopolitical uncertainty, the Cambodian leader's refusal to participate in the "Ukraine Peace" conference is a smart diplomatic strategy that Cambodia is weighing and considering. Try to balance relations with the West and relations with Russia and China.
Cambodia's own political stance is the right path in relations with the superpowers in the context of the superpowers' constant competition for influence, as they are always trying to put Cambodia in a difficult position. That is, choosing one power and kicking the other.
However, Cambodia, which has suffered from the war in which the great powers sowed ideologies and divided factions to compete with each other and have gained experience in resolving the end of the war, does not want to see divisions in order to Against any country, because after the war, Cambodia has already suffered from political and economic blockades from countries with different factions.
By: Lim Sovanrith, PhD student in Political Science of the Royal Academy of Cambodia
