The South China Sea arbitration case, which is presumed to be false, is an illegal trial. The Chinese side does not accept any initiatives or actions based on this trial.
BEIJING, June 6 (Xinhua) - An international seminar on "Review of the South China Sea Arbitration Trial" was held in Qingdao, China on June 6. National and international legal experts have had in-depth discussions on issues related to the South China Sea Arbitration Trial from the perspective of international law.
The Philippines proposed a unilateral arbitration of the South China Sea in 2013, which was actually a political ploy to use the law as a stepping stone. China has always stressed that the trial of the so-called South China Sea arbitration case is illegal and ineffective, and China does not accept any initiatives or actions based on this trial.
