Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, Bamboo Grape Foundation Foundation, in collaboration with local authorities and the private sector, organized a cycling program to participate in the 2024 Environmental Tourism Event and the 2nd Cambodia Freshwater Festival
(Siem Reap): The Viney Bamboo Foundation in collaboration with local authorities and the private sector on June 08, 2024 organized a cycling program to participate in the 2024 Environmental Tourism Event and the 2nd Cambodia Freshwater Festival.
The event was also attended by Mr. Kob Ron, Chief of Chreav Commune, Mr. Eng Kunthea, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association, Siem Reap Branch, Mr. Sea Sophal, Bamboo Vine and Private Sector Foundation, representatives of the association, as well as many cyclists.
Mr. Sea Sophal continued that in the past, when it comes to cycling, everyone rides to the Angkor area, which is organized as a cycling route and is also popular for tourists. He said that the landscape along the road next to the Tonle Sap Lake changes with the seasons, such as the low water season is very attractive, including biodiversity, flooded forests, plantations and the lives of local people, which is a unique spectacle. One eye from another area.
He added that the main benefit for participating in this event is to protect the conservation of natural resources and protect biodiversity conservation areas such as Boeung Pearang (Siem Reap) and Boeung Prey K'aek (Kampong Phluk), which is rich in flocks of birds. Enter the eggs in the dry season. If there are tourism activities there, it will also reduce fishing crimes and partially flooded forests.
Mr. Sea Sophal expects that this cycling activity will help spread the potential of tourism to a wider audience. Indeed, this cycling program is part of the 2024 Environmental Tourism Event and the 2nd Cambodia Freshwater Festival, organized by the Bamboo Shoots Foundation.
Ms. Cham Srey Oeun hopes that the launch of this program will increase awareness of the impact of plastic pollution and contribute to local communities as well as contribute to the development of green tourism.
Separately, Mr. Kob Ron said that Chreav is an agricultural district and also has a road for national and international tourists to enjoy cycling and enjoy the beautiful scenery on the streets, especially to see the business. People's agriculture as well.
Mr. Kob Ron hopes that in the future, the commune will become an agricultural tourism district and more national and international tourists will be able to improve the lives of farmers in Chreav commune to some extent.
It should be noted that the cycling program to participate in the eco-tourism event 2024 and the second Cambodia Freshwater Sea Festival also stopped at some locations to promote environmental hygiene to the people and also collected garbage in some locations.
