(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, has issued five sharp reform recommendations on migrant workers to show transparency and efficiency in ensuring maximum benefits for migrants.
These five recommendations include:
First, the revocation of the license of an inactive private agency
Second, private agencies are not allowed to send workers without a partner in the host country.
Third, the Ministry will evaluate the agency on an annual basis, with the first-ranked company receiving incentives. In particular, companies with bad rankings (No. 3) will be publicized.
And fifth, the Ministry has coordinated with the bank so that workers can get loans at an interest rate of not more than 10% per annum in the near future. Cambodian Red Cross Donates 19th Humanitarian House to Poor Elderly in Angkor Ban Commune, Kang Meas District
(Kampong Cham): The President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on June 8, 2024, led his colleagues with the participation of monks and invited and handed over the 19th house as a program of humanitarian housing in Choun Daun Province. Homeless old man named Bon Seng Nguon, 72 years old, lives in Angkor Ban 7 village, Angkor Ban commune, Kang Meas district.
Mr. Touch Chhay, Executive Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Red Cross Branch, said that Ms. Bon Seng Nguon was a poor old woman living under the house of a poor neighbor with only two grandchildren and one grandson whose parents had migrated outside the province.
Not only does she have no job to earn a living, but she also has a physical illness. Today, the old woman lives on the help of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Equity Card 2 and the food subsidy from the neighbors. This poor old lady owns 13 meters by 22 meters of land in Angkor 7 village, however, due to the poor living conditions, she can not afford to build a house at all.
Separately, 15 grandparents who witnessed the handover ceremony of this new house, each received rice, fish, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce and T-shirt, as well as 20,000 Riels.
