Please be informed that as of the announcement of the Ministry of Health on June 9, 2024, Cambodia has found 19 cases of Kovid disease: a total of 139,207 people, a total of 136,115 people were cured, a total of 3,056 people died. . Dr. Yong Pov: The trend of reading news in print seems to be declining, but the demand for reading information is increasing rapidly, journalists need to strengthen the quality to prevent fake news
(Phnom Penh): It is said that the trend of reading information in print seems to be declining significantly. However, according to Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, although the trend of reading news in print seems to be declining, the demand for reading information has increased dramatically and the trend of reading and following news in Cambodia has not decreased. No, and the demand for information is growing steadily.
Dr. Yong Pov pointed out that although the reading of information in print format has decreased due to the advancement of digital technology, but the demand for reading and tracking information in Cambodia is still growing steadily, only the masses, especially young people tend to read and Track information on electronic devices such as phones, tablets and computers.
Dr. Yong Pov said that the need for information is the most important thing for today's society. So reading news is on the rise, but just change the way you read news by looking at print newspapers and magazines, turning to high-speed digital reading. "The need for information is necessary. Whoever reads less information is not right, it is more."
At the same time, Dr. Yong Pov expressed the view that for the media and journalists must improve the quality of their writing. Therefore, at the stage of increasing professional information, there will be a decrease in non-professional information in Cambodian society.
Dr. Yong Pov emphasized: "We understand the need for information, almost more need for coffee than food, because start looking at information before coffee. Well, I would say that the influence of information is very strong, broadcast through this digital system is to reach the reader immediately in a minute at most.
At the same time, the geopolitical expert also expressed concern about the rapid credibility of the digital sector, especially artificial intelligence (AI), if you create content to pollute society, it will cause immediate social unrest. . In this sense, professional journalists and stakeholders are required to participate in disseminating true information together.
"Digital and artificial intelligence are man-made, but in some cases humans are out of control, which requires the utmost care to manage digital and These artificial intelligence to orient the use and utilization for the living and development of society and the world.
"We can not escape from digital and artificial intelligence, if we can escape from this era, so we need to manage, increase resilience and take advantage of digital technology and artificial intelligence for," he said. Daily social life.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Meas Sophea, Supreme Advisor to the King and Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear Constituency, on the morning of June 8, 2024, led a team to bring an ambulance donated by him and his wife to the health center. Ranasir is located in Ranasir commune, Sangkum Thmey district.
