(Vietnam): The General Department of Customs of Cambodia attended the 33rd ASEAN Customs Meeting in Vietnam to promote trade facilitation and improve the investment, trade and business environment in the region.
Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, who led the delegation to attend the meeting, took the opportunity of a bilateral meeting with a delegation from the Thai Customs Administration and a delegation from the Japanese Customs Administration for further purposes. Strengthen customs cooperation and bilateral relations.
The agenda of the meeting with the Thai Customs Administration includes: monitoring the progress of the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding on Transit Goods, cooperation in the fight against transnational crime, and the preparation of bilateral meetings of the Customs Unit of the Cambodia-Thailand border provinces. Coming soon.
In particular, the meeting with the Japanese Customs Administration has the following agendas: monitoring the progress on cooperation between the two customs administrations in the past, providing technical assistance in capacity building to Cambodian customs, mutual support in Regional and World Customs Forum (WCO). The two delegations also discussed the further preparation of a framework document on cooperation between the two customs administrations.
