Voice of the Heritage Site "Yunnan Tour, Visit Angkor", a major event in the cooperation between Cambodia and China, officially launched in Kunming, Yunnan Province, China
(China): The Voice of the Heritage Site "Travel in Yunnan, Visit Angkor" is an important event in the cooperation between Cambodia and China, promote culture, tourism, investment and strengthen ties between Cambodia and China. The series was officially inaugurated on June 7, 2024 in Kunming, Yunnan Province, China.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, and Ms. Zheng Yian, Permanent Member and Chairman of the Propaganda Department of the CPC Yunnan Provincial Committee, with the participation of representatives from the Ministry of Tourism, representatives of the Association of Journalists, Journalists and Travel Agencies. As well as many other investment companies.
Minister Neth Pheaktra said that the program "Sightseeing in Yunnan to visit Angkor" will provide a good opportunity for all of us to understand the beauty of the World Heritage Site in Cambodia and Yunnan Province and learn about its history. Long lasting with an attractive culture for tourism.
On behalf of the Ministry of Information of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Minister Neth Pheaktra expressed his congratulations on the celebration of this important event within the framework of the Year of People-to-People Exchange "Cambodia-China", which the top leaders of Cambodia and China is set to actively and vigorously promote cooperation in tourism, trade and investment.
He said that China and Cambodia are good friends and good partners who have traditionally enjoyed friendly relations since ancient times, and are deeply rooted in the long history of our two countries.
The Minister of the Cambodian delegation said that the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China have set 2024 as the year of people-to-people and Cambodian-Chinese exchanges. The program "Travel in Yunnan to visit Angkor" is designed to strengthen cultural exchanges, tourism and people-to-people cooperation in order to strengthen the Cambodian-Chinese relations to be stronger and more vibrant in the new era.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that Cambodia is a country with the oldest civilization in Southeast Asia and rich in cultural heritage, traditions and customs. Angkor Wat is a heritage that makes the people of Cambodia and the world very proud.
Angkor Wat was successfully inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1992. The Royal Government of Cambodia has focused on the protection and conservation of the Angkor site and has turned this archeological site into a world-famous tourist destination, attracting tourists from all over the world.
According to data from the Ministry of Tourism, in 2023, Cambodia received 5.45 million tourists, including 550,000 Chinese tourists, and in the first three months of 2024, Cambodia received 1 tourist. 58 million, of which 190,000 are Chinese tourists.
Minister Neth Pheaktra expressed his optimism that through the organization of campaigns and tourism events between Cambodia and China will make it more attractive for tourists to visit, and in which the media really plays an important role in transmitting Messages about various potential tourism packages to the public.
In this regard, Ms. Zheng Yuan, Permanent Member and Chairman of the Propaganda Department of the CPC Yunnan Provincial Committee, praised the cooperation between China and Cambodia as a steel friend.
She believes that the Voice of Heritage site program "Travel to Yunnan, visit Angkor" will boost the tourism industry of both countries. During the opening ceremony, Cambodia and China showcased their tourism potential and also had art performances. Ministry of Environment graduates and plans to build a large-scale regional station in Phnom Kulen, which can guarantee the planting of 3 million seedlings per year
