Cambodia, Thailand, Vietnam agree to pilot first inland waterway transport by end of 2024
(Trat): Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam have agreed to try to organize the transportation of tourists by water from October or November 2024, which is the season with a lot of foreign visitors. For the first time for Cambodia's tourism sector to connect water transport with neighboring countries.
Mr. Long Dimanche, Deputy Governor of Sihanoukville and a representative of the Cambodian side, said that the CVETC business forum is a regional cooperation that emphasizes discussions to promote tourism in the three countries, including issues raised. Must work together to facilitate immigration procedures, customs, ports, water transport, communication between sellers - buyers and so on.
Mr. Long Dimanche encouraged the private sector to work together to organize tour packages for tourists to establish mutual waterway travel in accordance with the above agreement.
Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association in Cambodia, said that through today's business forum, there will be positive developments for Cambodia's tourism sector, especially the first inland waterway tourism exchanges with Thailand and Vietnam. Provide a new experience for the private sector and tourists.
The president of the association said that in addition to public services, Cambodia needs to increase the promotion of tourism in the sea, because for the past two years, the promotion has declined, so when this connection is made. Officially, if tourism promotion remains low, Cambodia will lose out on this cooperation.
The concern of Mr. Thuon Sinan is that the price of services in Sihanoukville has increased, including accommodation, food is the most expensive in ASEAN. He said the rise could lose competition with neighboring countries. On the other hand, Cambodia also needs to refrain from demanding extra money from tourists, which he calls "the act of snatching money from some individuals."
At the same time, he also urged Cambodian tour operators to promote their country's products to tourists in order to attract more tourists within the framework of CVTEC, do not wait for guests to contact Ask to bring home, that is, to knock on the door to advertise in the guest house.
Mr. Soy Sinol, Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Tourism, said that the CVTEC Business Forum is a new opportunity for Cambodia's coastal tourism and also suitable for development in Kampot, especially recently. Launched Kampot Multi-Purpose Port.
The Director of the Kampot Provincial Department of Tourism confirmed his readiness to be ready to receive guests within the framework of CVTEC, including all services in the tourism sector, while the people and tourists in Thailand have been very interested in the tourism potential in the province. Kampot, such as heritage buildings.
Mr. Taing Sochetkrisna, Director of Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Tourism, also said that Sihanoukville is ready to facilitate the work within the framework of CVTEC when the private sector can organize visits to tourists and the state is waiting. While tourism ports are already in place, island and coastal destinations are plentiful.
The Thai side also said that if the inland waterway transport connection is achieved, the Cambodian side, the Thai side and the Vietnamese side will achieve the "three countries, one destination" tourism vision, which always strives to discuss and Practice often then.
It should be informed that the three parties, Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam, also agreed to organize this CVTEC business forum every year to discuss the exchange of regional relations as well as the promotion of tourism. For Cambodia and Thailand is already hosting this forum, but Vietnam, so next year, the CVTEC forum can be held in Vietnam again.
Mr. Ung Dipola led a team to plant 1,000 saplings along National Road 5 in Trapeang Chong Commune, Bakan District, Pursat Province.
(Pursat): On the morning of June 8, 2024, the working group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Trapeang Chong commune, Bakan district organized a tree planting ceremony on both sides of National Road No. 5 with a length of about 14 km in Trapeang commune. .
