Senate Leaders and Global Life-Sharing Fund Meet with 4 Provincial Leaders to Understand Priority Needs on Health, Education and Citizens' Welfare
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunneang, Chairman of the Senate Investigation and Anti-Corruption Commission, and Mr. Kim Jong Nam, Chairman of the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea, and their colleagues met in Kampong Cham, Kampong Speu Province, Kandal Province. And Siem Reap to understand the priority needs of the health, education and well-being of the people.
On that occasion, Mr. Mam Bunneang and Mr. Kim Jong Nam brought a memorandum on the provision of humanitarian aid, which includes: medicine, medical equipment and daily necessities in the amount of $ 5 million for the implementation of 5 years from 2025 By 2029, the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea through the Senate handed over to the administrations of Kampong Cham, Kampong Speu, Kandal and Siem Reap provinces at the provincial halls of the four provinces.
It should be recalled that on June 5, 2024, the Senate of Cambodia signed a Memorandum of Understanding between the Senate Commission on Investigation and Anti-Corruption and the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea on "Providing Humanitarian Aid to the Senate of The Kingdom of Cambodia.
The MoU was signed by Mr. Mam Bunneang and Mr. Kim Jong Nam under the chairmanship of Mr. Ouch Borith, Second Vice President of the Senate, to continue to provide humanitarian assistance to the Cambodian Senate for the second time for implementation in five years. Additional years (2025-2029).
In the spirit of the Memorandum of Understanding, the Global Life-Sharing Fund will provide humanitarian assistance to the administrations of Kandal, Siem Reap, Kampong Speu and Kampong Cham Provinces, with each province receiving $ 5 million over five years. Five) years to improve the lives, education and well-being of the Cambodian people.
Mr. Mam Bunneang emphasized that all these humanitarian aid is really contributing to improving the quality of life of the Cambodian people, especially the health and education of people in both urban and rural areas. .
On that occasion, the four provincial governors briefed the delegation on the geographical situation, demographics, employment, social affairs, economy, as well as the priority needs in the health and education sectors that needed to be supported by the Global Life-Saving Fund. .
(Phnom Penh): The Olympics is an international sporting event attended by athletes from all over the world and is usually held every four years, and you may have noticed that the symbol of the Olympics is Five contiguous contiguous divisions. The question is, what does this Olympic symbol mean?
The five Olympic teams represent the five continents that participated in the Olympics at the time, including Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe and Oceania (Australia).
Each of the five colors, including blue, yellow, black, green, and red, along with the white surface of the Olympic flag, represents the colors on the flags of the countries from which they were created. Became the official symbol of the Olympics in 1915. Special class on: How to write investigative news and report will start on June 15
