(Stung Treng): Two bags of drugs were transported by the suspects by water from neighboring countries through Cambodia, but met with patrol forces to prevent fishing crimes, then hit the boat and hit the shore and escaped. This incident happened on the afternoon of June 6, 2024 in Koh Hip village, O'Svay commune, Borey O'Svay Sen Chey district.
Mr. Nin Pisey, Director of the Ramsar Office of the Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment, said that on June 6, 2024, at 1:30 pm, Mr. Phok Nimol, Deputy Director of the Office, together with the park ranger, cooperated with the fishing community to patrol. Illegal fishing offenses during the closed fishing season in the Ramsar site.
During the mission, environmental and community forces patrolled at Bong Krak Kbal, Vern Sean village, and found a suspicious boat driver chasing the boat to Kbal Koh Ta Hoeung in Koh Hip village, Ou Svay commune, Borey district. O'Svay Sen Chey The suspect drove the boat into the bank and escaped.
The suspect left behind a boat, a TBC machine and two bags of suspected drugs. After suspecting the object in the bag, the force contacted to cooperate with the district police inspectorate, and the inspector made a note and sent it to the Stung Treng Provincial Police Commissioner to continue the procedure.
As of June 7, 2024, the provincial police has not confirmed what kind of drug and how much it weighs, because the procedure has not been completed yet.
ASEAN Minister for Science, Technology and Innovation issues Joint Statement after the 20th Meeting in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The 20th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science, Technology and Innovation (AMMSTI-20) was held on June 7, 2024 in Siem Reap. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
The meeting reaffirmed the commitment to strengthen cooperation in the fields of science, technology and innovation to ensure the effective implementation of the ASEAN Community Plan 2025 and the ASEAN Community Vision 2045 to address global and regional challenges. .
Malaysia-led ASEAN Business Startup Initiative. Serving as a common gateway to the new ASEAN Business Ecosystem, this initiative provides information on new businesses in ASEAN, related activities related to entrepreneurship, technology and information.
The ASEAN Talent Mobility System is designed to provide opportunities for ASEAN science, technology and innovation talents to mobilize, collaborate and contribute to regional growth. (AP) Implementation of the ASEAN Energy Sustainability Assessment Guidelines: Building a Thai-led Energy Sustainability Assessment Capacity.
ASEAN Member States will learn about energy sector resilience assessment based on the ASEAN Energy Sustainability Assessment Guidelines through the “Energy Sustainability Assessment Training: Towards "Towards a climate-adaptable energy system."
The meeting noted the progress of 93 science, technology and innovation activities carried out by nine sub-committees under the Science, Technology and Innovation Committee and 68 other activities supported by dialogue and other partners.
The meeting also commended the long-term cooperation between ASEAN, its dialogue partners and other partners in promoting science, technology and innovation for mutual benefit, including advocacy for funding for science, technology and technology. Innovation.
The meeting noted that the 21st ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science, Technology and Innovation (AMMSTI-21) will be hosted by Indonesia, scheduled for June 2025. The meeting thanked the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia for the warm hospitality to the ASEAN Ministers and Delegates and for the luxurious arrangements.
