Mr. Chap Dina inspected the actual sales situation in Central Market after unscrupulous people posted when the vendors have not opened the stall yet
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chap Dina, Deputy Governor of Daun Penh District, under the guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Chea Khema, Governor of Daun Penh District, on the evening of June 7, 2024, led officials of local authorities and Central Market Commission. Check the actual sales situation in the market after the unscrupulous people took pictures of the stalls in the morning, when the vendors have not opened the stalls yet.
He claimed that the photos distributed showing the vendors' stalls closed were taken in the early morning before they opened their businesses. "On June 7, Central Market traders, as well as traders in all markets in Phnom Penh, are doing business normally, there is nothing to disturb their eating habits," he said. .
Please be informed that on June 7, 2024, on social media, a few pictures of stalls in the Central Market were shared, imagining that the vendors were closing their stalls.
(Phnom Penh): An active drug trafficker and former prisoner involved in drug trafficking and arms trafficking shot himself when the police force of the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police in cooperation with the specialized force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Phnom Penh has been under siege since the afternoon of June 7, 2024 around Samhan Market in Sangkat Toul Sangke 1, Khan Russey Keo.
According to the report, during the operation, when the police were rushing to crack down, the perpetrators fired about 10 shots at the police, but no one was injured. Police did not return fire.
The operation to crack down on drug trafficking was under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, director of the Anti-Drug Crime Department, in collaboration with the specialized police force and local police force in Russey Keo district, under the command of General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner.
According to local authorities, the perpetrator was imprisoned after being arrested and detained in connection with drug trafficking and arms trafficking. The perpetrator was monitored by the specialized police force of the Anti-Drug Crime Department for a long time until the crackdown now.
After the siege, there was no way to escape, the perpetrator shot himself. Please note that this operation did not cause any police officers and citizens to be injured or injured, although the perpetrators fired several shots.
