The following is the Royal Decree: Council for the Development of Cambodia organizes a workshop to disseminate investment laws and regulations to officials in Kratie and Stung Treng provinces.
(Kratie): The Council for the Development of Cambodia, in collaboration with Kratie and Stung Treng Provincial Administrations, organized a workshop to disseminate investment laws and investment regulations to officials of the Kratie and Stung Treng Provincial Investment Sub-Committees to strengthen their capacity and legal knowledge. And legal documents related to investment as well as the provision of better services in this field.
Mr. Duong Pov expressed his gratitude and appreciation for the presence of the delegation of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which organized this important seminar and informed about the geographical, demographic, and some achievements related to investment, potential and economic situation of the province. Kratie too.
Mr. Try Dalux said at the ceremony that the promotion of national economic growth is a necessary policy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature led by Samdech Hun Manet. To boost national economic growth, achieve the target of middle-income countries by 2030 and high-income countries by 2050, investment is the most important catalyst.
Therefore, the Council for the Development of Cambodia, led by Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, Samdech's staff on investment, has put in place strategies to improve the working environment of investment-related officials to facilitate the work of investors. Like doing business in Cambodia.
Mr. Try Dalux highlighted that the seminar was held as part of raising awareness of investment laws and regulations. By understanding the laws and regulations, this will contribute to better service delivery.
For Try Dalux, better, faster and more accurate service is what investors want and attract them to do more business in Cambodia.
The Deputy Secretary-General expressed his strong hope that through this workshop, participants will gain the knowledge to exercise the authority entrusted to them with professional ethics and a high sense of responsibility.
During the opening ceremony, the Deputy Secretary General also brought souvenirs, krama, 100,000 Riels to the participants and a series of documents, including laws and regulations related to investment, as well as presentation documents of the speakers to the participants. Also.
Mr. Thou Chanpov, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province, highly appreciated the workshop and thanked Mr. Try Dalux for leading the working group of the Council for the Development of Cambodia to present at the seminar on Dissemination of Investment Law and Sub-Decree on Law Enforcement. Investment for provincial administration to implement.
