(Battambang): In response to the request of the people in Prek Luong commune, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province, Mr. Khat Sat, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Prek Luong commune and his colleagues cooperated with the commune authorities and the people to prepare canals and roads. The river bank, which is the basic need of the local people, has recently reached more than 4,000 meters and the river bank more than 200 meters.
According to the village chief, Daun Ind, some of the hardships during the rainy season during the floods flooded the villagers and destroyed many hectares of farmers' crops as well as aquaculture.
He added that after the canal, it helped relieve the flood and also helped farmers to grow vegetables through several hectares in the dry season by drawing water from the Sangker River.
Ms. Soeung Vanna, Prek Luong Commune Chief, also expressed her congratulations for this achievement, which connected Daun Ind village to Bak Amrek village to help solve the problem for the farmers in time.
She added that in addition to the benefits of flood relief, our people also get a new road that facilitates the difficulty of transporting agricultural products to the market, as well as helping to maintain the price of your agricultural products.
Separately, Mr. Khay Kakada, Chief of Rohal Suong Village, also expressed his congratulations, as his village received a dam with a length of more than 200 meters, which has the advantage of helping to prevent flooding into the villagers' villages and has destroyed crops. Lots of crops and trails as well.
