Mrs. O Vandin inspected the provision of health services at 6 health centers in Kampong Thom province to promote primary health care
(Kampong Thom): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health visited Kampong Thom province, inspected 6 health centers and chaired a meeting with the leaders in charge of health in Kampong Thom province in order to promote the provision of services in the centers. Health and promote primary health care in the province.
The meeting was attended by the Deputy Governors of the Provincial Board of Governors, the Directors of the Provincial Health Departments, the Deputy Governors of the 9 Districts / Municipalities, the Heads of the 3 OD Health Offices, the 3 Directors of the Provincial / District Referral Hospitals, and the Heads of the Health Centers. 56 places, partner organizations and government officials, provincial halls and health departments, a total of about 100 participants.
On the occasion of completing this mission, Ms. O Vandin introduced and recommended to all relevant working groups on 9 main points, including:
1: Appreciate the efforts made to improve the function of the health center.
3. Improve the health center's integrated plan, which includes improving health center services and community involvement. The implementation of this integrated work plan must be monitored and adjusted as necessary.
4: The commune's three-year rolling plan has already been integrated with health center activities, but there are still challenges in implementation. Communes and health centers should work together to address health-related issues at their local level.
5. Health centers should begin to use digital communication with communities such as pregnant women, diabetics and hypertensives in each of the limited population areas and monitor compliance with them.
6: The 6 health centers that she visited provided good health services such as sanitation staff and the use of educational materials. However, air conditioning service recorder and medication management system should be improved for all health centers.
7: The health center should establish a hotline number for each health center, just have a separate phone number without using a personal phone and give to the guard 24 hours to the next day in turn.
8. Health centers should carry out grassroots activities highlighted in the 2014 publication by integrating services such as immunization, seasonal health education, screening and prenatal counseling, especially in the area. Remote.
9. The health center shall report the progress of the work based on the integrated health plan of the health center on a quarterly basis to the OD, the health department and the national working group.
Please note that the above 6 health centers are: Sandan Health Center, Meanchey Health Center, Sambo Health Center, Sankor Health Center, Prey Pros Health Center and Kampong Thom Health Center, located in Kampong Thom OD Health Office.
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha Announces the Inauguration of Prey Veng Provincial Council for the 4th Mandate
(Prey Veng): The Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Minister of Interior and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Sar Sokha, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Prey Veng Provincial Council on the afternoon of June 7, 2024. The fourth mandate was held at Prey Veng Provincial Hall.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha stated that the council is a representative of the people in the whole province, which has the power to make both regulatory decisions and executive power within the framework set by the law and regulations in force to manage the affairs. Basis to meet the needs of the people in its jurisdiction.
He affirmed that all councils must strive to serve the interests and needs of all people equally, transparently, accountable, equitable and environmentally friendly, especially not to adhere to any political tendencies.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha congratulated the members of the Provincial Council for representing the people, namely the Commune / Sangkat Councilors, who voted in favor of being elected as Provincial Councilors for the fourth mandate in order to continue to lead Prey Veng Province. Board of Governors.
Dr. Abhisit Dr. Sar Sokha also advised all councils to strive to serve the interests and needs of the people fairly and transparently, especially not to adhere to any political tendencies.
Kampong Trabek District Administration Clarifies on Social Media Posting that there is a Market Closure in Kampong Trabek District
(Prey Veng): Kampong Trabek District Administration has clarified that in Kampong Trabek District, there are two major urban markets, Kampong Trabek Market and Kor Andek Market, at 11 noon on June 7, 2024, the two markets above. Received information that customs officials inspected the two markets, so traders were scared to close the stalls.
After receiving this information, the district and commune administrations inspected and found that some stalls were closed, in Kampong Trabek market, traders closed about 10% and turtle market, traders closed about 60%. As of 5:00 pm on June 7, 2024, no customs officials inspected the two markets.
Authorities are currently searching for sources who have reported that customs officials have visited. Authorities also advised the trader to reopen the shop as usual, do not be afraid and believe this false information.
