ASEAN Secretary-General officially invited by US State Department to pay working visit to US
(Jakarta): At the invitation of the United States Department of State, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), will lead a delegation from the ASEAN Secretariat to pay a working visit to the United States from June 10 to 13, 2024.
The main purpose of this working visit is to promote the ASEAN-US Comprehensive Strategic Partnership based on the success of existing areas of cooperation.
The ASEAN Secretary-General will meet with key stakeholders, including senior government officials, parliamentary leaders, private sector partners, academia, academia, academics, university leaders and the media.
The ASEAN Secretary-General is also scheduled to meet with the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) and the US-ASEAN Business Council to discuss key issues under ASEAN-US cooperation, including peace, security and security. Public-private partnerships.
During his stay in the United States, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn will also meet with the ASEAN Committee in Washington DC, where he will discuss the current situation and future direction of the ASEAN-US Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, as well as exchange views on its role. The Committee aims to promote and strengthen the dialogue partnership between ASEAN and the United States.
