General knowledge: How long have Khmer ancestors been able to raise dogs, chickens, elephants, cattle, etc.?
What is shown here is evidence of a culture that has an indisputable date and is also a testament to the true nature of human activity, that is, it was created by human intelligence. In addition, the fact that wildlife has become a domestic animal also shows the age of Khmer culture, which from birth has coexisted harmoniously with each other and with the natural environment around them.
In the early days, our ancestors lived by farming and raising animals to eat meat and eggs. Excavations from prehistoric sites show that they were able to bury the dead by burying jewelry or other items in the graves. Cultural remnants say that people like to build houses high above the ground and live together in villages, districts, and some live in caves or plateaus.
Source: Book of Khmer Original Religious Beliefs of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, China's Global Civilization Initiative for Promoting Peace and Cultural Diversity
By Hou Chamroeun, Researcher, Center for the Development of Cambodia
