(Phnom Penh): Mr. An Dara, Chairman of the Board of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia, explained that the processing of cashew nuts is high and good for investment, but no one wants to invest because the investment in cashew crops in Cambodia is expensive, which leads the company Who will plan to invest non-profit or make a small profit.
"This is why there are not many foreign companies investing in cashew crops in Cambodia." This was further confirmed by the Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Cashew Federation.
Mr. An Dara said that, in fact, the investment in cashew crops is the highest price for cashew nuts, just the first fall, which costs about $ 1,200 per ton, while the cashews are dried between. $ 1,500- $ 1,700 per ton is a good price for unprocessed cashews.
He added that the above factors are the reason to question why there are no foreign companies to invest in the cashew sector in Cambodia, in fact, most of the companies we see are all Cambodian companies. President of the Cashew Federation: At least $ 260 million is needed to achieve the Royal Government's goal of promoting 25% cashew processing by 2027 (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. An Dara, Chairman of the Board of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia, said that in order to achieve the target policy of the National Government on cashew nuts, we need at least 260 million dollars to promote the processing of cashew nuts by 25% by 2027.
Mr. An Dara said that Cambodia has produced an abundance of fresh cashews, which makes it impossible for Cambodia to rely on neighboring countries to use some cashews because Cambodia has low processing.
"The Cambodian government last year issued a national policy on cashews, with the government aiming to process 25 percent of cashews by 2027 and 50 percent by 2032," he said. In that, the Cashew Federation of Cambodia has worked hard to work closely with the Royal Government and relevant institutions to promote Cambodia's cashews to be recognized as good quality cashews.
He added that previously there were less than 10 cashew processing companies, but now there are up to 42 companies, including 3-4 companies with foreign investors who want to process cashew nuts in Cambodia.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, urged all relevant authorities to take effective measures to crack down on gangsters. He said this at the monthly meeting of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command on June 7, 2024.
The provincial governor has set out some important principles as follows:
* First, measures to crack down on gangsters must be made clear and highly responsible by setting the time and place to take repressive measures, as well as expanding the scope of prevention and suppression to a wide range of high efficiency.
* Second, the Department of Education, Youth and Sports must cooperate with school principals to hold meetings and report gangsters to police officers to take timely action.
* Third: The drug problem is a sensitive issue that requires the three forces to work together to clean up and be effective. For any post official who succeeds in this, there must be immediate administrative measures, because this mechanism we must strengthen and enforce the law very strictly.
* Fourth: Regarding the issue of order, sales, order, parking, the municipal authorities must review to avoid the problem of anarchy, which causes criticism from the people.
* Fifth: For the ID card, the commissioner must review this work and strengthen the list of remaining names, both old and new names, and establish a telegram group to easily monitor to avoid people not going to the polls. Because there are not enough documents.
* Sixth: Related to the management of natural resources, so far there is no new encroachment, but all districts must advertise and inform our people, we do not have to cut because now we have a letter from the Ministry Clear. In case of aggression, the relevant municipal and district authorities must crack down and report the repressive measures to the Ministry clearly.
* 7th: For the opening and closing of the fishing season, the specialized department must follow clear procedures in accordance with the principles set by the Ministry. In case of crime, cooperate with the relevant authorities to take repressive measures in a timely manner.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak urges the Land Registration Team in Area 2 and disseminates to the people to come and complete the registration before the rainy season arrives and strongly hopes that the introduction of all these important principles promotes Provide effective and responsible implementation of action plans.
