(Phnom Penh): Mr. Met Makara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness and a representative of the Disability Action Council, signed an agreement with the United Nations Development Program on the morning of June 7, 2024. The signing ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Chea Somethy, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness.
The Memorandum of Understanding between the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) and the Council for the Action of Persons with Disabilities (DPM) will provide a framework for joint and facilitative cooperation, as well as strengthen cooperation between the two sides. In the field of disability, in particular the promotion of a national policy framework that supports the disability environment, the promotion of the rights and meaningful participation of people with disabilities in Cambodia.
It should be noted that in the next 3 years, UNDP continues to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in (1). Develop, revise and promote the implementation of national and international standards related to disability work in Cambodia (2). Reform and develop the capacity, systems and mechanisms of the Disability Action Council.
