Capital requirements and cost reduction are key to boost cashew processing for export, want to process 5,000 tons of cashew need $ 7 million (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. An Dara, President of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia said. The key to boosting mango processing for export is to provide capital for the collection of cashew nuts for processing and cost reduction.
Mr. An Dara said that currently Cambodia produces more than 750,000 tons of cashew nuts per year, of which 95% of raw nuts are exported to neighboring countries, especially Vietnam, and only 5% are processed by factories. Locally.
He said banking institutions also played an important role in promoting low-interest lending, reducing collateral so that factories could afford to buy cashew nuts for processing throughout the year.
He also noted that in this process, it is necessary to reduce costs as much as possible to be able to compete with other countries.
He said that one cashew processing plant has the capacity to process at least 3,000 to 5,000 tons per year, however, those factories do not have enough funds to buy fresh cashew nuts to store for processing for a period of time. That year, this is a big challenge for processing companies, and if a company wants to process 5,000 tons a year, it needs at least $ 7 million in capital.
According to An Dara, there are currently about 42 cashew processing factories in the district, but only about eight are processed to a standard that can be exported.
