(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on Thursday, June 6, 2024, in Kampot Province, met and discussed with the leaders and officials of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampot Province, Kep Province. Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampong Speu and Takeo provinces.
On that occasion, the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of the six provinces gave a brief report on the situation of staff, civil servants, leadership, cooperation, weather forecast in the area on a regular basis and the problems encountered, as well as the results of maintenance and restoration work. Re-irrigation system and intervention to pump water to save dry rice in 2023 of each provincial department.
Welcoming the Minister, he expressed his pleasure to have the opportunity to meet with the leaders and officials of the six provincial departments of Water Resources and Meteorology in person to increase the closeness and reduce the gap between the upper and lower levels. As well as listening to oral reports and challenges that arise and opportunities for each department to exchange experiences and share knowledge with each other.
The Minister praised and appreciated the efforts of the leaders and civil servants of the six provincial water resources and meteorological departments, especially the intervention in the past dry season on water supply for irrigation. Agriculture and clean water for daily use.
The Minister also highlighted the importance and necessity of inter-institutional cooperation between the relevant departments by setting up small working groups such as:
* 1: Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and Ministry of Rural Development * and 2: Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, Ministry of Rural Development and Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology work together to solve general problems related to agriculture and water sector. Beautiful and so on.
It should be noted that the meeting between the Minister and the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of the six provinces ended with meaning and content, as well as a long-term vision to prepare for the work ahead. Under the most pleasant and friendly atmosphere.
