According to a guideline from the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ethical Council of Artists recently observed a sharing on social media to critique and improve the immoral activities of performing arts groups in a number of wedding haircuts. To degrade the beautiful traditions of the nation and show excessive gestures, lack of knowledge and education, which are selfish actions and affect the interests of society as a whole.
In this regard, the Ethical Council of Artists would like to appeal and determine the following measures:
* The art groups participating in the Khmer wedding ceremony must immediately stop immoral activities and strive to understand and make efforts to properly organize according to the noble traditions of the nation, which is inherited from the ancestors.
The Artistic Ethics Council of Artists will cooperate with the relevant authorities to research and summon those art groups to educate, guide and contract out activities. In case of continuing to commit these immoral acts, a legal measure will be taken in accordance with the principles in force.
* A wedding ceremony is a ceremony that gives happiness to the children who are the new couple. In this regard, parents should carefully examine and consider in finding each art group that comes to participate in the most important wedding ceremony in the life of their children.
The Ministry of Culture calls on people from all walks of life not to share any video clips or negative images that are obscene and affect the dignity of society. The Ethical Council of Artists would like to respect and express our deep gratitude for the spirit of love, protection and participation in preserving the national cultural values of all Cambodians in preventing all forms of negative images that affect the value of ancestral heritage.
