Senior official of the Ministry of Tourism: Children are not a tool to soften the hearts or ask for sympathy from tourists, the use of children in tourism affects the image and honor of the nation
(Battambang): Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, said that children are not the attraction of tourists, children are not a tool to soften or ask for sympathy from tourists, children are not in any interest in exchange with tourists . Therefore, all tourism service businesses must absolutely avoid using children for any purpose for their own benefit.
In addition, Mr. Hor Sarun stated that if we do not think in advance and participate in the implementation consistently, problems will occur and all these problems will be negative and destroy us in the future. In addition, another issue that is important to pay attention to is the prevention of the spread of HIV / AIDS, especially in tourism.
He added that AIDS is understood by most of the public to be eradicated and no longer occur in Cambodia. This is a misunderstanding. AIDS is still a problem in our society, not only has it not been eradicated, but there is a worrying increase in the number of people in certain groups who could easily spread to other groups if We do not care.
In the face of the fight against HIV / AIDS, the National Policy to End AIDS and the Sustainability of the AIDS Program for 2023-2028 was approved by the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers under the highest chairmanship of Samdech Manet on March 15, 2025. The policy outlines strategic actions in each sector to prevent the spread of HIV / AIDS, including tourism.
