(Trat): The opening of the tourist waterway between Trat to the Cambodian coast and with Koh Tral will be a new opportunity for Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam (CVTEC) tourism, which requires the Cambodian side to participate in providing policy. Facilitate the connection of the waterway while the Thai side is ready.
Sroung Viyada, president of the Thai Tourism Industry Council in Trat province, said that each year about 12 million tourists pass through the southern corridor, which borders Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam. However, due to the fact that some roads are difficult to travel and are being repaired, all parties must be able to connect tourist transport by water.
Ms. Viyada said that the achievement of this cooperation is to connect tourism destinations "three countries, one destination".
The President of PATA said that for Cambodia, everything is ready, such as tour operators, sea transport, tourism investors are ready to receive and send tourists, while the immigration, Cambodia has only officials to work. Deploy locations only later, and the provincial administration, each provincial tourism department also supports. The question is, is each ministry willing to do this?
According to the call of Mr. Thuon Sinan, the Ministry of Tourism should propose a policy to the Royal Government to connect sea transport with Thailand and Vietnam as soon as possible, because Cambodia has built a number of ports in the province. Kampot, Kep, Koh Kong, which is in the national interest.
Mr. Thuon Sinan confirmed that traveling by water is faster and provides a new experience for tourists.
According to Kunthea Phirum, a representative of GTC Speedboat, his company has sent seven technical teams to study the sea route from Sihanoukville. From Sihanoukville Tourist Port to Trat Multi-Purpose Port is about 90 miles in 3 hours and 40 minutes.
(Siem Reap): On the morning of Friday, June 7, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, HE Samdech Manet, presided over the opening of the ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science and Technology. And the 20th innovation organized in the territory of Siem Reap province, the land of famous Khmer temples.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani Hun Manet's opportunity to open the 20th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science, Technology and Innovation:
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that science and technology have always been important pillars that support the progress of humanity, help provide solutions, make our lives better and easier, and help expand the scope and possibilities of Mankind's control over our society, nature, and our planet.
* President Hun Manet stated that advances in technology have reduced the geographical distance, accelerated and strengthened globalization, which has helped bring our world closer together and provided many opportunities in terms of sharing. Share knowledge and create economic resources for the whole world.
* President Hun Manet stated that ASEAN has indeed benefited greatly from the globalization supported by the advancement of science and technology, and that this globalization has transformed ASEAN from a region with a majority of countries. New independence became one of the major growth centers of the world.
* President Hun Manet stated that science and technology continue to evolve at a rapid pace, we need the world to use and scrutinize emerging technologies that can change the world.
* President Hun Manet stated that we can see the use of artificial intelligence almost everywhere in our lives, such as simple tasks in finding information on smartphones. While providing many opportunities, artificial intelligence also brings a number of key challenges such as ethics, environment, transparency, equality, data privacy concerns and skills retraining needs.
* President Hun Manet stated that it is true that our humanity is entering a world we have never known before, so we must move forward with caution.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that he would like to highlight two key principles that he thinks can help guide us in overcoming challenges as well as new opportunities manifested through science, technology and innovation in general and artificial intelligence. Speaking separately.
* President Hun Manet stated that he would like to emphasize the need for the development of science, technology and innovation based on "people-centered". We certainly have the right to take advantage of technological advances, but at the same time we have a responsibility to balance and ensure that technology benefits mankind.
* President Hun Manet stated that the capture and use of artificial intelligence must have a limit that takes into account morality and social values. The general public has already expressed fears and anxieties that their rights and privacy could be violated by the enormous capabilities of artificial intelligence programs.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that without basic education and skills and continued participation, it would certainly be difficult for consumers in general to distinguish between fake and real information or to distinguish between artificial images and With the original image.
* President Hun Manet stated that sometimes such developments cause great losses to society and the government. Transformation of the original image through these technologies can irritate social and public sentiment and can also lead to social divisions, chaos and instability that can affect social harmony as well as hard-won peace. .
* President Hun Manet stated that the public has also expressed concern about future job losses and other challenges.
* President Hun Manet stated that adhering to a people-centered approach to the use of artificial intelligence is very important and we need to promote a change in the attitudes of policy makers, researchers and the private sector.
* President Hun Manet stated that multilateralism is an effective way to capture emerging technologies to ensure that they serve humanity, not humanity.
* President Hun Manet stated that countries must compete vigorously in capturing the latest technology, but we must also ensure that we can still create space for cooperation in our balanced competition.
* President Hun Manet stated that ASEAN, which has a long history of promoting multilateral cooperation in the fields of science, technology and innovation, should make more efforts to advocate for the need to adhere to the principles of multilateralism. To orient the future of new technologies.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that he would like to recommend APASTI 2026-2035 to pay more attention to equitable access to technology and technology transfer, development of talented human resources and mobility of individuals. Talented through technology transfer, talented human resource development.
* President Hun Manet stated that through in-depth discussions and exchanges throughout the week, we will be able to put forward practical ideas based on bilateral and multilateral cooperation in the direction of accelerating the development of science, technology and technology. Innovation for the benefit of humanity.
* President Hun Manet announced the opening of the 20th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science, Technology and Innovation from now on.
