(Phnom Penh): The Institute of Technology of Cambodia (aka Techno School) has organized the 13th Science Conference for 2 days from 6-7 June 2024, focusing on promoting innovation: human capital, research and connectivity. Industry or private sector to share and exchange knowledge on scientific research results.
The 13th Scientific Conference was chaired by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and was attended by about 2,000 national and international guests.
The 13th Scientific Conference of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia was held in cooperation with national, international partners, the private sector and many other institutions. The scientific conference was held in conjunction with the first International Conference on Water Supply and Sanitation and the First Conference on Food Research, Innovation and Food Technology.
At the same time, the organization of the conference also aims to promote multidisciplinary integration between the institute with the public and private sectors to move towards the transfer of technology into industry and society, strengthen research and innovation capacity in education. Higher education; And to disseminate scientific research results and promote the activities of professors, researchers and students in technology research and development.
"The Institute of Technology of Cambodia has a mission to cultivate human resources in the field of engineering and technology, strengthen systematic research, increase the progress of innovation and increase the relationship between the Institute and private institutions at all levels. In addition, we will try our best to strengthen the quality of research and share research to society.
The 13th Science Conference features presentations on more than 90 innovative scientific research topics from professors, students, international partners and leading companies in the field of science and research in Cambodia.
The science conference was also attended by about 1,200 high school students, in which students attended the exhibition and visited the laboratory of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
