The King orders the appointment of Mr. Prang Hang Sereyrith as Director of Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has appointed Mr. Prang Hang Sereyrith as Director of the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport.
Mr. Prang Hang Sereyrith is a Cambodian intellectual who holds a Master's degree in the United Kingdom. Mr. Prang Hang Sereyrith has been the Deputy Director of Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport for many years.
Mr. Serey Rithy also served as Head of Department at the General Department of Logistics.
In addition to the above positions, he is also the Chairman of the Working Group of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia at the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and also the Chairman of the Party Youth Administration in Ontario, Canada.
Please note that Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport is a public higher education institution under the management of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. The institute has admitted students in 2021.
Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport was established for the purpose of training human resources with clear skills, comprehensive knowledge and ethics, correct behavior to solve the crisis, lack of technical experts in the field of public works and transportation now and in the future. Contribute to the economic and social development (skills, knowledge and ethics).
The institute is training students in 6 majors, including: Road, Expressway, Bridge, Railway and Port Construction, Sewage Treatment, Economics and Road Transport Management, Logistics and Supply Chain Management. , Ship driving skills and ship engine skills.
