In addition to deciding to leave the opposition party they used to live with, the 10 leaders of the Candlelight Party in Prek Narin commune also decided to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party. They understand that the Cambodian People's Party is a political party with a clear policy to lead the building and development of the nation as a strong support for peace and social stability, which is an indispensable capital in nation building.
Investing in solar energy is higher than investing in other energy sources
PARIS (Reuters) - The world's top energy research firm said on Thursday that investment was flowing into solar energy more than all other energy sources combined, with investment likely to increase. Up to $ 500 billion this year. According to the AFP news agency.
The Energy Agency estimates that global investment in clean energy this year will double to $ 2 trillion, AFP reported, citing a report released by the International Energy Agency (IEA). Compared to investing in fossil fuels.
The IEA says combined investment in renewable energy and power grids exceeds the amount invested in fossil fuels for the first time in 2023.
IEA Executive Director Fatih Birol said in a statement released with the agency's annual report on global energy investment: "Clean energy investment is setting new records, even in the face of strong economic conditions. "The competition shows the momentum behind the new global energy economy."
Companies and governments around the world are increasing the cost of producing clean energy to reduce carbon emissions from fossil fuels, which are fueling climate change.
Improved supply chains and lower costs are driving investment in various forms of clean energy, such as solar panels, wind turbines, electric cars and heat pumps, as well as nuclear power generation, the report said.
Joint investment in renewable energy and nuclear power generation is now expected to increase to 10 times the amount of fossil fuels invested in China, led by investment in solar energy. Invested the largest share.
Cost of solar panels has fallen by 30% in the last two years, and by 2024 "PV investment is expected to reach $ 500 billion due to lower module prices." "To have new investment." According to the AFP news agency.
