MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian investigators on Thursday arrested a French national on suspicion of gathering intelligence on Russian military activities, Russian investigators said on Thursday. This is according to the release by Reuters on June 6, 2024.
The Commission of Inquiry into Serious Crimes has said it has opened a criminal case against the unnamed Frenchman for violating Russian law on "foreign agents".
The statement said the man committed "gathering information targeting the military (and) military technical activities of the Russian Federation", a punishable act.
"Such information, if obtained by foreign sources, could be used against state security," the commission said. He added that the man had visited Russia several times over the years and had met with Russian citizens.
The charge carries a sentence of five years or more. However, there was no immediate comment from the French Foreign Ministry in Paris.
A video clip released by the Commission of Inquiry shows a man wearing jeans and a black T-shirt arrested in a restaurant, with a masked security officer being dragged into a car and walking into a building. One. The suspect's face was covered in snow.
President Hun Manet made the remarks while presiding over the opening ceremony of the "Asia-Pacific General Assembly of the 2024 International Youth Chamber of Commerce" in Siem Reap on the evening of June 6, 2024.
The General Assembly will be held for three days from June 6-9, 2024, with nearly 4,000 national and international participants from 21 countries in the region and 23 countries from various regions.
Samdech Hun Manet thanked all stakeholders, including the Siem Reap Provincial Administration and especially the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, for their tireless cooperation and good support to contribute to JCI-Cambodia in organizing this General Assembly. Successful remarks by President Hun Manet at the Opening Ceremony of the 2024 JCI Asia-Pacific General Assembly
(Siem Reap): The Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, presided over the opening ceremony of the "Asia-Pacific General Assembly of the 2024 International Chamber of Commerce and Industry" in Siem Reap on the evening of June 6, 2024.
The following are the main points made by President Hun Manet on the occasion of the opening of the 2024 JCI Asia-Pacific General Assembly:
* President Hun Manet stated that he was pleased to address the 2024 JCI Asia-Pacific General Assembly, one of the largest youth gatherings in our Asia-Pacific region.
* Samdech Thep Dei stated that Samdech is honored that Cambodia, especially Siem Reap, the center of our history and culture, has been chosen to host this important event.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government highly appreciates the JCI's efforts to promote the resilience of the youth, who have made significant contributions to the Royal Government's efforts to develop human capital.
* Samdech would like to thank JCI and JCI-Cambodia for incorporating sustainable development and social uplift into their priority agenda. The past commitment of JCI and JCI-Cambodia to drive positive change for the better is a commendable initiative that underscores JCI's important role as a Royal Partner. Government in developing countries.
* President Hun Manet stated that such difficult circumstances can easily cause us to lose hope and even enable us to become more individualistic. Circumstances like this can also make us forget that our future depends on every young person who takes over.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia recognizes the important role of the youth in building a bright future for Cambodia. Cambodia, once considered a killing field, is now a nation of complete peace ... and our unique temples, such as Angkor Wat and beautiful beaches, are attracting millions of tourists. Every year.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has identified the development of human capital, which focuses on education and the promotion of youth empowerment as the most important determinants of national destiny.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that many policy programs to strengthen youth development. The Royal Government of Cambodia has set a priority policy program to provide technical and vocational training to 1.5 million young people from poor, vulnerable and vulnerable families across the country who can learn by Free of charge and even get an additional monthly allowance.
* Samdech Hun Manet thanked all stakeholders, including the Siem Reap Provincial Administration and especially the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, for their tireless cooperation and good support to contribute to JCI-Cambodia in organizing this General Assembly. To be successful.
* President Hun Manet stated that the General Assembly becomes a catalyst for innovation and our renewed commitment to building a sustainable common destiny.
* President Hun Manet stated that the General Assembly will be a forum that promotes better cooperation and progress for the Asia-Pacific region and for the whole world in the context of striving to achieve sustainable development goals and Prevent the effects of climate change.
