(Phnom Penh): Another Cambodian-American who has been politically active with the opposition for many years has decided to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party after despairing of political life with the opposition.
Von Yen is a former monk and had the opportunity to live in the United States until he obtained American citizenship. Van Yen has been politically active with the opposition for many years, from the CNRP to the Candlelight Party. Von Yen is one of the individuals who helped raise funds from Cambodians in the United States to serve the political activities of the Candlelight Party.
Through these supportive activities, Mr. Van Yen has been given high positions in the party by the opposition, such as being given the opportunity to be a candidate for the National Assembly in Koh Kong province and a working group of the Candlelight Party in Svay Rieng province.
Now, Wen Yen is tired of working with the opposition because he sees the disintegration and weakening of the opposition. In particular, the opposition of Sam Rainsy to the Prek Chik Funan Techo canal project has angered opposition supporters.
With the decision to leave the opposition, Mr. Van Yen respectfully asked for the opportunity from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to have the opportunity to continue political life with the Cambodian People's Party.
Samdech Techo thanked the Republic of Korea for its attention to Cambodia despite the change of leadership and considered this a legacy given by Samdech through efforts to re-establish diplomatic relations with the Republic of Korea after his visit. First to the Republic of Korea in 1996. He strongly believes that the growth of economic and trade relations with the Republic of Korea will surely lead to an increase in political relations.
The Ambassador thanked Samdech Techo for allowing him and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call and also expressed their pleasure to meet Samdech Techo again. He congratulated Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia and sent a congratulatory letter from the former President of the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea.
The Ambassador expressed his appreciation to Samdech Techo for leading Cambodia for more than 30 years, bringing continuous growth and development. In his role as President of the Senate, he believes that Samdech Techo will continue to lead further socio-economic development for the people of Cambodia.
He also thanked Samdech Techo's efforts and contribution in re-establishing diplomatic relations with the Republic of Korea in 1997. The Ambassador expressed his pleasure that he was honored to accompany the Prime Minister on his first official visit to the Republic of Korea.
Samdech Techo said that the two sides strive to implement the existing agreement, especially through the implementation of the free trade agreement, which will help increase the two countries' mutual trust and political value. Samdech Techo recommended that Korean investors consider the establishment of a special economic zone of Korean companies according to a formula plus in Cambodia.
He also recalled the lessons that Cambodia must remember and record for the Republic of Korea in assisting the world in the face of the Kovid 19 pandemic. Countries blocked, especially flights, only the Republic of Korea maintained flights between Phnom Penh and the Republic of Korea, which was the gateway for Cambodia as well as for relations with other countries.
Samdech Techo considered that he owed the Republic of Korea for this great help that allowed Cambodia to breathe at that time. He also thanked the Republic of Korea for its assistance in the areas of infrastructure, road construction, human resource training and the recruitment of Cambodian workers in the Republic of Korea. And so on.
Samdech hopes that Samdech will see with his own eyes in the near future the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge across these two rivers, which Samdech directly proposed. Samdech Techo also mentioned that our two countries, Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, are very close countries, with many Cambodian women marrying Korean men, so what should be done so that those Cambodian-Korean hybrids can know Both languages are Cambodian and Korean to get to know their identity.
Finally, Samdech Techo Senate President asked the Ambassador to send a message of greetings as well as blessings to the President and the new President of the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea. Samdech Techo also expressed his hope that during his upcoming visit to the World Knowledge Forum, he will have the opportunity to meet with the President as well as the President of the new National Assembly of the Republic of Korea.
The Ambassador thanked Samdech Techo for sharing his thoughts and experiences and wished Samdech Techo good health because his health is very important for peace, prosperity and to continue to contribute to building. Peace and stability in the region. Eight Candle Makers in Prek Dach Commune, Leuk Dek District Declared Separation and Asked to Join the CPP
