The Governor of Kampong Speu Province requested the Global Life-Sharing Fund of the Republic of Korea to provide additional medical equipment at health centers to support and upgrade two secondary schools in Bor Seth and Thpong districts to become high schools to facilitate education. And reduce dropout rates due to being away from home.
