Cambodia-China-France Friendship Radio Arrests Ukrainian-Russian Citizen with Explosives Suspected of Terrorism
PARIS (Reuters) - Police in France have arrested a 26-year-old Ukrainian-Russian man after he blew himself up with an explosive device in a hotel room, the French anti-terrorism prosecutor's office PNAT said on Wednesday. North Paris. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, June 6, 2024.
The incident happened earlier this week, with the man being treated by firefighters after suffering severe burns. A search of his room turned up explosives. The PNAT is now working with local intelligence agencies to open an investigation into men suspected of plotting terrorism and bombings. Neither the Ukrainian Embassy nor the Russian Embassy in Paris has responded to requests for comment.
France is on high alert for security threats, with less than two months to go until the Paris Olympics.
