(Kratie): Mr. Phim Phira, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, chaired a meeting to discuss the partnership between vocational education and training institutions and the private sector in Kratie province at the Provincial Theater on the morning of June 6, 2024.
Mr. Khly Ul stated that the Techo Sen Isan Polytechnic Institute was established on June 11, 2001 under the Asian Development Bank (ADB) Grant Loan Scheme No. 421 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. "Kratie Biological Training Center."
In 2023, Kratie Vocational Training Center was transformed into Techo Sen Isan Polytechnic Institute by sub-decree on January 6, 2023.
In the last 5 years, the Institute has cooperated with Swiss Confederation, Assets and Skills Project, to train a total of 4,498 technical and vocational skills / 4460 people, of which 89/46 people in the Property Project, 60 additional skills / 39 people, the first phase and the second phase are continuing, the institute has cooperated with 103 enterprises in the province.
Mr. Phim Phira, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, said that the Vocational Training Institute with the private sector, both inside and outside the province, has made great contributions to joint training to train human resources in Kratie and help develop the country to move forward in Development.
He said that the growth of the private sector depends on having a workforce, human resources with real knowledge and skills in the operation of the enterprise to be active and sustainable.
The Deputy Governor sincerely commended the Swiss Confederation for providing financial support, technical education equipment to the Institute, and commended the leadership of the Department of Labor, Vocational Training and the Institute, staff, civil servants, teachers and staff. Those who have worked hard to fulfill their work with physical and mental strength and have a responsible spirit to contribute to the training and development of human resources effectively and quality.
Ministry of Labor Holds a Workshop on Strengthening Cambodian Private Recruitment Agencies to Recruit Ethical Workers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on the morning of June 6, 2024, opened a training workshop on strengthening the Cambodian private recruitment agency to recruit ethical workers held at Sunway Hotel. In Phnom Penh, with the participation of senior leaders of the Royal Government, the International Labor Organization (ILO) and members of the Association of Cambodian Recruitment Agencies (ACCA).
In addition to highlighting the attention and support mechanisms of the Royal Government, Minister Heng Sour also reminded the workshop that a successful migration requires five happy and happy parties, including the government side of the sending country, the government of the host country. Workers of the sending country and private companies of the host country, including migrants.
It should be noted that this training workshop on strengthening the Cambodian private recruitment agency in the ethical recruitment will provide an opportunity for all Cambodian private recruitment agencies to better understand the laws, regulations and policies related to the recruitment of migrant workers and To demonstrate its commitment to the implementation of fair and ethical selection principles for Cambodian private recruitment agencies.
