Regarding tourism, Mr. Anatoly Borovic said that the number of Russian tourists to Cambodia has been steadily increasing and Russia will consider having direct flights from Russia to Cambodia to increase the exchange of tourists between the two countries. He also thanked Cambodia for ensuring the safety of tourists visiting Cambodia, especially tourists.
The Ambassador also reminded Cambodia as an old friend, a trustworthy friend, a good partner and strives to strengthen and expand potential relations and promote cooperation for development and for the benefit of both countries.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo welcomed the Ambassador and also asked the Ambassador to thank the President of the Federal Council (Senate) of the Federal Parliament of the Russian Federation for sending a congratulatory letter to the Prince. Recently appointed President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Ambassador paid tribute to Samdech Techo and the Kingdom of Cambodia, and as one of Cambodia's oldest diplomats, he thanked the Prince for allowing him to meet today. He stated that the Russian people know Samdech Techo very well, as Samdech Techo has made enormous contributions to the friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and the former Soviet Union and continues to the Russian Federation today.
At the same time, the Ambassador congratulated Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate and congratulated the CPP on its brilliant results in the recent District, Municipal and Capital Council elections. This result shows the overwhelming trust of the majority of Cambodians in the CPP.
The Ambassador also reminded that Cambodia and Russia always send observers to observe the elections in their respective countries, and he expressed his appreciation and gratitude for this excellent relationship. He stated that the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation have a close friendship and a long history of 68 years. Russia is working to strengthen cooperation in various fields.
At the international forum, he reminded that Cambodia and Russia have helped and coordinated on UN, international and regional mechanisms, and thanked Cambodia for its role as a facilitator between ASEAN and Russia in strengthening the dialogue partnership. Russia in ASEAN as well.
Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, also thanked for all the assistance of the Soviet Union and continued to the Russian Federation, which helped Cambodia when Cambodia just liberated from the Khmer Rouge regime.
On other cooperation issues, Samdech Techo recommended to push for what is possible, especially for Russia to pay attention to the establishment of direct flights, because Samdech Techo considered that it is time to promote tourism. Russia has arrived in Cambodia and is pushing for a speedy settlement of its long-standing debt.
Samdech Techo also said that the decision to transfer the old generation to the new generation is for long-term peace and was the right decision of Samdech because about 9 months after the transfer, Cambodia has political stability, security, growth is still Inflation remains low and people's living standards remain good.
Finally, the Ambassador expressed his deepest respect to Samdech Techo and emphasized that Russia is a long-term friend and will always be with Cambodia in difficult times and Russia will not interfere in Cambodia's affairs.
The discussion ended in a happy atmosphere, with Samdech Techo and the Ambassador having an honest and frank discussion and exchanging views in a spirit of friendship and warmth.
