Techo International Airport is more than 75% complete and is scheduled to start operations in the first half of 2025
(Central): The 4F-level Techo International Airport has completed the construction of the first phase of about 75.8%, which is scheduled to start operations in the first half of 2025. This was confirmed by Dr. Mao Havannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation.
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. Mao Havannal presiding over the program of leading representatives of national and international airlines as well as representatives of air transport support companies to visit and understand the construction work of international airports. Techo on June 6, 2024.
This visit is organized for the second time to allow all company operators to be ready to serve and provide related services when Techo International Airport is completed and operational starts as planned in the first half of the year. The coming 2025.
The visit also aims to provide insights into the latest developments in the construction of the great and international structure of the Cambodian children born of the wisdom and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and President of the Senate, and Continue to apply the prudent wisdom of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Speaking at the event, Dr. Mao Havannal stated, "The company has made great efforts and tried its best to complete the construction as soon as possible as planned. As of June 1, 2024, the construction of the first phase of Techo International Airport 4F has reached about 75.8%.
Dr. Mao Havanal said that the project to build Techo International Airport here under the investment of 1,500 million dollars is a joint venture between the state and the private sector, the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation has a 10% stake in 100%.
He said that the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, as a shareholder, is also extremely proud when the construction project is completed as planned and launched profitably and helps drive the growth of Cambodian air transport.
At the same time, Dr. Mao Havanal said that from January to April 2024, Cambodia received more than 2 million air passengers, an increase of 25% compared to the same period. In 2023, there will be just over 1.6 million people.
From these figures, Dr. Mao Havannal can generally say that air transport activities in Cambodia have gradually recovered after the Kovid-19 crisis and are proudly moving forward.
