Please be informed that Kampot Multi-Purpose Port is located in Kilo 12 Village, Sangkat Koh Touch and Sangkat Boeung Touk, Bokor City, Kampot Province. It was approved by the Royal Government in 2005 and approved by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport During 2012, a total area of 207 hectares was owned by Kampot Pod Company.
The Kampot Multi-Purpose Port is expected to be an important artery for Cambodia's maritime transport, which will contribute to the further growth of the Cambodian economy and will be one of Cambodia's deep-sea ports. Will complement Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and Phnom Penh Autonomous Port.
Shipping by sea from Kampot Multi-Purpose Port to Asia-Pacific countries is possible without the need to change ships at any port, except for shipments to the United States and Europe, which require ship transfers at Large ports before reaching the final destination.
