(Xinhua) - Indonesia's tourism minister has expressed hope for an increase in tourists from China during a promotional event in Shanghai on Monday. According to the Xinhua news agency.
The Ministry of Tourism and Innovation Economy (MTCE) of the Republic of Indonesia has launched a number of promotional activities focusing on the Chinese market, Xinhua reported.
Chinese tourists stayed in Indonesia for an average of eight to 11 days, and the average cost per trip rose to $ 1,386.55, according to the minister.
The Ministry of Tourism has set a target of 1 to 1.5 million Chinese tourists for this year, citing the rapid growth of the Chinese economy as one of the reasons why the second-largest economy has become a market. Important for Indonesia tourism.
The number of Chinese tourists visiting Indonesia rose to 286,375 in the first three months of this year, according to Xinhua.
