The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources: This morning, Samdech Hun Sen inaugurated the Kampot Multi-Purpose Port worth $ 140 million.
(Kampot): On the morning of Thursday, June 6, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, inaugurated the Kampot Multi-Purpose Port. The first phase is worth about 140 million US dollars.
Kampot Multi-Purpose Port is located in Kilo 12 Village, Sangkat Koh Touch and Sangkat Boeung Touk, Bokor City, Kampot Province. 2012 on a total area of 207 hectares owned by Kampot Pod Company.
The port's waters are state property, which the Royal Government has designated to be used in a total area of 678 hectares, along with the construction of a 2,600-meter-long, 170-meter-wide and 10-meter-deep navigation canal that can accommodate ships. 10,000 tons or equivalent to 666TEU can dock.
The waterway also features a 1,000-meter-diameter bezel for navigation vessels and the installation of navigation aids to enable the ship to operate safely and securely.
The first phase of the Kampot Multi-Purpose Port Development Project has a total construction cost of approximately US $ 140 million, which is an investment capital of Kampot Port Company.
Kampot Pod also plans to build and expand the infrastructure of the Kampot multi-purpose port in the next phase. The second and third phases are planned to be built with a water depth of up to 13 meters, which will allow 20,000-tonne vessels to operate safely in and out of the port, and to build a port for passengers. Also.
At the same time, the new port will also contribute to provide employment opportunities for people living in Kampot and other provinces. Currently, there are a total of 176 staff members who have been working at the port, and this number will increase in the future depending on the size of the port's operations and growth.
As for the geographical location, Kampot Multi-Purpose Port is located in an area that is favorable for connecting water, land and railway transportation system to Phnom Penh and other provinces via National Road No. 3, National Road No. 4, National Road No. 41. National Road No. 48, Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and connecting the southern railway to the north of Cambodia.
Please note that the location of this port also includes the construction of container fields, special economic zones, logistics centers, warehouses of all kinds, warehouses, customs, manufacturing and distribution plants and ferries, which connects the transport with the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port via the road. Funan Techo Prek Chik Navigation, which the Royal Government plans to open in the near future.
