Progress and activities to provide the first surgical services of the new Romeas Hek Referral Hospital
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Kuch Sitha, Director of the Health Department of Svay Rieng Provincial Administration, said on June 5, 2024 that under his leadership, the Director of the Department has established a working group to coordinate the surgical work of Romeas Hek Referral Hospital. Provide its first surgery service in 2 cases successfully, safely and with high confidence to the people.
Dr. Kuch Sitha said that the new Rhino Hex Referral Hospital building was built under the support of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Deputy Chief of the Royal Task Force. The government visited Svay Rieng province and chaired the Royal Government working group to help local people in Romeas Hek district.
The new referral hospital building is located in Ta Trav village, Kampong Trach commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, which was opened on December 7, 2021 and completed on July 1. 2023 and was launched on September 1, 2023.
In addition, the new referral hospital is able to provide services covering 16 communes (204 villages) with a total population of 154,453 people, 76762 females.
