He stressed that the agricultural sector, especially Cambodian rice production, has experience in producing rice using short-term, low-water use, which can help Cuba overcome difficulties while Cuba is under siege. Cuba can use Cambodian rice production techniques to put into practice in Cuba, because today Cuba is facing food shortages, which is an important issue to be addressed.
Regarding the medical field, Samdech Techo thanked the Cuban government for its support and assistance to Cambodia during difficult times, especially when Cambodia had just emerged from the Pol Pot regime. Cambodia has sent many students to study in Cuba, as Cuba has the technology to study and produce vaccines, so Samdech Techo recommended that the Ambassador continue to work with the Cambodian Ministry of Health.
During the meeting, the Ambassador congratulated Samdech Techo on his appointment as President of the Senate and also conveyed greetings from the President of the National Assembly and the Prime Minister of Cuba to Samdech Techo.
The Ambassador expressed her admiration and admiration for Cambodia for its success in food security and for its high level of development, and that Cuba also wants to learn from Cambodia.
She said that the importance of relations between the two countries is that the rice production project started by a Cambodian delegation traveled to Halawa, Cuba, and that the Cuban Deputy Minister of Agriculture also visited Cambodia to promote rice production in Cambodia. In Cuba as well.
Regarding the health sector, she stated that Cuba has health technology and aims to share it with Cambodia. Our two countries should have a memorandum of understanding on health and other areas such as culture. She also intends to work with relevant Cambodian ministers to learn more about the potential of both countries.
The ambassador also described Cuba's current difficulties, with both economic and financial blockades making it difficult to import food. She thanked Cambodia for voting in favor of lifting sanctions on Cuba at the UN General Assembly every year.
In response, Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, thanked the Ambassador for bringing greetings and wishes from the President, President of the National Assembly and Prime Minister of Cuba to Samdech Techo.
He recalled his visit to the Republic of Cuba, especially in 1999, 2000 and 2022, during which he had in-depth discussions and discussions on promoting bilateral relations and the changing world situation with top leaders. Of the Republic of Cuba.
Regarding bilateral relations, Samdech Techo reminded that we have many agreements and memoranda for our cooperation. We need to push for the implementation of all existing agreements and memoranda and find out what can be done because our two countries have so much potential.
The Ambassador expressed her pleasure at hearing Samdech Techo's memories in the Republic of Cuba, during which he discussed with the Cuban Commander-in-Chief the defense of the Republic of Cuba, which strives for social equality and justice. She also considered that the friendship between Cambodia and Cuba is based on nation building and security, with both countries being non-aligned members.
The Ambassador wished Samdech Techo Senate President good health and long life for the stability, security and lasting peace of Cambodia and thanked Samdech Techo for treating the Republic of Cuba as a brother.
The President of the Senate requested the Ambassador of the Republic of Cuba to send a message of greetings and blessings to the President, the Prime Minister and the President of the National Assembly of the Republic of Cuba.
General Sar Thet sends condolence message to Heng Sivaro, brother of Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin
(Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of the National Police Force, sent a message of condolences to Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, for the death of Heng Sivaro, his brother. Tuesday, June 13, 2024, at the age of 72, due to an accident.
In this sad and sad time, on behalf of the National Police Force, General Sar Thet, I would like to express my deepest condolences and prayers and dedicate to the merits of Preah Ratanatray to support the soul of Disciple Heng Sivaro. Birth is born in death, do not forget.
Kampong Cham Provincial Administration and Global Life Sharing Corporation of the Republic of Korea Sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Humanitarian Donations to Kampong Cham Provincial Administration
(Kampong Cham): The Kampong Cham Provincial Administration and the Global Life Sharing Corporation of the Republic of Korea signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Humanitarian Donations to the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration to improve the quality of life for Cambodians in the areas of health, education and well-being.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on Humanitarian Donation to Kampong Cham Provincial Administration was held on June 5, 2024 at the Senate in Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Mr. Mam Bunneang, Chairman of the 10th Commission.
Kampong Cham provincial administration officials said that in considering the mutual covenants and agreements here and for other good and valuable considerations, the two sides agreed as follows:
Item 1: Objective: This agreement is designed to improve and achieve the quality of life for the Cambodian people in the fields of health, education and well-being through the donation of Korean medical supplies, such as medicine, equipment and supplies. Daily necessities provided by Party "B".
Article 2: Conditions and Termination: The fixed amount of this agreement is $ 5,000,000, implemented for 50 months (June 2024-April 2029). Some project work needs to be studied based on the agreement of both parties.
Article 3: Materials donated by Party "B" Materials that can organize the health system and improve the quality of life of the Cambodian people, especially in the fields of health, education and well-being, etc.
Article 4: General Conditions: The detailed outline of each project is added to this Agreement after this Memorandum has been thoroughly reviewed and recognized by both parties. The number of projects can be decided with the consent of both parties.
In the event of any misunderstanding or lack of confirmation of this Agreement, the Agreement in English shall be used. The agreement in English shall provide the final basis for the interpretation and implementation of the terms of the agreement.
Article 5: Management: The management and communication of projects must be communicated through the coordinator, Mr. Min Bung Chang R&S Steel (Cambodia), prepared by both parties. Both sides must continue to communicate and cooperate to promote the best results of the project.
Article 6: Signing as evidence The two sides agreed to sign a memorandum of understanding on the donation agreement on June 8, 2024.
